              <folder name="II.1.1.1.1.3 [CT3] Operational Fulfilment Definition" id="id-6e43ad78cb984dbcb785671fe7b2ebec">
                <documentation>Continuum navigation coordinate: II.1.1.1.1.3. Navigation asserts no semantic containment. Occurrence: architectural; no additional architectural instance or semantic relationship. Canonical element directory: canonicalId=2b52c0de17b146da962f303e99f90a4a; Exchange identifier=id-d066b2ac060b5d0fa4429dde7b2c73c2. Existing governed hierarchy member; directory retained for leaves.</documentation>
                <element xsi:type="archimate:Capability" name="[CT3] Operational Fulfilment Definition" id="id-d066b2ac060b5d0fa4429dde7b2c73c2">
                  <documentation>Define the context requirements, expected outcomes and housekeeping of an operational undertaking.

**Overview**

The semantic execution envelope applies to one-step and multi-step activity and stays distinct from dispatch and supervision.

**Intent**

Keep the semantic promise of an undertaking separate from the machinery that executes it.

**Boundary**

A fulfilment definition does not execute, orchestrate or choreograph its activity.</documentation>
