            <folder name="II.1.1.1.4 [CT2] Interoperability &amp; Exchange" id="id-79ba660b324343c185d1e97c6eda840b">
              <documentation>Continuum navigation coordinate: II.1.1.1.4. Navigation asserts no semantic containment. Occurrence: architectural; no additional architectural instance or semantic relationship. Canonical element directory: canonicalId=0f2e5222874949d8b0cce234941ecb20; Exchange identifier=id-dbd66e69788450649e184966aa724797. Existing governed hierarchy member; directory retained for leaves.</documentation>
              <element xsi:type="archimate:Capability" name="[CT2] Interoperability &amp; Exchange" id="id-dbd66e69788450649e184966aa724797">
                <documentation>- **Architectural Scope**: Resolve destinations, transform schemas, route, transport, deliver, acknowledge, and coordinate standards-based information exchange across enterprise boundaries.
- **Functional Responsibilities**:
  - Providing multi-protocol boundary adaptation for healthcare standards (HL7 v2, FHIR REST, DICOM, secure messaging).
  - Executing bidirectional structural and semantic transformations between legacy formats and canonical representations.
  - Ensuring reliable addressed delivery and fan-out distribution to external clinical endpoints.
  - Processing and distinguishing technical delivery acknowledgements from business acknowledgements.
- **Boundary Rule**: Egress terminates Harmonia management of the emitted representation (Axiom AX-13).

Interoperability &amp; Exchange moves information across participating boundaries through destination resolution, transformation, delivery and acknowledgements. It preserves the difference between technical transmission and the recipient's business response so that an exchange can be understood under its actual contract. Standards govern the external representation while internal management semantics remain private.

**Boundary**

Egress ends Harmonia management of the emitted representation. Retained delivery evidence does not extend control over an external recipient or transfer payload authority.</documentation>
