              <folder name="II.1.1.2.2.2 [CT3] Authoritative Durable State Establishment" id="id-18272429526f44c28aa72644c876d669">
                <documentation>Continuum navigation coordinate: II.1.1.2.2.2. Navigation asserts no semantic containment. Occurrence: architectural; no additional architectural instance or semantic relationship. Canonical element directory: canonicalId=0d5bd68ff50f410aaceed05377e1a4df; Exchange identifier=id-591ee54ab6145bf58e837667f64a4265. Existing governed hierarchy member; directory retained for leaves.</documentation>
                <element xsi:type="archimate:Capability" name="[CT3] Authoritative Durable State Establishment" id="id-591ee54ab6145bf58e837667f64a4265">
                  <documentation>Atomically establish durable managed state and its authoritative version progression.

**Overview**

Durable acceptance gives managed information an explicit committed state from which applicable active representations can be reconstructed.

**Intent**

Give managed change an explicit committed state and authoritative progression basis.

**Boundary**

Commit is distinct from semantic source authority and from successful active convergence; applications do not gain a raw persistence path.</documentation>
