              <folder name="II.1.1.2.2.3 [CT3] Binary Content Association &amp; Resolution" id="id-ce1107f07a4141568324c676021aefa1">
                <documentation>Continuum navigation coordinate: II.1.1.2.2.3. Navigation asserts no semantic containment. Occurrence: architectural; no additional architectural instance or semantic relationship. Canonical element directory: canonicalId=5314959509dc4b558711ec169ddee5a0; Exchange identifier=id-08ef90abe8f35705add6ae823077cc76. Existing governed hierarchy member; directory retained for leaves.</documentation>
                <element xsi:type="archimate:Capability" name="[CT3] Binary Content Association &amp; Resolution" id="id-08ef90abe8f35705add6ae823077cc76">
                  <documentation>Maintain content associations and custody knowledge sufficient for governed payload resolution, retrieval and assembly.

**Overview**

Document attachments, diagnostic media and operational artefacts share a need to locate usable content while distinguishing logical meaning from physical possession.

**Intent**

Make logical information and its usable payloads consistently associable while retaining custody boundaries.

**Boundary**

No universal binary custody, storage topology or persistence authority is implied.</documentation>
