            <folder name="II.1.1.2.6 [CT2] Semantic Governance &amp; Conformance" id="id-91577e79eb4049ad8008ff51fa6fec1c">
              <documentation>Continuum navigation coordinate: II.1.1.2.6. Navigation asserts no semantic containment. Occurrence: architectural; no additional architectural instance or semantic relationship. Canonical element directory: canonicalId=9ee41437bd4c4bd18389f05c12108f97; Exchange identifier=id-7d6f635ffb6f5c6181bde1d07b859662. Existing governed hierarchy member; directory retained for leaves.</documentation>
              <element xsi:type="archimate:Capability" name="[CT2] Semantic Governance &amp; Conformance" id="id-7d6f635ffb6f5c6181bde1d07b859662">
                <documentation>- **Architectural Scope**: Govern canonical models, schemas, terminologies, value sets, mapping tables, constraint rules, and semantic conformance validation across the enterprise.
- **Functional Responsibilities**:
  - Defining and publishing canonical healthcare data models and profile structures.
  - Governing clinical terminology mappings, value sets, and concept lookups (SNOMED CT, LOINC).
  - Validating inbound and outbound message representations against published semantic rules.
  - Governing semantic versioning, deprecation, and backward compatibility across schema revisions.
- **Component Relationship**: Informs the Calliope strategic logical component, but Calliope is the responsibility centre, not the capability definition.

This capability makes canonical information models, terminology bindings, mappings and conformance rules governable across enterprise use. It addresses both what representations mean and whether they respect the published rules, keeping version and compatibility concerns explicit. A conformant representation can therefore be distinguished from one that merely uses a supported transport or parser.

**Boundary**

Conformance does not establish clinical truth, information authority or disclosure permission. Calliope is an established responsibility centre, not the definition of the capability.</documentation>
