              <folder name="II.1.1.3.3.2 [CT3] Operation-Bound Policy Enforcement" id="id-c33ed781f0ba4659bf7c9dfd35faeae9">
                <documentation>Continuum navigation coordinate: II.1.1.3.3.2. Navigation asserts no semantic containment. Occurrence: architectural; no additional architectural instance or semantic relationship. Canonical element directory: canonicalId=cb32b32c657445b3b9b27bebc069ace9; Exchange identifier=id-9c71dcd24d0154db8ee01ab204012f48. Existing governed hierarchy member; directory retained for leaves.</documentation>
                <element xsi:type="archimate:Capability" name="[CT3] Operation-Bound Policy Enforcement" id="id-9c71dcd24d0154db8ee01ab204012f48">
                  <documentation>Enforce resolved policy constraints at the boundary where a governed action is attempted.

**Overview**

Distributed participants apply the applicable effective authorisation and fail closed when authority is absent or untrustworthy.

**Intent**

Ensure an operation cannot proceed merely because its caller omitted or bypassed a voluntary policy check.

**Boundary**

Enforcement participation does not distribute policy ownership or make security context persistent content.</documentation>
