vice or implementation construct is allocated EC-14. The catalogue defines a capability, not a software component or deployment boundary.\n\n\n\n\\end{itemize}\n\\subsubsection*{Conceptual Behavioural Sequence}\n\n\\textit{RAD source listing (presentation only; no inferred ancestry).}\n\\begin{quote}\nDefine Good Behaviour\n\n↓\n\nGather Evidence\n\n↓\n\nAssess Evidence against Good Behaviour\n\n↓\n\nAdjudicate Assessed Detail\n\n↓\n\nReport\n\\end{quote}\n\nThis sequence explains the capability; it is not an implementation workflow specification or a derived Business Process. “Define Good Behaviour” identifies assurance expectations and criteria; it does not transfer ownership of governing requirements to Service Guardian. Source information ownership remains with its responsible capability; assurance owns its contextual evidentiary association.\n\n\nThe \\href{https://github.com/fhirfactory/harmonia/blob/98410db60155198a75f74c79d98060070209faa1/docs/markdown/02-strategy/capabilities/business-enabling-capabilities.md\\#health-service-assurance-approved-business-enabling-capabilities}{Business Enabling assurance principles} govern disposition, generic processing assurance, evidence/\\allowbreak{}criteria temporality, assessment/\\allowbreak{}adjudication, independence, failure/\\allowbreak{}recovery and explicit evidence insufficiency. These semantics are not universally reducible to PASS /\\allowbreak{} FAIL /\\allowbreak{} UNKNOWN and do not imply an assurance information model or persistence mechanism.\n\n\n\\par\\smallskip\n&quot;,&quot;id_aliases&quot;:[&quot;EC-14&quot;],&quot;key&quot;:&quot;enterprise:ec-14&quot;,&quot;latex_label&quot;:&quot;cap:ec-14&quot;,&quot;local_id&quot;:&quot;EC-14&quot;,&quot;name&quot;:&quot;Service Guardian&quot;,&quot;name_aliases&quot;:[],&quot;name_status&quot;:&quot;Canonical&quot;,&quot;owner_identifier&quot;:null,&quot;owner_key&quot;:null,&quot;parent_identifier&quot;:&quot;HCM-EC-trust-accountability-assurance&quot;,&quot