                <documentation>Continuum navigation coordinate: II.1.2.1.1.1. Navigation asserts no semantic containment. Occurrence: architectural; no additional architectural instance or semantic relationship. Canonical element directory: canonicalId=0922a1141f82416ca9de12054c28a69a; Exchange identifier=id-8850d02455155526bb82a3317a3e7966. Existing governed hierarchy member; directory retained for leaves.</documentation>
                <element xsi:type="archimate:Capability" name="[CT3] Care Eligibility Determination" id="id-8850d02455155526bb82a3317a3e7966">
                  <documentation>Determine whether applicable eligibility conditions for care access are satisfied.

Care Eligibility Determination establishes whether the conditions governing access to applicable care are met. It contributes a qualified access decision alongside intake and referral, so that an identifiable request can be distinguished from one that satisfies the relevant criteria. Its purpose is eligibility in the applicable context rather than clinical diagnosis or service allocation.

**Boundary**

Eligibility alone does not reserve capacity, allocate a care place or deliver care.</documentation>
