              <folder name="II.1.2.1.1.3 [CT3] Care Referral Management" id="id-dfa9926302054527a9e715c007e8e7a8">
                <documentation>Continuum navigation coordinate: II.1.2.1.1.3. Navigation asserts no semantic containment. Occurrence: architectural; no additional architectural instance or semantic relationship. Canonical element directory: canonicalId=ebdaa781bba542f8b744ef34a836a269; Exchange identifier=id-53444359e5665b29817e1bf2198ed57a. Existing governed hierarchy member; directory retained for leaves.</documentation>
                <element xsi:type="archimate:Capability" name="[CT3] Care Referral Management" id="id-53444359e5665b29817e1bf2198ed57a">
                  <documentation>Manage a request for another participant/service to assess, manage or assume applicable care responsibility.

Care Referral Management concerns a request for another participant or service to assess, manage or assume applicable care responsibility. It preserves the distinction between the requester's intent and the recipient's disposition, allowing care coordination to recognise an unresolved referral rather than assume a successful handoff. Referral is therefore broader than sending a document.

**Boundary**

Submission or receipt does not establish acceptance, an appointment, delivered care or responsibility actually assumed.</documentation>
