              <folder name="II.1.2.1.2.1 [CT3] Care Discharge Coordination" id="id-a5ad0aa98c4b422b81d82d7be7c3291e">
                <documentation>Continuum navigation coordinate: II.1.2.1.2.1. Navigation asserts no semantic containment. Occurrence: architectural; no additional architectural instance or semantic relationship. Canonical element directory: canonicalId=62e436db8ce44a98ba855de68ac6b876; Exchange identifier=id-e4d13d2f89595e61a5190d63673c8051. Existing governed hierarchy member; directory retained for leaves.</documentation>
                <element xsi:type="archimate:Capability" name="[CT3] Care Discharge Coordination" id="id-e4d13d2f89595e61a5190d63673c8051">
                  <documentation>Coordinate applicable discharge requirements and progression.

Care Discharge Coordination brings applicable discharge requirements and progression into a coherent operational context. It supports the transition out of a care circumstance while keeping readiness, physical exit and continuing responsibility distinguishable. The capability concerns coordinating those requirements rather than deciding that every clinical condition for discharge has been met.

**Boundary**

Discharge readiness and departure are not themselves evidence that another participant has accepted care responsibility.</documentation>
