            <folder name="II.1.2.1.3 [CT2] Care Scheduling &amp; Capacity Management" id="id-9843d76f9a1042fe94f8e54dce74efa3">
              <folder name="II.1.2.1.3.1 [CT3] Care Appointment Management" id="id-5d3eb358ed664ddbb3e162b90f38422c">
                <documentation>Continuum navigation coordinate: II.1.2.1.3.1. Navigation asserts no semantic containment. Occurrence: architectural; no additional architectural instance or semantic relationship. Canonical element directory: canonicalId=14dc21b28938425498ff7b04e49efd30; Exchange identifier=id-ad4cadf7fe205a499f487d5aec98ba4f. Existing governed hierarchy member; directory retained for leaves.</documentation>
                <element xsi:type="archimate:Capability" name="[CT3] Care Appointment Management" id="id-ad4cadf7fe205a499f487d5aec98ba4f">
                  <documentation>Establish and manage a scheduled opportunity for care.

Care Appointment Management establishes a scheduled opportunity for care and maintains that opportunity as arrangements change. Within scheduling and capacity it supplies the temporal commitment around which participants can organise, while leaving the actual availability of places and resources distinguishable. A scheduled opportunity is useful coordination information even before attendance or care occurs.

**Boundary**

A booking does not establish attendance, intervention performance or satisfaction of diagnostic-service-specific scheduling constraints.</documentation>
