                  <property key="v0.2 / Source Locators" value="[{&quot;anchor&quot;:&quot;ct2--care-scheduling--capacity-management&quot;,&quot;line&quot;:396,&quot;source&quot;:&quot;business&quot;,&quot;text&quot;:&quot;| Care Appointment Management | Establish and manage a scheduled opportunity for care. |&quot;},{&quot;anchor&quot;:&quot;ct2--care-scheduling--capacity-management&quot;,&quot;line&quot;:392,&quot;source&quot;:&quot;business&quot;,&quot;text&quot;:&quot;**Decomposition assertion:** Each named child in this table is a CT3 Business Capability whose immediate CT2 parent is Care Scheduling &amp; Capacity Management; that CT2 has the CT1 parent stated above.&quot;},{&quot;anchor&quot;:&quot;ct2--care-scheduling--capacity-management&quot;,&quot;line&quot;:403,&quot;source&quot;:&quot;business&quot;,&quot;text&quot;:&quot;**Boundary:** Available staff, equipment or an unoccupied bed does not establish usable service capacity. Available for service coverage ≠ deployed to a care requirement ≠ assigned operational work. Care Resource Deployment consumes availability, role, qualification, engagement and privilege context without changing authoritative rosters, qualifications, employment or privilege records. It establishes no Harmonia authority over clinical work, enterprise assets or hospital-wide logistics. Operational capacity is distinct from strategic/tactical capacity planning and from collective service readiness (OI-BC-002).&quot;}]"/>
