              <folder name="II.1.2.1.3.2 [CT3] Care Resource Deployment" id="id-2419cfb0fe8047f5bc663262a8c92633">
                <documentation>Continuum navigation coordinate: II.1.2.1.3.2. Navigation asserts no semantic containment. Occurrence: architectural; no additional architectural instance or semantic relationship. Canonical element directory: canonicalId=7854224c3b064116b0d48f01ce5537d8; Exchange identifier=id-fb15438e5dad5d19af167c1e064ff34a. Existing governed hierarchy member; directory retained for leaves.</documentation>
                <element xsi:type="archimate:Capability" name="[CT3] Care Resource Deployment" id="id-fb15438e5dad5d19af167c1e064ff34a">
                  <documentation>Apply legitimately available and appropriately authorised resources to a current or planned operational care requirement, particularly using roster/on-call and service-coverage context.

Care Resource Deployment applies legitimately available resources to a current or planned care requirement. It considers coverage, role, qualification, engagement and privilege context to distinguish availability in principle from deployment to a particular need. Its contribution is the operational application of resources, without changing the authoritative facts that make their use legitimate.

**Boundary**

Deployment is neither roster authoring nor clinical work assignment and does not confer clinical authority or ownership of enterprise assets.</documentation>
