              <folder name="II.1.2.1.3.3 [CT3] Care-Place Allocation" id="id-4d0671b0caf14b83a9fc3196601e921f">
                <documentation>Continuum navigation coordinate: II.1.2.1.3.3. Navigation asserts no semantic containment. Occurrence: architectural; no additional architectural instance or semantic relationship. Canonical element directory: canonicalId=f8a4df47bea742a0869802472136d55f; Exchange identifier=id-b9cdfa1c4c27554f92b4165837b8a362. Existing governed hierarchy member; directory retained for leaves.</documentation>
                <element xsi:type="archimate:Capability" name="[CT3] Care-Place Allocation" id="id-b9cdfa1c4c27554f92b4165837b8a362">
                  <documentation>Allocate an applicable care place to a care requirement.

Care-Place Allocation associates a care requirement with an applicable care place. Its outcome is the allocation itself, distinct from defining the place or establishing its readiness. This separation supports reasoning about reserved, allocated and usable places without assuming that an apparently empty location is fit for the requirement.

**Boundary**

Allocation does not establish clinical suitability beyond the applicable context or make an unready place ready.</documentation>
