              <folder name="II.1.2.1.3.4 [CT3] Care-Place Readiness Management" id="id-e78c9d21c07249c6a7bb3dbf34f7a35d">
                <documentation>Continuum navigation coordinate: II.1.2.1.3.4. Navigation asserts no semantic containment. Occurrence: architectural; no additional architectural instance or semantic relationship. Canonical element directory: canonicalId=4dd0f1b9f9334c5c80066a8974fdfb7a; Exchange identifier=id-040505098b205e8db531a93757549c7d. Existing governed hierarchy member; directory retained for leaves.</documentation>
                <element xsi:type="archimate:Capability" name="[CT3] Care-Place Readiness Management" id="id-040505098b205e8db531a93757549c7d">
                  <documentation>Establish and manage whether a particular care place is ready for allocation or use.

Care-Place Readiness Management establishes whether a particular place can be allocated or used in its operational context. It connects the place's condition with its intended use so that vacancy can be distinguished from readiness. This is a place-specific responsibility within scheduling and capacity, supporting credible allocation rather than merely counting physical spaces.

**Boundary**

Readiness of one place does not establish collective readiness or usable capacity of the whole service.</documentation>
