              <folder name="II.1.2.1.3.5 [CT3] Operational Care Capacity Management" id="id-e8b8da567e664daa9f9fbf3a9dd5842f">
                <documentation>Continuum navigation coordinate: II.1.2.1.3.5. Navigation asserts no semantic containment. Occurrence: architectural; no additional architectural instance or semantic relationship. Canonical element directory: canonicalId=3040519e1fec43699c14a3cafb2d945d; Exchange identifier=id-34cfdfaefd4b52a9b58219b9a6227604. Existing governed hierarchy member; directory retained for leaves.</documentation>
                <element xsi:type="archimate:Capability" name="[CT3] Operational Care Capacity Management" id="id-34cfdfaefd4b52a9b58219b9a6227604">
                  <documentation>Understand and manage the service’s usable capacity to accommodate care in its current operational context.

Operational Care Capacity Management establishes and manages the service's usable ability to accommodate care under current conditions. It considers capacity as a service-level concern rather than a simple count of staff, devices or vacant beds. This supports decisions grounded in what can actually be accommodated, while keeping current capacity distinct from plans for future provision.

**Boundary**

Resource availability, strategic capacity requirements and collective service readiness are distinct; the latter's placement remains unresolved.</documentation>
