              <folder name="II.1.2.1.3.6 [CT3] Operational Care Flow Coordination" id="id-e5540f8960304addbc9eed4f59118586">
                <documentation>Continuum navigation coordinate: II.1.2.1.3.6. Navigation asserts no semantic containment. Occurrence: architectural; no additional architectural instance or semantic relationship. Canonical element directory: canonicalId=d1dedb10ea694af5b88dbe1b6192f3ac; Exchange identifier=id-ac1518843b8359b18ed7500763ad836d. Existing governed hierarchy member; directory retained for leaves.</documentation>
                <element xsi:type="archimate:Capability" name="[CT3] Operational Care Flow Coordination" id="id-ac1518843b8359b18ed7500763ad836d">
                  <documentation>Coordinate operational care flow and its progression within the care-delivery environment.

Operational Care Flow Coordination addresses progression of care flow within the delivery environment. It provides the coordinating responsibility around operational movement and impediments, rather than treating each scheduled opportunity or place allocation as an isolated fact. Its outcome concerns coherent flow under current conditions, not the clinical determination of what care should occur.

**Boundary**

Coordinating flow does not transfer clinical work, workforce governance or general hospital-logistics authority.</documentation>
