            <folder name="II.1.2.1.4 [CT2] Care Support Logistics Management" id="id-3d2a117be6d7446f88e25a58e622362f">
              <folder name="II.1.2.1.4.1 [CT3] Care Support Work Coordination" id="id-f748f7123022453db19ca3f52e9d8ca1">
                <documentation>Continuum navigation coordinate: II.1.2.1.4.1. Navigation asserts no semantic containment. Occurrence: architectural; no additional architectural instance or semantic relationship. Canonical element directory: canonicalId=f9f5c69b0f0b472287cd4ac56ccff6f3; Exchange identifier=id-a895e887fe115faa9c303cf60916173a. Existing governed hierarchy member; directory retained for leaves.</documentation>
                <element xsi:type="archimate:Capability" name="[CT3] Care Support Work Coordination" id="id-a895e887fe115faa9c303cf60916173a">
                  <documentation>Coordinate authorised operational support work: what needs doing, who performs it and how progression, completion or escalation is coordinated.

Care Support Work Coordination organises authorised operational support work around care: what needs doing, who will perform it and how progress, completion or escalation is coordinated. It gives supporting activity an explicit progression responsibility, rather than assuming that issuing a request means the work occurred. The work remains bounded by applicable authority and resource constraints.

**Boundary**

Dispatch does not establish worker availability, qualification or privilege, and support coordination does not determine clinical work.</documentation>
