              <folder name="II.1.2.1.4.3 [CT3] Patient Movement Coordination" id="id-8ade6121292247e097287905fe4d4cb6">
                <documentation>Continuum navigation coordinate: II.1.2.1.4.3. Navigation asserts no semantic containment. Occurrence: architectural; no additional architectural instance or semantic relationship. Canonical element directory: canonicalId=f404b6647fe04a3390e57022bdef0843; Exchange identifier=id-b224448612cb5d62bbce730c2a84fb08. Existing governed hierarchy member; directory retained for leaves.</documentation>
                <element xsi:type="archimate:Capability" name="[CT3] Patient Movement Coordination" id="id-b224448612cb5d62bbce730c2a84fb08">
                  <documentation>Coordinate physical patient transit and applicable mobility constraints.

Patient Movement Coordination concerns the person's physical transit and the mobility constraints relevant to it. Within care-support logistics it supports movement appropriate to the patient's circumstances without treating transport completion as a clinical transition. Its responsibility is useful wherever care requires a change of physical location.

**Boundary**

Transport progression does not establish clinical handover, destination acceptance of care or authority over the clinical plan.</documentation>
