              <folder name="II.1.2.2.1.1 [CT3] Clinical Quality Criteria Management" id="id-f4bc836ecbf34179a5da14a712549e50">
                <documentation>Continuum navigation coordinate: II.1.2.2.1.1. Navigation asserts no semantic containment. Occurrence: architectural; no additional architectural instance or semantic relationship. Historical predecessor: R.2.2 [CT3] Clinical Quality Criteria Management; canonicalId=7a51321b00464016920976b269981edd; Exchange identifier=id-143c6a0eb6675280a374d05aac61fe58 Canonical element directory: canonicalId=1f48527a9a7c4382a7f8a660ccb9f29f; Exchange identifier=id-f913c25edca8547fa47e0a6382936f18. Existing governed hierarchy member; directory retained for leaves.</documentation>
                <element xsi:type="archimate:Capability" name="[CT3] Clinical Quality Criteria Management" id="id-f913c25edca8547fa47e0a6382936f18">
                  <documentation>Establish and manage measures, indicators, expectations and criteria against which clinical quality is considered.

Clinical Quality Criteria Management establishes the measures, indicators and expectations used to consider clinical quality. It makes the basis of a later judgement explicit so that evidence can be assessed against an identifiable expectation rather than an unstated standard. Criteria are distinct from the measurements or findings produced when they are applied.

**Boundary**

Managing criteria does not originate the underlying evidence or establish a quality conclusion.

