              <folder name="II.1.2.2.1.2 [CT3] Clinical Quality Evidence Management" id="id-c3de9cc437564169b8efe57dc36036e5">
                <documentation>Continuum navigation coordinate: II.1.2.2.1.2. Navigation asserts no semantic containment. Occurrence: architectural; no additional architectural instance or semantic relationship. Historical predecessor: R.2.3 [CT3] Clinical Quality Evidence Management; canonicalId=f31902d474894670aeef3e0abbedccf0; Exchange identifier=id-3940059fa2735c8fa10020170420ee91 Canonical element directory: canonicalId=1b0a1c6945ed4fadba045ff4753c104c; Exchange identifier=id-2e79b5737c3b5cfdbc86b901d77cd21c. Existing governed hierarchy member; directory retained for leaves.</documentation>
                <element xsi:type="archimate:Capability" name="[CT3] Clinical Quality Evidence Management" id="id-2e79b5737c3b5cfdbc86b901d77cd21c">
                  <documentation>Manage the body of applicable evidence used for clinical-quality consideration without owning its originating activity.

Clinical Quality Evidence Management maintains the body of material applicable to quality consideration. Its purpose is to retain evidence in a form and context that can support review without treating availability as proof of quality. The originating activity and its authority remain distinguishable from the later quality purpose for which its information is used.

**Boundary**

Evidentiary use transfers neither source ownership nor authority to determine the activity being reviewed.

