              <folder name="II.1.2.2.1.3 [CT3] Clinical Quality Reporting" id="id-a9bff0e09a1b40e8bbd2f4390ca80bdc">
                <documentation>Continuum navigation coordinate: II.1.2.2.1.3. Navigation asserts no semantic containment. Occurrence: architectural; no additional architectural instance or semantic relationship. Historical predecessor: R.2.4 [CT3] Clinical Quality Reporting; canonicalId=e5812fcdf3f5465b9b1d8ba536075c5f; Exchange identifier=id-3e15dac60a7851bf820f6269d07b6a37 Canonical element directory: canonicalId=70f34839c23042d59469e6ef96944057; Exchange identifier=id-c08e4d5e84485cfb920455ac3e20ed0c. Existing governed hierarchy member; directory retained for leaves.</documentation>
                <element xsi:type="archimate:Capability" name="[CT3] Clinical Quality Reporting" id="id-c08e4d5e84485cfb920455ac3e20ed0c">
                  <documentation>Communicate established clinical-quality measures, assessments, findings and conclusions to authorised consumers.

Clinical Quality Reporting communicates established quality measures, assessments and findings to authorised consumers. It makes the outcome of quality consideration usable beyond the assessment context while retaining its basis and standing. Reporting therefore represents a communication responsibility, not another opportunity to originate or silently change the reported judgement.

**Boundary**

Communicating a quality concern does not perform the operational or clinical improvement response.

