              <folder name="II.1.2.2.1.4 [CT3] Clinical Quality Review &amp; Assessment Management" id="id-33de86832d834327ace7427f167f3fcc">
                <documentation>Continuum navigation coordinate: II.1.2.2.1.4. Navigation asserts no semantic containment. Occurrence: architectural; no additional architectural instance or semantic relationship. Historical predecessor: R.2.5 [CT3] Clinical Quality Review &amp; Assessment Management; canonicalId=4b17ec92f0af4c4b9556912dbdd0f29f; Exchange identifier=id-943c0e41cdf55f05ac5fdd126cbcae3d Canonical element directory: canonicalId=8318c35b302b4dcaa0e795fbfdc93e3b; Exchange identifier=id-0d3beb2699a45eb081120d317f4a9a33. Existing governed hierarchy member; directory retained for leaves.</documentation>
                <element xsi:type="archimate:Capability" name="[CT3] Clinical Quality Review &amp; Assessment Management" id="id-0d3beb2699a45eb081120d317f4a9a33">
                  <documentation>Review evidence against applicable criteria and establish a clinical-quality assessment, finding or conclusion.

This capability evaluates quality evidence against applicable criteria and establishes a finding, assessment or conclusion. It is the judgement-bearing responsibility within Clinical Quality Management, distinct from maintaining the material and from communicating the result. Making that distinction supports scrutiny of the criterion and evidentiary basis for a quality assessment.

**Boundary**

An assessment is not a report of itself or the subsequent improvement action it may inform.

## ARB identity continuity

