              <documentation>Continuum navigation coordinate: II.1.2.2.1. Navigation asserts no semantic containment. Occurrence: architectural; no additional architectural instance or semantic relationship. Historical predecessor: R.2.6 [CT2] Clinical Quality Management; canonicalId=dc1bece79eb7452e951d03a2ee6dfaa6; Exchange identifier=id-e9b2533401765481aa27d5c901bd8fd2 Canonical element directory: canonicalId=89761f2d38f846c39df1df0975964288; Exchange identifier=id-cf5dcdc3ef505f91906dbc1eb61a469c. Existing governed hierarchy member; directory retained for leaves.</documentation>
              <element xsi:type="archimate:Capability" name="[CT2] Clinical Quality Management" id="id-cf5dcdc3ef505f91906dbc1eb61a469c">
                <documentation>Manage the clinical-quality distinctions materially required for R1/R2.

Clinical Quality Management supplies the criteria and evidence basis for evaluating clinical quality and communicating established findings. Its four children preserve the difference between the expected standard, the material considered, the assessment reached and the report of that assessment. This supports scrutiny of why a quality conclusion is justified rather than treating the presence of measurements as a judgement.

**Intent**

Make clinical-quality conclusions understandable in relation to their criteria, evidence and assessment authority.

**Boundary**

Reporting does not originate the conclusion or perform subsequent improvement. Neither a separate monitoring provider nor generic Continuous Improvement placement is established by this decomposition.

## ARB identity continuity

