            <folder name="II.1.2.2.2 [CT2] Clinical Safety Management" id="id-ff12b41c54d842c6bd49771a5b1692f2">
              <folder name="II.1.2.2.2.1 [CT3] Clinical Risk Identification" id="id-2070f775f2034640bc9a633d09b9469d">
                <documentation>Continuum navigation coordinate: II.1.2.2.2.1. Navigation asserts no semantic containment. Occurrence: architectural; no additional architectural instance or semantic relationship. Historical predecessor: R.2.7 [CT3] Clinical Risk Identification; canonicalId=690da55f1f5b4c44ba58cf67a717a564; Exchange identifier=id-aa118374de83598fa0d455e546899188 Canonical element directory: canonicalId=d54c19c6efaf42af82ad71a4142149d4; Exchange identifier=id-f8ecf9800e2451508fc9c7a43d0bc920. Existing governed hierarchy member; directory retained for leaves.</documentation>
                <element xsi:type="archimate:Capability" name="[CT3] Clinical Risk Identification" id="id-f8ecf9800e2451508fc9c7a43d0bc920">
                  <documentation>Recognise and characterise a clinical safety risk from applicable evidence.

Clinical Risk Identification recognises and characterises a safety risk from relevant evidence. It establishes the concern to which mitigation or active response may be directed, rather than assuming that every monitored deviation is already a clinical risk. Its value is the meaningful characterisation that makes proportionate safety consideration possible.

**Boundary**

Evidence observation alone does not identify risk or establish a mitigation or response decision.

