              <folder name="II.1.2.2.2.2 [CT3] Clinical Risk Mitigation Management" id="id-214e080158e14c728aa40e95a1f8630e">
                <documentation>Continuum navigation coordinate: II.1.2.2.2.2. Navigation asserts no semantic containment. Occurrence: architectural; no additional architectural instance or semantic relationship. Historical predecessor: R.2.8 [CT3] Clinical Risk Mitigation Management; canonicalId=0bd3311d89af45bb935fde20e719369c; Exchange identifier=id-b09b2931af455e1f816a1e0dd2566cd1 Canonical element directory: canonicalId=2c232ade21ec45619c3ee4e928bd97ee; Exchange identifier=id-e85728e190e25bb488c845e6e92016a4. Existing governed hierarchy member; directory retained for leaves.</documentation>
                <element xsi:type="archimate:Capability" name="[CT3] Clinical Risk Mitigation Management" id="id-e85728e190e25bb488c845e6e92016a4">
                  <documentation>Manage prospective/preventative measures reducing identified risk likelihood, exposure or consequence.

Clinical Risk Mitigation Management addresses prospective measures intended to reduce an identified risk's likelihood, exposure or consequences. It gives prevention a distinct responsibility alongside risk characterisation and active response. Required measures can involve other capabilities without transferring the ownership of their actions or information to safety management.

**Boundary**

Mitigation differs from containing or remediating a concern that has materialised or requires active intervention.

