              <folder name="II.1.2.2.2.3 [CT3] Clinical Risk Response Management" id="id-008de7ff790149f5bbb3e2042d63c4fd">
                <documentation>Continuum navigation coordinate: II.1.2.2.2.3. Navigation asserts no semantic containment. Occurrence: architectural; no additional architectural instance or semantic relationship. Historical predecessor: R.2.9 [CT3] Clinical Risk Response Management; canonicalId=20f719ab4b6741b393ef570b4d1b05df; Exchange identifier=id-495b46bdf1f05f93a7f948a5e95d7663 Canonical element directory: canonicalId=5e36cb137e4e4782b2ddbf78cdf0da7b; Exchange identifier=id-f4c49bf8522555c9aead252c0f829e25. Existing governed hierarchy member; directory retained for leaves.</documentation>
                <element xsi:type="archimate:Capability" name="[CT3] Clinical Risk Response Management" id="id-f4c49bf8522555c9aead252c0f829e25">
                  <documentation>Manage active response, containment and remediation where risk has materialised, is emerging or requires active intervention.

Clinical Risk Response Management manages active intervention, containment or remediation where a safety risk is emerging, materialised or otherwise demands action. Its purpose is to address the developing situation rather than only reduce future exposure. The responsibility remains clinical-risk-specific while the actual actions may belong to other established abilities.

**Boundary**

It is not a general enterprise incident-management container and does not acquire the clinical authority of responding participants.

