              <documentation>Continuum navigation coordinate: II.1.2.2.2. Navigation asserts no semantic containment. Occurrence: architectural; no additional architectural instance or semantic relationship. Historical predecessor: R.2.10 [CT2] Clinical Safety Management; canonicalId=650ccec030fa46cc8c9d6b508a841778; Exchange identifier=id-a0a61a36bcd45bf28f83c5ec1c6c5579 Canonical element directory: canonicalId=28d1bf3e514e4c29837ebedaf9e4917b; Exchange identifier=id-354b3f173afe530c8ff123c2a01b51fb. Existing governed hierarchy member; directory retained for leaves.</documentation>
              <element xsi:type="archimate:Capability" name="[CT2] Clinical Safety Management" id="id-354b3f173afe530c8ff123c2a01b51fb">
                <documentation>Manage the clinical-risk distinctions materially required for R1/R2.

Clinical Safety Management distinguishes recognising a safety risk from reducing future exposure and actively dealing with a developing or materialised concern. These responsibilities may use overlapping evidence, but their purposes differ: characterisation makes the risk intelligible, mitigation changes prospective risk, and response addresses the situation requiring action.

**Intent**

Support proportionate safety action grounded in the nature of the identified clinical risk.

**Boundary**

Monitoring evidence is not automatically risk identification. Other capabilities can perform required actions without transferring their responsibilities; the three children are not a mandatory sequence or exhaustive safety taxonomy.

## ARB identity continuity

