            <documentation>Continuum navigation coordinate: II.1.2.2. Navigation asserts no semantic containment. Occurrence: architectural; no additional architectural instance or semantic relationship. Historical predecessor: R.2.11 [CT1] Clinical Quality, Safety &amp; Improvement; canonicalId=b967c383dbcd4c24abe6a83ea5e79e00; Exchange identifier=id-e31496b3af1450f6ad7f931218f14b60 Canonical element directory: canonicalId=63837bf848774572a06b935af95581a2; Exchange identifier=id-1966794a16a75e03a984971281f020e8. Existing governed hierarchy member; directory retained for leaves.</documentation>
            <element xsi:type="archimate:Capability" name="[CT1] Clinical Quality, Safety &amp; Improvement" id="id-1966794a16a75e03a984971281f020e8">
              <documentation>Operational clinical quality, safety and improvement: monitoring clinical outcomes; identifying quality and safety concerns; adverse event and incident management, reporting and response; infection control; operational quality and safety monitoring; continuous quality improvement; and coordination of operational responses to identified concerns.

This capability addresses operational clinical quality and safety, including concerns, incidents, response and improvement. Its established safety branch distinguishes risk identification, prospective mitigation and active response. Its quality branch distinguishes criteria, evidence, assessment and reporting. Together these make it possible to reason about clinical quality without equating an observation, a judgement and the action taken in response.

**Intent**

Support recognition and management of clinical safety concerns and informed improvement of clinical quality.

**Boundary**

This is neither a generic enterprise incident container nor a replacement for macro-level Health Service Assurance. Its bounded decomposition does not exhaust clinical quality and safety practice.

**Harmonia Architectural Relevance**

Information about outcomes, risks, incidents and operational responses materially supports these responsibilities. Integrating that evidence does not assign clinical quality judgement or originating clinical authority to the platform.

## ARB identity continuity

Historical identity [b967c383dbcd4c24abe6a83ea5e79e00](b967c383dbcd4c24abe6a83ea5e79e00.md) has direct correspondence with this capability under HCRL 1.1.5-002. Historical provenance and UUID reservation remain with that record; this resource retains its existing identity and independent standing.</documentation>
