                <documentation>Continuum navigation coordinate: II.1.2.3.1.1. Navigation asserts no semantic containment. Occurrence: architectural; no additional architectural instance or semantic relationship. Historical predecessor: R.2.12 [CT3] Preventative Health Cohort Management; canonicalId=fef479f0fd5048b19b2aec770f0233fe; Exchange identifier=id-abb6bc8768f151f7889ffeb2382f7d01 Canonical element directory: canonicalId=97625bb28e5745d5994e1bffd4037188; Exchange identifier=id-d328fb8f811d551699099f3f2a6e1f43. Existing governed hierarchy member; directory retained for leaves.</documentation>
                <element xsi:type="archimate:Capability" name="[CT3] Preventative Health Cohort Management" id="id-d328fb8f811d551699099f3f2a6e1f43">
                  <documentation>Establish and manage the target population, inclusion/exclusion criteria, membership, stratification and applicable entry/exit context.

Preventative Health Cohort Management establishes who belongs to the population targeted for a preventative purpose. Inclusion, exclusion, stratification and entry or exit context make membership explainable rather than a list detached from its rationale. It provides a governed population context through which programme activity and reporting can be understood.

**Boundary**

A population at risk is not automatically a defined cohort, and cohort membership is not an individual clinical determination.

