              <folder name="II.1.2.3.1.2 [CT3] Preventative Health Education Services" id="id-ee58642b00b347d8b364469be4e277c6">
                <documentation>Continuum navigation coordinate: II.1.2.3.1.2. Navigation asserts no semantic containment. Occurrence: architectural; no additional architectural instance or semantic relationship. Historical predecessor: R.2.13 [CT3] Preventative Health Education Services; canonicalId=dbe10959237f405caeadef2a5748303a; Exchange identifier=id-c9caa2cf828a5c6f92cc681ec086e060 Canonical element directory: canonicalId=7541d9b3b65d47d286dabdc093cb0eed; Exchange identifier=id-210f08cf0a7e50a4b6515b7c25be2bf5. Existing governed hierarchy member; directory retained for leaves.</documentation>
                <element xsi:type="archimate:Capability" name="[CT3] Preventative Health Education Services" id="id-210f08cf0a7e50a4b6515b7c25be2bf5">
                  <documentation>Provide education intended to prevent adverse health outcomes and influence preventative knowledge or behaviour.

Preventative Health Education Services provides education intended to influence knowledge or behaviour so that adverse health outcomes can be prevented. Its purpose distinguishes it from general organisational communication: the educational contribution is directed to a preventative-health need. It can support organised programme activity without being equivalent to programme management or clinical intervention.

**Boundary**

Communicating educational material does not establish individual clinical assessment, treatment or programme effectiveness.

