              <folder name="II.1.2.3.1.3 [CT3] Preventative Health Problem Identification" id="id-00bc6c623beb4000ac0d141c6ef36a01">
                <documentation>Continuum navigation coordinate: II.1.2.3.1.3. Navigation asserts no semantic containment. Occurrence: architectural; no additional architectural instance or semantic relationship. Historical predecessor: R.2.14 [CT3] Preventative Health Problem Identification; canonicalId=b35d3521141c419fb676a79b2ede40bd; Exchange identifier=id-ea890856698a55b686338449e9b99984 Canonical element directory: canonicalId=c1567022671f433fa1eeb37a9d156d92; Exchange identifier=id-f53321c902e4521ba2fd87e1b18260c1. Existing governed hierarchy member; directory retained for leaves.</documentation>
                <element xsi:type="archimate:Capability" name="[CT3] Preventative Health Problem Identification" id="id-f53321c902e4521ba2fd87e1b18260c1">
                  <documentation>Identify and characterise a preventative-health problem warranting organised attention.

This capability establishes the preventative-health problem warranting organised attention. It gives an intended programme a reason grounded in the concern being addressed rather than assuming that a population statistic already defines the response. The identified problem can frame subsequent cohort and programme considerations without becoming an individual's clinical diagnosis.

**Boundary**

Population evidence informs problem identification but does not by itself establish a programme, cohort or individual care need.

