              <folder name="II.1.2.3.1.4 [CT3] Preventative Health Programme Management" id="id-bde443e85a944118ae2e2866cf56f1be">
                <documentation>Continuum navigation coordinate: II.1.2.3.1.4. Navigation asserts no semantic containment. Occurrence: architectural; no additional architectural instance or semantic relationship. Historical predecessor: R.2.15 [CT3] Preventative Health Programme Management; canonicalId=d71def9e76a544ff9761c672bb24f3be; Exchange identifier=id-48544f17a07c53839f82a273cce0d86e Canonical element directory: canonicalId=563d36b179d34cb6913253d06e8d77f6; Exchange identifier=id-6edcb625bec25de7b04c55e5f651ced8. Existing governed hierarchy member; directory retained for leaves.</documentation>
                <element xsi:type="archimate:Capability" name="[CT3] Preventative Health Programme Management" id="id-6edcb625bec25de7b04c55e5f651ced8">
                  <documentation>Establish and manage an organised response to a preventative-health need/objective without absorbing its delivery capabilities.

Preventative Health Programme Management establishes and manages an organised response to a preventative need or objective. It keeps the programme purpose and coordinated activity intelligible while allowing appointments, interventions and other delivery abilities to retain their own responsibilities. Screening and immunisation illustrate programmes rather than creating additional capability tiers.

**Boundary**

Managing the programme does not acquire the clinical or operational authority of the activities delivering it.

## ARB identity continuity

Historical identity [d71def9e76a544ff9761c672bb24f3be](d71def9e76a544ff9761c672bb24f3be.md) has direct correspondence with this capability under HCRL 1.1.5-002. Historical provenance and UUID reservation remain with that record; this resource retains its existing identity and independent standing.</documentation>
