              <folder name="II.1.2.3.1.5 [CT3] Preventative Health Programme Monitoring" id="id-857165b7e9ca470fbc6177ec075487e5">
                <documentation>Continuum navigation coordinate: II.1.2.3.1.5. Navigation asserts no semantic containment. Occurrence: architectural; no additional architectural instance or semantic relationship. Historical predecessor: R.2.16 [CT3] Preventative Health Programme Monitoring; canonicalId=e05f6310f6d544efaca5568604f27dd8; Exchange identifier=id-c31871a53f5255b08d5210ea58ce2683 Canonical element directory: canonicalId=945b40ced8004e1cbf7c98c731d17daf; Exchange identifier=id-2353057b450154eda7dddfb4ea6b088f. Existing governed hierarchy member; directory retained for leaves.</documentation>
                <element xsi:type="archimate:Capability" name="[CT3] Preventative Health Programme Monitoring" id="id-2353057b450154eda7dddfb4ea6b088f">
                  <documentation>Observe programme operation, reach, participation, coverage, progress and applicable performance.

This capability observes how a preventative programme is operating, including reach, participation, coverage and progress. It supplies an account of programme performance in the programme's own scope, rather than substituting population-health state for evidence of programme activity. That account can inform reporting or consideration of the programme without itself being an assurance conclusion.

**Boundary**

Programme monitoring is distinct from individual health monitoring, population assessment and independent assurance.

## ARB identity continuity

Historical identity [e05f6310f6d544efaca5568604f27dd8](e05f6310f6d544efaca5568604f27dd8.md) has direct correspondence with this capability under HCRL 1.1.5-002. Historical provenance and UUID reservation remain with that record; this resource retains its existing identity and independent standing.</documentation>
