              <folder name="II.1.2.3.1.6 [CT3] Preventative Health Reporting" id="id-744c17609b3f4f8aa812ca9d2a787268">
                <documentation>Continuum navigation coordinate: II.1.2.3.1.6. Navigation asserts no semantic containment. Occurrence: architectural; no additional architectural instance or semantic relationship. Historical predecessor: R.2.17 [CT3] Preventative Health Reporting; canonicalId=4faef45b4ebe4fa69e57c3d81bfea05f; Exchange identifier=id-1703ff7fa038538e9aa18358f56d18b0 Canonical element directory: canonicalId=d2ef01c4cab348df822e802ab084faae; Exchange identifier=id-a8aaef5643875dc0b4f7b5b85e1aed1a. Existing governed hierarchy member; directory retained for leaves.</documentation>
                <element xsi:type="archimate:Capability" name="[CT3] Preventative Health Reporting" id="id-a8aaef5643875dc0b4f7b5b85e1aed1a">
                  <documentation>Report established preventative-health problems, programmes, cohorts, activity, performance and outcomes.

Preventative Health Reporting communicates established information about preventative problems, programmes, cohorts, activity and outcomes. It brings these different subjects together for a reporting purpose while preserving their distinct meanings. A programme's reach and an observed population outcome can both be relevant without implying that one proves the other.

**Boundary**

Reporting does not originate the underlying problem, cohort or evaluation conclusion.

