              <documentation>Continuum navigation coordinate: II.1.2.3.1. Navigation asserts no semantic containment. Occurrence: architectural; no additional architectural instance or semantic relationship. Historical predecessor: R.2.18 [CT2] Preventative Health; canonicalId=80affa7bcd284ecbbcbc5092f8497ddf; Exchange identifier=id-63f5840bf3bf5ba5828c7d2b13795221 Canonical element directory: canonicalId=81be04a2d58548a4aea94f9aae90feb6; Exchange identifier=id-f383763eeeb6577bb01125fad97c5075. Existing governed hierarchy member; directory retained for leaves.</documentation>
              <element xsi:type="archimate:Capability" name="[CT2] Preventative Health" id="id-f383763eeeb6577bb01125fad97c5075">
                <documentation>Address preventative-health needs through organised activity with sufficient R1/R2 distinctions.

Preventative Health organises a response to a health problem before adverse outcomes arise or worsen. The established children distinguish why attention is warranted, how an organised programme is managed, who it targets, the education provided, what programme operation shows and what is reported. This allows a screening or immunisation programme to be explained without creating a new capability for every programme type.

**Intent**

Connect a preventative purpose with an identifiable target population and observable organised activity.

**Boundary**

Programme performance differs from population-health assessment and individual clinical monitoring. Unmodelled specialist responsibilities are not silently assigned to the existing children.

## ARB identity continuity

