            <documentation>Continuum navigation coordinate: II.1.2.3. Navigation asserts no semantic containment. Occurrence: architectural; no additional architectural instance or semantic relationship. Historical predecessor: R.2.19 [CT1] Community Health &amp; Wellbeing; canonicalId=175174c5cce549d2b154a4f6704721dc; Exchange identifier=id-0efaf106654e5f19bf85139a3a93a4fb Canonical element directory: canonicalId=b326b4aaf02a41a986ed22d184cbc152; Exchange identifier=id-2456cb6acb345c4c9f2ce404c69e8a2e. Existing governed hierarchy member; directory retained for leaves.</documentation>
            <element xsi:type="archimate:Capability" name="[CT1] Community Health &amp; Wellbeing" id="id-2456cb6acb345c4c9f2ce404c69e8a2e">
              <documentation>Support community health and wellbeing, including the bounded preventative-health abilities required for R1/R2. Wider environmental health, outreach and social determinants remain enterprise context without inferred additional decomposition.

Community Health &amp; Wellbeing frames organised activity supporting health beyond a single person's episode of care. The governed decomposition focuses on preventative health: identifying needs, defining programmes and cohorts, educating, observing programme operation and reporting. Wider outreach, environmental and social-determinant concerns remain enterprise context rather than additional modelled children.

**Intent**

Support organised prevention with a clear relationship between the health problem, intended population and programme activity.

**Boundary**

Programme management does not acquire the clinical or appointment responsibilities needed to deliver a programme.

**Harmonia Architectural Relevance**

Programme and cohort distinctions materially shape the information, notifications and care enablement required. This supports the Relevant classification without assigning wider public-health operating authority to Harmonia.

## ARB identity continuity

