              <documentation>Continuum navigation coordinate: II.1.2.4.1. Navigation asserts no semantic containment. Occurrence: architectural; no additional architectural instance or semantic relationship. Canonical element directory: canonicalId=f5defe141228490598115fe41db89bd7; Exchange identifier=id-69970b9c42b256a0ae2eb697c3767796. Existing governed hierarchy member; directory retained for leaves.</documentation>
              <element xsi:type="archimate:Capability" name="[CT2] Digital Communication Channel" id="id-69970b9c42b256a0ae2eb697c3767796">
                <documentation>Provide digitally mediated communication, notification and collaborative interaction between patients, practitioners and other health-service participants.

Digital Communication Channel supports communication between patients, practitioners and other participants through digitally mediated messages, notifications and collaborative interaction. Its organisational purpose is the exchange between participants: for example, a notification can connect someone to a care event without itself delivering care or changing the event's originating facts.

**Boundary**

A presentation interface used to exercise another capability is not automatically this communication ability. No CT3 set or general presentation BEC placement is established here.

## Qualified relationship assertions

Original source predicates, evidence and qualifications remain in the metadata. The ARB has now adjudicated their native treatment; explicitly unestablished relationship existence remains excluded. Native representation does not promote source standing.

