              <folder name="II.1.2.5.1.1 [CT3] Back-Office Services" id="id-6604fbbfb2ef4768b5a66043889503f1">
                <documentation>Continuum navigation coordinate: II.1.2.5.1.1. Navigation asserts no semantic containment. Occurrence: architectural; no additional architectural instance or semantic relationship. Canonical element directory: canonicalId=9f4d3705403647f4a1e25bc3dece035f; Exchange identifier=id-44b93d25bc505fd7a63a17526ab77cf5. Existing governed hierarchy member; directory retained for leaves.</documentation>
                <element xsi:type="archimate:Capability" name="[CT3] Back-Office Services" id="id-44b93d25bc505fd7a63a17526ab77cf5">
                  <documentation>Provide administrative/support services on which health-service activity depends.

Back-Office Services provides the administrative and support activity on which health-service operations depend. Within Corporate Support Services it retains an enterprise context for dependencies that may affect whether service activity can proceed. The model stops at this broad responsibility rather than allocating each administrative function to Harmonia.

**Boundary**

Consumption of support status does not transfer administrative operating authority or establish a more detailed decomposition.</documentation>
