              <folder name="II.1.2.5.1.2 [CT3] Communications &amp; Publicity" id="id-b67cb43a6a434ccba6cab298916fe5e6">
                <documentation>Continuum navigation coordinate: II.1.2.5.1.2. Navigation asserts no semantic containment. Occurrence: architectural; no additional architectural instance or semantic relationship. Canonical element directory: canonicalId=1fec53fb12444abcac41094dace1d3c2; Exchange identifier=id-ea854ef849a35f8dac4fd8c6810b020a. Existing governed hierarchy member; directory retained for leaves.</documentation>
                <element xsi:type="archimate:Capability" name="[CT3] Communications &amp; Publicity" id="id-ea854ef849a35f8dac4fd8c6810b020a">
                  <documentation>Manage organisational communication/publication arrangements relevant to information availability/distribution.

Communications &amp; Publicity manages organisational publication and communication arrangements relevant to information availability and distribution. It provides enterprise communication context without being identical to clinical record exchange or digitally mediated participant interaction. The governed decomposition retains that broad support role without adding specific publicity or communications functions.

**Boundary**

Organisational communication does not originate the clinical facts or governed conclusions it may convey.</documentation>
