              <folder name="II.1.2.5.1.3 [CT3] Facilities Management" id="id-8485c038ac3d41a9a5005b9de137b71b">
                <documentation>Continuum navigation coordinate: II.1.2.5.1.3. Navigation asserts no semantic containment. Occurrence: architectural; no additional architectural instance or semantic relationship. Canonical element directory: canonicalId=9c82e623bd174409b90d24af6b58ebf0; Exchange identifier=id-7528db1a70905b898c093d3ae7e47bcc. Existing governed hierarchy member; directory retained for leaves.</documentation>
                <element xsi:type="archimate:Capability" name="[CT3] Facilities Management" id="id-7528db1a70905b898c093d3ae7e47bcc">
                  <documentation>Manage physical facilities/services and applicable resource, location, availability and facility-state context.

Facilities Management manages physical facilities and services, including the state and availability context relevant to health activity. It contributes the real-world conditions that location definitions alone cannot establish. This distinguishes a place recognised in a directory from a facility being operated and maintained for use.

**Boundary**

Harmonia's consumption of facility constraints does not make it the facilities operator or establish collective service readiness.</documentation>
