                <documentation>Continuum navigation coordinate: II.1.2.6.1.1. Navigation asserts no semantic containment. Occurrence: architectural; no additional architectural instance or semantic relationship. Canonical element directory: canonicalId=aeb8e6d2225a4df38e61ae116850b32c; Exchange identifier=id-bd52520eecc15d55b22866aee1a3c819. Existing governed hierarchy member; directory retained for leaves.</documentation>
                <element xsi:type="archimate:Capability" name="[CT3] Diagnostic Data Management" id="id-bd52520eecc15d55b22866aee1a3c819">
                  <documentation>Manage acquired or produced diagnostic evidence as information, including identity, association, integrity, organisation, availability and lifecycle.

Diagnostic Data Management maintains acquired or produced diagnostic evidence as usable information. Its responsibility includes identity, association, integrity, organisation and lifecycle so that evidence can be found and understood in the right diagnostic context. It addresses the evidence record independently of the professional conclusion subsequently drawn from it.

**Boundary**

Managing diagnostic data neither interprets that data nor governs the authoritative expression of findings in a report.</documentation>
