                  <property key="v0.2 / Source Locators" value="[{&quot;anchor&quot;:&quot;ct2--diagnostic-support-provision&quot;,&quot;line&quot;:470,&quot;source&quot;:&quot;business&quot;,&quot;text&quot;:&quot;| Diagnostic Data Management | Manage acquired or produced diagnostic evidence as information, including identity, association, integrity, organisation, availability and lifecycle. |&quot;},{&quot;anchor&quot;:&quot;ct2--diagnostic-support-provision&quot;,&quot;line&quot;:463,&quot;source&quot;:&quot;business&quot;,&quot;text&quot;:&quot;**Decomposition assertion:** Each named child in this table is a CT3 Business Capability whose immediate CT2 parent is Diagnostic Support Provision; that CT2 has the CT1 parent stated above.&quot;},{&quot;anchor&quot;:&quot;ct2--diagnostic-support-provision&quot;,&quot;line&quot;:475,&quot;source&quot;:&quot;business&quot;,&quot;text&quot;:&quot;**Boundary:** Scheduling ≠ performance ≠ evidence management ≠ interpretation ≠ governed report ≠ distribution. Specimen and data responsibilities remain distinct. Diagnostic interpretation does not establish patient-level Clinical Determination from the total clinical context. Generic appointments are distinct from diagnostic-specific constraints. Diagnostic Order Management is not established here as a subordinate capability. Signing/finalisation are report behaviours, not additional CT3s. Services may exercise a subset, concurrently or iteratively; no mandatory diagnostic workflow is established.&quot;}]"/>
