              <folder name="II.1.2.6.1.2 [CT3] Diagnostic Interpretation" id="id-3bcaeda92c4a48aaaad18e1b9b5b2773">
                <documentation>Continuum navigation coordinate: II.1.2.6.1.2. Navigation asserts no semantic containment. Occurrence: architectural; no additional architectural instance or semantic relationship. Canonical element directory: canonicalId=82ad867109f1438eb1b0916ed9cd820f; Exchange identifier=id-5db277707e1f50fab4fc4ce1c9dddaba. Existing governed hierarchy member; directory retained for leaves.</documentation>
                <element xsi:type="archimate:Capability" name="[CT3] Diagnostic Interpretation" id="id-5db277707e1f50fab4fc4ce1c9dddaba">
                  <documentation>Establish what diagnostic evidence demonstrates within the diagnostic service’s professional scope.

Diagnostic Interpretation establishes what diagnostic evidence demonstrates within the service's professional scope. It turns evidence into diagnostic findings without claiming the wider patient-level judgement that considers all clinical circumstances. Separating interpretation from acquisition and reporting makes the professional contribution clear even when one service performs all three.

**Boundary**

Patient-level Clinical Determination remains distinct, as do report authorisation and distribution.</documentation>
