              <folder name="II.1.2.6.2.3 [CT3] Medication Dose Administration Aid Provision" id="id-f5adc5dc4f2940fa91712536999b6a05">
                <documentation>Continuum navigation coordinate: II.1.2.6.2.3. Navigation asserts no semantic containment. Occurrence: architectural; no additional architectural instance or semantic relationship. Canonical element directory: canonicalId=bd597608766b4d709703977c02cc5f07; Exchange identifier=id-6c8a8c7d0d8f51f8982e57af660d1033. Existing governed hierarchy member; directory retained for leaves.</documentation>
                <element xsi:type="archimate:Capability" name="[CT3] Medication Dose Administration Aid Provision" id="id-6c8a8c7d0d8f51f8982e57af660d1033">
                  <documentation>Prepare and provide organised medication doses supporting administration according to an already established regimen.

This capability prepares and supplies organised doses to support administration under an already established medication regimen. Its purpose is to make that regimen easier to follow in practice while preserving the difference between organising doses and choosing therapy. The business responsibility is not defined by any particular commercial packaging arrangement.

**Boundary**

Preparing a dose aid does not establish the regimen or demonstrate that a dose was administered.</documentation>
