              <folder name="II.1.2.6.2.4 [CT3] Non-Prescription Medication Provision" id="id-946ad21e0e0d4fefb28a5c599d49f1e3">
                <documentation>Continuum navigation coordinate: II.1.2.6.2.4. Navigation asserts no semantic containment. Occurrence: architectural; no additional architectural instance or semantic relationship. Canonical element directory: canonicalId=7bbe4810fb974a8ab6d47b30d6475df3; Exchange identifier=id-64b219d99dbd55af98af1d87b7ee4f5e. Existing governed hierarchy member; directory retained for leaves.</documentation>
                <element xsi:type="archimate:Capability" name="[CT3] Non-Prescription Medication Provision" id="id-64b219d99dbd55af98af1d87b7ee4f5e">
                  <documentation>Provide medication not requiring an applicable prescription, subject to professional, regulatory and safety controls.

Non-Prescription Medication Provision makes medication available where the applicable conditions do not require a prescription. It remains a professional, regulated and safety-constrained responsibility rather than an unrestricted supply transaction. Its distinction from prescription dispensing preserves the different authority basis under which provision occurs.

**Boundary**

Provision neither establishes diagnosis nor proves use or administration of the medication.</documentation>
                  <property key="v0.2 / Source Capture Key" value="business-capability:non-prescription-medication-provision"/>
                  <property key="v0.2 / Snapshot Reference ID" value="HCM-BC-non-prescription-medication-provision"/>
