              <folder name="II.1.2.6.2.5 [CT3] Prescription Medication Dispensing" id="id-817902bcf59147b89bb2f8a77295f2db">
                <documentation>Continuum navigation coordinate: II.1.2.6.2.5. Navigation asserts no semantic containment. Occurrence: architectural; no additional architectural instance or semantic relationship. Canonical element directory: canonicalId=fef5b79eea77438d9d453a7daef744fc; Exchange identifier=id-710e6b63b34f5919a25a78c6591ce61b. Existing governed hierarchy member; directory retained for leaves.</documentation>
                <element xsi:type="archimate:Capability" name="[CT3] Prescription Medication Dispensing" id="id-710e6b63b34f5919a25a78c6591ce61b">
                  <documentation>Professionally prepare and provide medication according to an applicable authorised prescription/order and dispensing requirements.

Prescription Medication Dispensing is the professional preparation and provision of medication against an applicable authorised prescription or order. It fulfils a pharmacy responsibility grounded in the prescribed intent and dispensing requirements. The resulting dispensing event provides different evidence from the prescribing decision and from later administration to the individual.

**Boundary**

Dispensing does not establish that medication was administered; unresolved specialised compounding must not be silently assigned here.</documentation>
