              <folder name="II.1.2.7.1.2 [CT3] Clinical Knowledge Context Extraction" id="id-2f36bf536f1544bd92de52e5794f7617">
                <documentation>Continuum navigation coordinate: II.1.2.7.1.2. Navigation asserts no semantic containment. Occurrence: architectural; no additional architectural instance or semantic relationship. Canonical element directory: canonicalId=0911997eb4584172afd10b1d37946061; Exchange identifier=id-4c3010101ae95144ba9af9f010df539b. Existing governed hierarchy member; directory retained for leaves.</documentation>
                <element xsi:type="archimate:Capability" name="[CT3] Clinical Knowledge Context Extraction" id="id-4c3010101ae95144ba9af9f010df539b">
                  <documentation>Extract relevant material while preserving its source/context relationship.

Clinical Knowledge Context Extraction selects relevant material while retaining its relationship to the source and context. Its purpose is to make potential knowledge material available without stripping away the circumstances needed to understand it. Extracted material remains distinguishable from the reusable knowledge subsequently formulated from it.

**Boundary**

Extraction does not establish approval or turn source information into an individual clinical conclusion.</documentation>
