              <folder name="II.1.2.7.1.6 [CT3] Clinical Knowledge Review &amp; Approval Management" id="id-a34c59b80b324631b9e73aa625a39325">
                <documentation>Continuum navigation coordinate: II.1.2.7.1.6. Navigation asserts no semantic containment. Occurrence: architectural; no additional architectural instance or semantic relationship. Canonical element directory: canonicalId=ee04d00077d548a7a0a2dffd424c3d78; Exchange identifier=id-e92f6df14dcd51a0905d0c294b78beb1. Existing governed hierarchy member; directory retained for leaves.</documentation>
                <element xsi:type="archimate:Capability" name="[CT3] Clinical Knowledge Review &amp; Approval Management" id="id-e92f6df14dcd51a0905d0c294b78beb1">
                  <documentation>Manage review, endorsement, approval/rejection, conditions and applicable history for intended governed use.

This capability manages the review and governed standing of reusable knowledge, including endorsement, rejection, conditions and history. It establishes how the knowledge may legitimately be treated for its intended use rather than assuming that formulation makes it trustworthy or approved. Temporal standing matters where a later review changes the conditions for use.

**Boundary**

Approval does not establish applicability to a particular individual or replace the responsible clinical judgement.</documentation>
