            <folder name="II.1.2.7.2 [CT2] Health Information Management" id="id-67076ca6e3f945659ba301c51602939f">
              <folder name="II.1.2.7.2.1 [CT3] Health Information Catalogue and Index Management" id="id-0ccba96949a84d20a6b8cd88d08367bd">
                <documentation>Continuum navigation coordinate: II.1.2.7.2.1. Navigation asserts no semantic containment. Occurrence: architectural; no additional architectural instance or semantic relationship. Canonical element directory: canonicalId=4c834101307546d39a0ac36b07358faf; Exchange identifier=id-0499c33921ce517c8a82f4eb516adc6d. Existing governed hierarchy member; directory retained for leaves.</documentation>
                <element xsi:type="archimate:Capability" name="[CT3] Health Information Catalogue and Index Management" id="id-0499c33921ce517c8a82f4eb516adc6d">
                  <documentation>Manage descriptive catalogues/indexes through which information existence and location can be established.

This capability maintains the descriptive aids through which information existence and location can be established. It makes information discoverable without equating the catalogue entry with the content it describes. Within information management it answers where relevant information may be found before the separate question of obtaining it under an authorised context.

**Boundary**

Discoverability does not authorise access, retrieve the content or communicate it to a recipient.</documentation>
