                  <property key="v0.2 / Source Locators" value="[{&quot;anchor&quot;:&quot;ct2--health-information-management&quot;,&quot;line&quot;:657,&quot;source&quot;:&quot;business&quot;,&quot;text&quot;:&quot;| Health Information Catalogue and Index Management | Manage descriptive catalogues/indexes through which information existence and location can be established. |&quot;},{&quot;anchor&quot;:&quot;ct2--health-information-management&quot;,&quot;line&quot;:650,&quot;source&quot;:&quot;business&quot;,&quot;text&quot;:&quot;**Decomposition assertion:** Each named child in this table is a CT3 Business Capability whose immediate CT2 parent is Health Information Management; that CT2 has the CT1 parent stated above.&quot;},{&quot;anchor&quot;:&quot;ct2--health-information-management&quot;,&quot;line&quot;:662,&quot;source&quot;:&quot;business&quot;,&quot;text&quot;:&quot;**Boundary:** Semantic authority ≠ semantic binding ≠ content; a persisted value is not self-describing health information. Structure/binding management does not govern the referenced terminology/value set. Catalogue existence/location ≠ retrieval ≠ communication ≠ presentation; discoverability does not authorise access. Compartment membership may inform but does not determine authorisation. Correlation establishes neither clinical interpretation nor entity identity. Current state and immutable historical operational truth remain distinct; managing information does not originate its facts. Structures are not equated with FHIR resources, physical schemas or storage mechanisms.&quot;}]"/>
