              <folder name="II.1.2.7.2.2 [CT3] Health Information Compartmentalisation" id="id-810b0750660347c5a15ffa5104d32f27">
                <documentation>Continuum navigation coordinate: II.1.2.7.2.2. Navigation asserts no semantic containment. Occurrence: architectural; no additional architectural instance or semantic relationship. Canonical element directory: canonicalId=660d78d6a34041939d1c290266d47f03; Exchange identifier=id-8f7817d6ddd25778ae7d5d5effbbbd16. Existing governed hierarchy member; directory retained for leaves.</documentation>
                <element xsi:type="archimate:Capability" name="[CT3] Health Information Compartmentalisation" id="id-8f7817d6ddd25778ae7d5d5effbbbd16">
                  <documentation>Manage contextual association, partitioning and bounded information groupings.

Health Information Compartmentalisation establishes contextual associations and bounded groupings of information. It makes the relationship of information to a business context explicit, allowing groupings to carry meaning beyond physical storage location. That context can inform governed use while remaining distinct from sensitivity classification and a particular access decision.

**Boundary**

Compartment membership neither establishes permission nor replaces classification or terminology governance.</documentation>
