              <folder name="II.1.2.7.2.3 [CT3] Health Information Data Correlation" id="id-a526f4d3bfc442458e19aaf1c500da29">
                <documentation>Continuum navigation coordinate: II.1.2.7.2.3. Navigation asserts no semantic containment. Occurrence: architectural; no additional architectural instance or semantic relationship. Canonical element directory: canonicalId=6c41e90a8cf24ed689d9d6a363c8d3fe; Exchange identifier=id-aeafb86f7bb65c15acebe5f0048c9ef8. Existing governed hierarchy member; directory retained for leaves.</documentation>
                <element xsi:type="archimate:Capability" name="[CT3] Health Information Data Correlation" id="id-aeafb86f7bb65c15acebe5f0048c9ef8">
                  <documentation>Establish meaningful relationships between independently managed information items/sets.

Health Information Data Correlation establishes meaningful relationships between independently managed information items or sets. It helps information be understood together without requiring a merger of their identities, histories or originating authority. The responsibility is the association itself, rather than a clinical conclusion inferred from the associated content.

**Boundary**

Correlation does not establish person identity, clinical interpretation or ownership transfer between the related items.</documentation>
