              <folder name="II.1.2.7.2.4 [CT3] Health Information Data Management" id="id-266b0b21a6a9442a88e20edaba213ddd">
                <documentation>Continuum navigation coordinate: II.1.2.7.2.4. Navigation asserts no semantic containment. Occurrence: architectural; no additional architectural instance or semantic relationship. Canonical element directory: canonicalId=9565887a92164432933ea97e95af2368; Exchange identifier=id-f83a006f0fc9592a8d5a9198c81aaae3. Existing governed hierarchy member; directory retained for leaves.</documentation>
                <element xsi:type="archimate:Capability" name="[CT3] Health Information Data Management" id="id-f83a006f0fc9592a8d5a9198c81aaae3">
                  <documentation>Manage actual health-information content within applicable governed structures.

Health Information Data Management concerns the actual content maintained within applicable governed structures. It keeps the represented information distinct from definitions describing how that information should be organised and interpreted. Within Health Information Management, its responsibility is meaningful content rather than mere successful persistence of values.

**Boundary**

Managing content does not originate its clinical facts or acquire the authority of its semantic references.</documentation>
