              <folder name="II.1.2.7.2.5 [CT3] Health Information Data Retrieval" id="id-2054378632ce4174a24fafd429b19b3c">
                <documentation>Continuum navigation coordinate: II.1.2.7.2.5. Navigation asserts no semantic containment. Occurrence: architectural; no additional architectural instance or semantic relationship. Canonical element directory: canonicalId=082760fc4804489a81eaed3e4fd9daa9; Exchange identifier=id-1619920904835b448ad96b47ac031fc8. Existing governed hierarchy member; directory retained for leaves.</documentation>
                <element xsi:type="archimate:Capability" name="[CT3] Health Information Data Retrieval" id="id-1619920904835b448ad96b47ac031fc8">
                  <documentation>Obtain identified information under an applicable authorised request/context.

Health Information Data Retrieval obtains identified information under an applicable authorised request and context. It supplies the content whose existence may already be known through a catalogue or index. The distinction matters because locating an item, obtaining it and presenting it to a person each establish different outcomes.

**Boundary**

Retrieval does not itself grant permission, provide participant communication or confer authority over the retrieved facts.</documentation>
