              <folder name="II.1.2.7.2.6 [CT3] Health Information Lifecycle Management" id="id-a29dbb15557a4c33b1fba5d1e0654fe2">
                <documentation>Continuum navigation coordinate: II.1.2.7.2.6. Navigation asserts no semantic containment. Occurrence: architectural; no additional architectural instance or semantic relationship. Canonical element directory: canonicalId=874cd3b294184f928dbb7f656abd97f0; Exchange identifier=id-12f544f28418535f8054f8e1a398cd9c. Existing governed hierarchy member; directory retained for leaves.</documentation>
                <element xsi:type="archimate:Capability" name="[CT3] Health Information Lifecycle Management" id="id-12f544f28418535f8054f8e1a398cd9c">
                  <documentation>Govern state, amendment, correction, supersession, currency, retention and disposition while preserving provenance and historical meaning.

Health Information Lifecycle Management governs how information's state and temporal standing change through amendment, correction, supersession, retention and disposition. It allows current knowledge to change without retrospectively rewriting what was previously received, known or managed. That distinction supports interpretation of both the present representation and its historical operational meaning.

**Boundary**

Current authoritative state differs from historical truth; preserving either does not confer originating authority for the represented facts.</documentation>
