              <folder name="II.1.2.7.2.7 [CT3] Health Information Structure Management" id="id-f77c60b0b0e843349e7f1834f508902f">
                <documentation>Continuum navigation coordinate: II.1.2.7.2.7. Navigation asserts no semantic containment. Occurrence: architectural; no additional architectural instance or semantic relationship. Canonical element directory: canonicalId=c3b3e39dd141448e96b7dd7b4c4516f2; Exchange identifier=id-772af14dd93455b2967714fa826da898. Existing governed hierarchy member; directory retained for leaves.</documentation>
                <element xsi:type="archimate:Capability" name="[CT3] Health Information Structure Management" id="id-772af14dd93455b2967714fa826da898">
                  <documentation>Manage structures, element/reference definitions, constraints and semantic bindings giving content unambiguous meaning.

This capability manages the structures, element definitions, references and bindings that make content interpretable. It addresses how a represented item can have an unambiguous meaning without treating the structure as the clinical fact itself. Semantic bindings identify applicable governed references while preserving their external authority.

**Boundary**

Structure management is not terminology governance and does not prescribe FHIR resources, physical schemas or storage technology.</documentation>
