            <documentation>Continuum navigation coordinate: II.1.2.7. Navigation asserts no semantic containment. Occurrence: architectural; no additional architectural instance or semantic relationship. Historical predecessor: R.2.23 [CT1] Health Information &amp; Knowledge Management; canonicalId=a1c557bd263047d0b3ff566cf50b98c1; Exchange identifier=id-1441d728bfb35d509cf6f8a39ed3f504 Canonical element directory: canonicalId=cca5d5abec204b339eb5b9bd924ed64e; Exchange identifier=id-593d0a2ec7f6521383b23ef03ca092ef. Existing governed hierarchy member; directory retained for leaves.</documentation>
            <element xsi:type="archimate:Capability" name="[CT1] Health Information &amp; Knowledge Management" id="id-593d0a2ec7f6521383b23ef03ca092ef">
              <documentation>Manage governed health-information content, structures, lifecycle, catalogues, compartments, correlation and retrieval, alongside reusable clinical knowledge and its governed standing.

This capability governs both health information and reusable clinical knowledge while preserving their different meanings. Health Information Management concerns content, structures, lifecycle, discovery context, grouping, correlation and retrieval. Clinical Knowledge Management concerns identifying and formulating reusable knowledge and establishing its governed standing. A source clinical fact can contribute to knowledge without becoming a general clinical conclusion merely through reuse.

**Intent**

Keep information interpretable and usable across time and context while making the standing and limits of reusable knowledge explicit.

**Boundary**

Managing or preserving information does not originate its clinical facts. Governing structures and binding concepts does not acquire the authority of the terminology they reference.

**Harmonia Architectural Relevance**

These are substantive information-management responsibilities within Harmonia's assigned boundary. The Core classification remains bounded by information authority, active/durable-state separation and clinical decision authority.

## ARB identity continuity

Historical identity [a1c557bd263047d0b3ff566cf50b98c1](a1c557bd263047d0b3ff566cf50b98c1.md) has direct correspondence with this capability under HCRL 1.1.5-002. Historical provenance and UUID reservation remain with that record; this resource retains its existing identity and independent standing.</documentation>
