              <folder name="II.1.2.8.1.2 [CT3] Clinical Device Feature &amp; Release Management" id="id-55006bcca1234c64ad9875fe144ef1e2">
                <documentation>Continuum navigation coordinate: II.1.2.8.1.2. Navigation asserts no semantic containment. Occurrence: architectural; no additional architectural instance or semantic relationship. Canonical element directory: canonicalId=23d87ead4cdc40b785b006ca80f6d7b1; Exchange identifier=id-64523cf9b3a850c0986ad84f59880fb8. Existing governed hierarchy member; directory retained for leaves.</documentation>
                <element xsi:type="archimate:Capability" name="[CT3] Clinical Device Feature &amp; Release Management" id="id-64523cf9b3a850c0986ad84f59880fb8">
                  <documentation>Manage functional/release state, including applicable software, firmware, configuration and enabled device characteristics.

This capability governs the functional state of a device, including applicable software, firmware, configuration and enabled characteristics. Two instances of the same model may therefore have materially different capabilities in service. The responsibility makes those differences intelligible without reducing device governance to physical inventory or location.

**Boundary**

Release state is distinct from maintenance condition, deployment and professional authority to use the device.</documentation>
