              <folder name="II.1.2.8.1.3 [CT3] Clinical Device Integration Provision" id="id-c162ed16a95849a1a7f6bc04480f79c6">
                <documentation>Continuum navigation coordinate: II.1.2.8.1.3. Navigation asserts no semantic containment. Occurrence: architectural; no additional architectural instance or semantic relationship. Canonical element directory: canonicalId=7abab1d7d68f48cea565df752fad34c4; Exchange identifier=id-2ce5b7402493530699b6bf9f6ea83d71. Existing governed hierarchy member; directory retained for leaves.</documentation>
                <element xsi:type="archimate:Capability" name="[CT3] Clinical Device Integration Provision" id="id-2ce5b7402493530699b6bf9f6ea83d71">
                  <documentation>Establish and maintain the device’s capability and configuration to participate in applicable information exchanges.

Clinical Device Integration Provision establishes the device capability and configuration required to participate in applicable information exchanges. Its outcome is an integration-ready arrangement, which must remain distinguishable from data actually acquired or exchanged. This allows an architect to discuss whether connectivity has been enabled without assuming that a particular clinical feed has operated successfully.

**Boundary**

Provisioning does not demonstrate data integration, clinical interpretation or downstream authority for the data.</documentation>
