              <folder name="II.1.2.8.1.4 [CT3] Clinical Device Inventory Management" id="id-a8b595411b7b458cbacee2115a248a95">
                <documentation>Continuum navigation coordinate: II.1.2.8.1.4. Navigation asserts no semantic containment. Occurrence: architectural; no additional architectural instance or semantic relationship. Canonical element directory: canonicalId=f8205d4cf8144f34b2da1139ff45c868; Exchange identifier=id-9a98e5b1b7f05f67b2a43383e5e996da. Existing governed hierarchy member; directory retained for leaves.</documentation>
                <element xsi:type="archimate:Capability" name="[CT3] Clinical Device Inventory Management" id="id-9a98e5b1b7f05f67b2a43383e5e996da">
                  <documentation>Establish what devices exist and their managed asset identity, specification, ownership/custody and inventory context.

Clinical Device Inventory Management establishes the managed identity and inventory context of the device estate. Specification, ownership and custody make it possible to distinguish which devices exist from their current release, deployment or use. That stable asset context supports subsequent technology-management responsibilities without claiming their different outcomes.

**Boundary**

Inventory presence does not establish readiness, functional release state or current assignment to a care requirement.</documentation>
                  <property key="v0.2 / Source Capture Key" value="business-capability:clinical-device-inventory-management"/>
                  <property key="v0.2 / Snapshot Reference ID" value="HCM-BC-clinical-device-inventory-management"/>
                  <property key="v0.2 / LaTeX Label" value="cap:bc-clinical-device-inventory-management"/>
                  <property key="v0.2 / Construct Type" value="capability"/>
