              <folder name="II.1.2.8.1.5 [CT3] Clinical Device Lifecycle Management" id="id-2c43b804222d4f4ead092fcff74c1020">
                <documentation>Continuum navigation coordinate: II.1.2.8.1.5. Navigation asserts no semantic containment. Occurrence: architectural; no additional architectural instance or semantic relationship. Canonical element directory: canonicalId=186667f5a3844d10a236af73bc91a0de; Exchange identifier=id-de61ba0f4b035f648ed61bfb9552a476. Existing governed hierarchy member; directory retained for leaves.</documentation>
                <element xsi:type="archimate:Capability" name="[CT3] Clinical Device Lifecycle Management" id="id-de61ba0f4b035f648ed61bfb9552a476">
                  <documentation>Govern introduction, continued service, review, replacement, withdrawal, decommissioning and retirement within the overall device estate.

Clinical Device Lifecycle Management governs whether devices enter, remain in or leave the managed estate. Introduction, review, replacement, withdrawal and retirement concern the device's overall service disposition. This gives technology management a longer-lived responsibility than the device's current loan, release or data-exchange session.

**Boundary**

Lifecycle disposition differs from monitoring and restoring device condition; the maintenance-membership discrepancy remains unresolved.</documentation>
