              <folder name="II.1.2.8.1.6 [CT3] Clinical Device Loan &amp; Deployment Management" id="id-04a2c1b93c2543a4ae14f50e728dd850">
                <documentation>Continuum navigation coordinate: II.1.2.8.1.6. Navigation asserts no semantic containment. Occurrence: architectural; no additional architectural instance or semantic relationship. Canonical element directory: canonicalId=5ac802cf322d408f82c4a28cd24cb43b; Exchange identifier=id-7218b8cce3dd59beafac830a7ffaba9f. Existing governed hierarchy member; directory retained for leaves.</documentation>
                <element xsi:type="archimate:Capability" name="[CT3] Clinical Device Loan &amp; Deployment Management" id="id-7218b8cce3dd59beafac830a7ffaba9f">
                  <documentation>Manage device loan, issue, assignment, placement, return and deployment.

Clinical Device Loan &amp; Deployment Management manages where devices are placed and the issue, assignment, return or loan context under which they are available. It connects an identifiable device with its operational deployment rather than assuming ownership or inventory presence explains its current use. This supports an intelligible account of the device estate as placements change.

**Boundary**

Deployment is not device-specific user enablement, clinical use or evidence of clinical privilege.</documentation>
