              <folder name="II.1.2.8.1.8 [CT3] Clinical Device Utilisation Support" id="id-89cdb337168a4f2ab446b08bd00f0fc2">
                <documentation>Continuum navigation coordinate: II.1.2.8.1.8. Navigation asserts no semantic containment. Occurrence: architectural; no additional architectural instance or semantic relationship. Canonical element directory: canonicalId=0100cdb80a0c41c5930b1ca66248adf9; Exchange identifier=id-ac89b649b2045f1f9a228857bc828d26. Existing governed hierarchy member; directory retained for leaves.</documentation>
                <element xsi:type="archimate:Capability" name="[CT3] Clinical Device Utilisation Support" id="id-ac89b649b2045f1f9a228857bc828d26">
                  <documentation>Enable and support otherwise appropriately authorised users to use the particular device safely and effectively.

Clinical Device Utilisation Support helps otherwise appropriately authorised users use a particular device safely and effectively. It represents the device-specific enablement needed beyond general professional qualifications. Within technology management it addresses the practical support for use, without making that support the clinical action performed with the device.

**Boundary**

Professional qualification or privilege alone does not establish device-specific enablement; enablement does not confer clinical authority.</documentation>
