            <documentation>Continuum navigation coordinate: II.1.2.8. Navigation asserts no semantic containment. Occurrence: architectural; no additional architectural instance or semantic relationship. Historical predecessor: R.2.24 [CT1] Health Products &amp; Clinical Technology; canonicalId=a631a8600b8b49df9ef452c48c91349a; Exchange identifier=id-8789275fcf145364aaac9cfbe25bbce6 Canonical element directory: canonicalId=54388e3202c2403089b5c476c78c4567; Exchange identifier=id-06479aa74b3554608b6305af19064390. Existing governed hierarchy member; directory retained for leaves.</documentation>
            <element xsi:type="archimate:Capability" name="[CT1] Health Products &amp; Clinical Technology" id="id-06479aa74b3554608b6305af19064390">
              <documentation>Manage health products and clinical technology in the care environment, with distinct device inventory, functional/release, deployment, utilisation, integration and lifecycle responsibilities. Product procurement and supply context is retained without inferring further Health Product Management decomposition.

This capability manages health products and clinical technology as business concerns in the care environment. Its established clinical-technology branch distinguishes knowledge of the device estate, functional state, deployment, user enablement, integration and lifecycle disposition. Product procurement and supply remain relevant context without a newly inferred Health Product Management decomposition.

**Intent**

Keep the technology context needed for safe service activity and information exchange coherent and governed.

**Boundary**

Device-specific enablement, clinical privilege and use in care are different concerns. The seven established device children do not resolve the separate maintenance-membership discrepancy.

**Harmonia Architectural Relevance**

Integration provision and device-data integration materially affect exchanged information and its care context. Supply-chain, maintenance and clinical-use authority are not transferred to Harmonia.

## ARB identity continuity

Historical identity [a631a8600b8b49df9ef452c48c91349a](a631a8600b8b49df9ef452c48c91349a.md) has direct correspondence with this capability under HCRL 1.1.5-002. Historical provenance and UUID reservation remain with that record; this resource retains its existing identity and independent standing.</documentation>
