              <documentation>Continuum navigation coordinate: II.1.2.9.1. Navigation asserts no semantic containment. Occurrence: architectural; no additional architectural instance or semantic relationship. Canonical element directory: canonicalId=f263989e25c9469cac1bbad6491432f0; Exchange identifier=id-3a606ade585a5938971ee858eec584a2. Existing governed hierarchy member; directory retained for leaves.</documentation>
              <element xsi:type="archimate:Capability" name="[CT2] Health Innovation" id="id-3a606ade585a5938971ee858eec584a2">
                <documentation>Consider health-service and clinical innovation within the R1/R2 business context.

Health Innovation provides the business frame for considering changes in health-service and clinical practice. Its established evaluation child examines suitability, value and implications so that an innovation can be understood in the context in which it might be used. The model stops at that evaluative responsibility rather than presenting a complete pipeline from idea to operational adoption.

**Intent**

Make consideration of innovation informed by its prospective benefits, consequences and suitability.

**Boundary**

Evaluation does not establish an adoption decision, professional authority or an implementation programme.</documentation>
