            <folder name="II.1.2.9.2 [CT2] Research Information Support" id="id-d3719b7af77c44ae8016ff4bfbd196fd">
              <folder name="II.1.2.9.2.1 [CT3] Governed Research Information Provision" id="id-175a43642b47471293a8b9a17133ac3b">
                <documentation>Continuum navigation coordinate: II.1.2.9.2.1. Navigation asserts no semantic containment. Occurrence: architectural; no additional architectural instance or semantic relationship. Canonical element directory: canonicalId=6907401e6786470083c1d34a65aa225b; Exchange identifier=id-a9a4e74fe8bb55508e4a7b75ea333980. Existing governed hierarchy member; directory retained for leaves.</documentation>
                <element xsi:type="archimate:Capability" name="[CT3] Governed Research Information Provision" id="id-a9a4e74fe8bb55508e4a7b75ea333980">
                  <documentation>Provide existing health information for an authorised research purpose under applicable ethics, governance, privacy, consent, security and information-use constraints.

Governed Research Information Provision makes existing health information available for an authorised research purpose under its applicable constraints. It represents a substantive information contribution while keeping ethics, governance, consent, privacy, security and permitted use material to provision. The responsibility concerns supplying existing information legitimately, rather than running the research that uses it.

**Boundary**

Availability is not research authorisation. Trials, genomic analysis and research-governance responsibilities are not subsumed by this deliberately narrow capability.</documentation>
