              <documentation>Continuum navigation coordinate: II.1.2.9.2. Navigation asserts no semantic containment. Occurrence: architectural; no additional architectural instance or semantic relationship. Canonical element directory: canonicalId=ef18f999eef3488ba584d263a551732b; Exchange identifier=id-50b36409f6b55504a198330f760ef888. Existing governed hierarchy member; directory retained for leaves.</documentation>
              <element xsi:type="archimate:Capability" name="[CT2] Research Information Support" id="id-50b36409f6b55504a198330f760ef888">
                <documentation>Provide the existing health information needed for authorised research within the deliberately bounded R1/R2 responsibility.

Research Information Support represents the ability to make existing health information available for a legitimate research purpose. Its single established child concentrates on governed provision, preserving the constraints under which information can be used rather than treating technical availability as research permission. The narrow decomposition reflects R1/R2 sufficiency rather than a claim to encompass every form of research support.

**Intent**

Support authorised research with information supplied under the applicable ethical, privacy and governance conditions.

**Boundary**

Research governance, trial oversight and specialist analysis remain unmodelled and are not absorbed into provision.

## Qualified relationship assertions

Original source predicates, evidence and qualifications remain in the metadata. The ARB has now adjudicated their native treatment; explicitly unestablished relationship existence remains excluded. Native representation does not promote source standing.

| Source predicate | Target element | Source standing / currentness | ARB native treatment |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| enabled_by | [[CT2] Research Information Curation](4f5b8cec90324c2989cdc30e80bc8cb9.md) | Proposed / current | Serving (reverse) — `id-a1dc68d6cb2651ba875a1917e6cbe43d` |</documentation>
