                <property key="v0.2 / Source Locators" value="[{&quot;anchor&quot;:&quot;ct2--research-information-support&quot;,&quot;line&quot;:832,&quot;source&quot;:&quot;business&quot;,&quot;text&quot;:&quot;##### CT2 — Research Information Support&quot;},{&quot;anchor&quot;:&quot;ct2--research-information-support&quot;,&quot;line&quot;:834,&quot;source&quot;:&quot;business&quot;,&quot;text&quot;:&quot;**Tier and ancestry:** CT2; parent Health Research &amp; Innovation (CT1).&quot;},{&quot;anchor&quot;:&quot;ct2--research-information-support&quot;,&quot;line&quot;:836,&quot;source&quot;:&quot;business&quot;,&quot;text&quot;:&quot;**Definition:** Provide the existing health information needed for authorised research within the deliberately bounded R1/R2 responsibility.&quot;},{&quot;anchor&quot;:&quot;ct2--research-information-support&quot;,&quot;line&quot;:844,&quot;source&quot;:&quot;business&quot;,&quot;text&quot;:&quot;**Boundary:** This is deliberate under-decomposition, not a claim that information provision exhausts research support. Research Assessment and Governance, Research/Trials Oversight, clinical-trial management, genomic analysis and other specialist research abilities are intentionally unmodelled unless Harmonia requirements make them material. Their absence does not assign them to information provision.&quot;}]"/>
                <property key="v0.2 / Snapshot Record JSON" value="{&quot;ancestry_status&quot;:&quot;established&quot;,&quot;architectural_status&quot;:&quot;Canonical&quot;,&quot;baseline_description&quot;:{&quot;Boundary&quot;:&quot;Research governance, trial oversight and specialist analysis remain unmodelled and are not absorbed into provision.&quot;,&quot;Capability Overview&quot;:&quot;Research Information Support represents the ability to make existing health information available for a legitimate research purpose. Its single established child concentrates on governed provision, preserving the constraints under which information can be used rather than treating technical availability as research permission. The narrow decomposition reflects R1/R2 sufficiency rather than a claim to encompass every form of research support.&quot;,&quot;Intent&quot;:&quot;Support authorised research with information supplied under the applicable ethical, privacy and governance conditions.&quot;},&quot;baseline_placement&quot;:{&quot;canonical_id&quot;:&quot;CT1-HEALTH-RESEARCH-INNOVATION.CT2-RESEARCH-INFORMATION-SUPPORT&quot;,&quot;owner_key&quot;:null,&quot;parent_key&quot;:&quot;capability:health-research--innovation&quot;,&quot;tier&quot;:&quot;CT2&quot;},&quot;baseline_unresolved&quot;:[&quot;relevance&quot;],&quot;baseline_version&quot;:&quot;0.1&quot;,&quot;canonical_id&quot;:&quot;CT1-HEALTH-RESEARCH-INNOVATION.CT2-RESEARCH-INFORMATION-SUPPORT&quot;,&quot;canonical_name&quot;:&quot;Research Information Support&quot;,&quot;category&quot;:&quot;business&quot;,&quot;governed_definition_latex&quot;:&quot;\nProvide the existing health information needed for authorised research within the deliberately bounded R1/\\allowbreak{}R2 responsibility.\n\n&quot;,&quot;id_aliases&quot;:[],&quot;key&quot;:&quot;business-capability:research-information-support&quot;,&quot;latex_label&quot;:&quot;cap:bc-research-information-support&quot;,&quot;local_id&quot;:&quot;RESEARCH-INFORMATION-SUP