            <documentation>Continuum navigation coordinate: II.1.2.9. Navigation asserts no semantic containment. Occurrence: architectural; no additional architectural instance or semantic relationship. Historical predecessor: R.2.25 [CT1] Health Research &amp; Innovation; canonicalId=2cc31384c8864c73989025cbe96dcfa7; Exchange identifier=id-30c9efe556ad537e8bcf6af838d48792 Canonical element directory: canonicalId=582bf62145fd42118e5d57bb714841e8; Exchange identifier=id-aae6d53e02cf5c689376034a9078b6f9. Existing governed hierarchy member; directory retained for leaves.</documentation>
            <element xsi:type="archimate:Capability" name="[CT1] Health Research &amp; Innovation" id="id-aae6d53e02cf5c689376034a9078b6f9">
              <documentation>Provide existing health information for authorised research under applicable constraints and evaluate health innovation; deliberately under-decomposed for R1/R2.

This capability frames the deliberately bounded research and innovation responsibilities material to Harmonia's R1/R2 architecture. Research Information Support concerns provision of existing information for authorised research; Health Innovation concerns evaluation of proposed or emerging innovation. These establish useful enterprise context without implying a complete research organisation or innovation lifecycle.

**Intent**

Support legitimate research information needs and informed consideration of changes to health-service or clinical practice.

**Boundary**

Information provision does not own trials, ethics approval or specialist research analysis. Evaluating innovation does not authorise adoption or implementation.

**Harmonia Architectural Relevance**

Governed provision of existing information materially enables authorised research. Innovation evaluation has no separate platform assignment; the CT1 classification must not be inherited by each descendant.

## ARB identity continuity

Historical identity [2cc31384c8864c73989025cbe96dcfa7](2cc31384c8864c73989025cbe96dcfa7.md) has direct correspondence with this capability under HCRL 1.1.5-002. Historical provenance and UUID reservation remain with that record; this resource retains its existing identity and independent standing.</documentation>
