          <folder name="II.1.2.10 [CT1] Health Rights, Advocacy &amp; Participation" id="id-46ad600375264f22a8bd07b9b8fc6534">
            <documentation>Continuum navigation coordinate: II.1.2.10. Navigation asserts no semantic containment. Occurrence: architectural; no additional architectural instance or semantic relationship. Historical predecessor: R.2.26 [CT1] Health Rights, Advocacy &amp; Participation; canonicalId=58376e5c53bf4af0a54f99f21ac52666; Exchange identifier=id-236d2d03222355b7a740fe7a2a19ff22 Canonical element directory: canonicalId=7ab5c82a500b45f39267883a6e78c482; Exchange identifier=id-59fb57e93d695a5781569d5fb185fdc4. Existing governed hierarchy member; directory retained for leaves.</documentation>
            <element xsi:type="archimate:Capability" name="[CT1] Health Rights, Advocacy &amp; Participation" id="id-59fb57e93d695a5781569d5fb185fdc4">
              <documentation>Protecting patient rights, facilitating informed consent, managing advance care directives, supporting patient advocacy, and enabling consumer participation in health decisions.

This capability represents the organisation's responsibility to protect patients' rights and enable their voice in health decisions. Consent, advance care directives, advocacy and consumer participation concern the legitimacy and personal consequences of care, rather than merely the availability of clinical information. The governed model retains this broad enterprise responsibility without an established subordinate capability set.

**Intent**

Support informed participation and respect for the individual's rights in decisions affecting their health.

**Boundary**

Recording a directive or restricting access can support rights without performing advocacy or managing consumer participation.

**Harmonia Architectural Relevance**

The established Adjacent classification reflects the use and supply of consent and record-access evidence. It does not assign the underlying rights, advocacy or participation activity to Harmonia.

## ARB identity continuity

Historical identity [58376e5c53bf4af0a54f99f21ac52666](58376e5c53bf4af0a54f99f21ac52666.md) has direct correspondence with this capability under HCRL 1.1.5-002. Historical provenance and UUID reservation remain with that record; this resource retains its existing identity and independent standing.</documentation>
