              <folder name="II.1.2.11.1.1 [CT3] Assurance Conclusion Determination" id="id-02bb121598644835b6343480bd960bf7">
                <documentation>Continuum navigation coordinate: II.1.2.11.1.1. Navigation asserts no semantic containment. Occurrence: architectural; no additional architectural instance or semantic relationship. Canonical element directory: canonicalId=10f538feae4042829fafeae472882128; Exchange identifier=id-4a9821af9af35a649a2f169f370acbe9. Existing governed hierarchy member; directory retained for leaves.</documentation>
                <element xsi:type="archimate:Capability" name="[CT3] Assurance Conclusion Determination" id="id-4a9821af9af35a649a2f169f370acbe9">
                  <documentation>Establish the legitimately supported conclusion, including insufficiency, qualification and unresolved concerns where applicable.

Assurance Conclusion Determination establishes what confidence is legitimately supported by the assessment. It preserves qualifications and unresolved concerns rather than forcing incomplete evidence into a positive or negative result. Within Assurance Evaluation it is the responsibility that gives the conclusion its standing, distinct from gathering or assessing the supporting material.

**Boundary**

Insufficiency proves neither assurance nor non-assurance, and the conclusion does not manage the subject's operational response.</documentation>
