            <folder name="II.1.2.11.2 [CT2] Health Service Assurance Specification" id="id-8c90c63be4494cf4a64b1b7eb0f8a905">
              <folder name="II.1.2.11.2.1 [CT3] Assurance Approach Definition" id="id-b6d595327d434d52ac34d6c5e82908cb">
                <documentation>Continuum navigation coordinate: II.1.2.11.2.1. Navigation asserts no semantic containment. Occurrence: architectural; no additional architectural instance or semantic relationship. Canonical element directory: canonicalId=d672f8831df54f2099927f820d0025f5; Exchange identifier=id-a28516f387e951deb72e816ac780649e. Existing governed hierarchy member; directory retained for leaves.</documentation>
                <element xsi:type="archimate:Capability" name="[CT3] Assurance Approach Definition" id="id-a28516f387e951deb72e816ac780649e">
                  <documentation>Define scope, evidence expectations, responsibilities, methods, applicable degree of independence and timing/frequency for service-delivery assurance.

Assurance Approach Definition establishes how service-delivery assurance will be undertaken, including scope, evidence, methods, responsibilities, timing and required independence. It gives assurance activity a defensible approach rather than assuming any available observation can support confidence. The approach must respect applicable higher-level requirements when deciding what constitutes sufficient evaluation.

**Boundary**

Self-attestation cannot replace required independent governed assurance, and an approach does not itself establish a conclusion.</documentation>
