              <folder name="II.1.2.11.2.2 [CT3] Assurance Evaluation Criteria Governance" id="id-7f65825f02874cd48d1624dbda4af5d5">
                <documentation>Continuum navigation coordinate: II.1.2.11.2.2. Navigation asserts no semantic containment. Occurrence: architectural; no additional architectural instance or semantic relationship. Canonical element directory: canonicalId=f3e32f2a2c9d47a89eaf124647161522; Exchange identifier=id-55bc2c3a7c375e1baeb0284bd21b9724. Existing governed hierarchy member; directory retained for leaves.</documentation>
                <element xsi:type="archimate:Capability" name="[CT3] Assurance Evaluation Criteria Governance" id="id-55bc2c3a7c375e1baeb0284bd21b9724">
                  <documentation>Establish and maintain criteria against which sufficient assurance can be determined.

This capability establishes and maintains the criteria against which assurance sufficiency is judged. It makes the evaluative basis of confidence explicit across the different concerns that can affect service delivery. Criteria can draw on clinical, workforce, technology, information or other contexts without turning those subjects into independent assurance capability trees.

**Boundary**

Criteria governance is distinct from applying criteria to evidence and does not remap the existing assurance BEC responsibilities.</documentation>
