              <documentation>Continuum navigation coordinate: II.1.2.11.2. Navigation asserts no semantic containment. Occurrence: architectural; no additional architectural instance or semantic relationship. Canonical element directory: canonicalId=ec5c4d1219464433b2cee5c5a988fef7; Exchange identifier=id-fe48e4fa8a025194ad49cc197a83d502. Existing governed hierarchy member; directory retained for leaves.</documentation>
              <element xsi:type="archimate:Capability" name="[CT2] Health Service Assurance Specification" id="id-fe48e4fa8a025194ad49cc197a83d502">
                <documentation>Specify how macro-level service-delivery assurance will be undertaken and what sufficiently supports confidence.

This capability defines the approach and evaluation criteria through which service-delivery assurance can be justified. Approach Definition addresses scope, method, responsibility, evidence and applicable independence; Criteria Governance establishes the basis for judging sufficiency. Their separation distinguishes the design of an assurance activity from the normative or evaluative material it applies.

**Intent**

Make the intended basis of confidence explicit before a conclusion is treated as assurance.

**Boundary**

An approach cannot waive a higher-level independence requirement. Contributing specialist concerns do not create separate Business Assurance hierarchies.</documentation>
