              <folder name="II.1.2.12.1.2 [CT3] Health Service Financial Management" id="id-4497595498d44c39a547754f26b41b72">
                <documentation>Continuum navigation coordinate: II.1.2.12.1.2. Navigation asserts no semantic containment. Occurrence: architectural; no additional architectural instance or semantic relationship. Canonical element directory: canonicalId=2fbf31e974574f288f087179e4023dc2; Exchange identifier=id-d3b307ced1bb58bab5dc299f2bd63ffb. Existing governed hierarchy member; directory retained for leaves.</documentation>
                <element xsi:type="archimate:Capability" name="[CT3] Health Service Financial Management" id="id-d3b307ced1bb58bab5dc299f2bd63ffb">
                  <documentation>Establish the service’s fit within funding, financial and charging arrangements without absorbing enterprise finance/accounting.

Health Service Financial Management establishes how the service fits applicable funding, financial and charging arrangements. It connects service viability with its surrounding financial context without attempting to become the enterprise finance function. The responsibility is service-specific alignment rather than the production of all financial transactions associated with care.

**Boundary**

Financial fit does not confer pricing, accounting, billing or enterprise revenue-management authority.</documentation>
                  <property key="v0.2 / Source Capture Key" value="business-capability:health-service-financial-management"/>
                  <property key="v0.2 / Snapshot Reference ID" value="HCM-BC-health-service-financial-management"/>
                  <property key="v0.2 / LaTeX Label" value="cap:bc-health-service-financial-management"/>
