              <documentation>Continuum navigation coordinate: II.1.2.12.1. Navigation asserts no semantic containment. Occurrence: architectural; no additional architectural instance or semantic relationship. Canonical element directory: canonicalId=d4fc5367352741a99bd334f7e8bf5856; Exchange identifier=id-a72e1eab6d6551e0b387e09c0ce9897e. Existing governed hierarchy member; directory retained for leaves.</documentation>
              <element xsi:type="archimate:Capability" name="[CT2] Health Service Alignment" id="id-a72e1eab6d6551e0b387e09c0ce9897e">
                <documentation>Position the service coherently in its wider health-service ecosystem.

Health Service Alignment positions a service among the other services, resources and arrangements on which it depends. It considers reciprocal dependencies, required resources, financial fit and the organisational changes needed for introduction or material change. Where modelling asks what service is needed, alignment asks how it can fit coherently into its environment.

**Intent**

Expose the dependencies and surrounding commitments that affect service viability.

**Boundary**

Alignment does not establish the service offering, own the required resources or settle the unresolved ancestry of collective operational readiness.</documentation>
                <property key="v0.2 / Source Capture Key" value="business-capability:health-service-alignment"/>
                <property key="v0.2 / Snapshot Reference ID" value="HCM-BC-health-service-alignment"/>
