              <folder name="II.1.2.12.2.4 [CT3] Health Service Need Identification" id="id-45a89f7a14284d789352f8379a41eb80">
                <documentation>Continuum navigation coordinate: II.1.2.12.2.4. Navigation asserts no semantic containment. Occurrence: architectural; no additional architectural instance or semantic relationship. Canonical element directory: canonicalId=976c90e05d0e44b1b24c89bf61eac005; Exchange identifier=id-10df1dc1dfd455a981b3e7c5ccafdf4d. Existing governed hierarchy member; directory retained for leaves.</documentation>
                <element xsi:type="archimate:Capability" name="[CT3] Health Service Need Identification" id="id-10df1dc1dfd455a981b3e7c5ccafdf4d">
                  <documentation>Establish an unmet health-service need requiring response.

Health Service Need Identification establishes the unmet service need for which an organisational response is being considered. It gives service modelling a reason grounded in what is missing rather than beginning with a predetermined solution. That identified need can then frame the abilities and resources required without assuming that a new offering has already been established.

**Boundary**

Identifying need does not define an offering, approve funding or determine the surrounding implementation arrangements.</documentation>
