              <documentation>Continuum navigation coordinate: II.1.2.12.2. Navigation asserts no semantic containment. Occurrence: architectural; no additional architectural instance or semantic relationship. Canonical element directory: canonicalId=9a3e90db97b94d1888a2a5c5effb8999; Exchange identifier=id-51689808d64b561a8041fe1b48bf3b01. Existing governed hierarchy member; directory retained for leaves.</documentation>
              <element xsi:type="archimate:Capability" name="[CT2] Health Service Modelling" id="id-51689808d64b561a8041fe1b48bf3b01">
                <documentation>Establish what service should exist and what it needs to become viable.

Health Service Modelling establishes the service needed and the ordinary business abilities required to make it viable. Its children distinguish recognising unmet need, identifying required abilities, supporting establishment and evaluating an existing service for improvement. The model can therefore revisit service assumptions without treating the original definition as permanently sufficient.

**Intent**

Connect a service's purpose with the abilities and preparation required for it to exist usefully.

**Boundary**

Capability Identification uses ordinary business meaning; it does not allocate Harmonia capability tiers. Implementation support does not take over recruitment, facilities, procurement or ICT responsibilities.</documentation>
