              <documentation>Continuum navigation coordinate: II.1.2.13.1. Navigation asserts no semantic containment. Occurrence: architectural; no additional architectural instance or semantic relationship. Canonical element directory: canonicalId=02a52157967f4b498807cac70e3410e9; Exchange identifier=id-31c38c7c37fd5b19bf446b9937406be5. Existing governed hierarchy member; directory retained for leaves.</documentation>
              <element xsi:type="archimate:Capability" name="[CT2] Compliance Governance" id="id-31c38c7c37fd5b19bf446b9937406be5">
                <documentation>Define how adherence to the authoritative WHAT will be determined, checked and reported.

Compliance Governance defines how adherence to established obligations, authorities and constraints will be determined. Assessment Definition specifies the evidence and basis for evaluation; Reporting &amp; Checkpoint Definition specifies where adherence is checked and what must be communicated. This makes the compliance test explicit without treating the design of a test as its successful execution.

**Intent**

Provide a defensible basis for checking and reporting whether the governing envelope has been respected.

**Boundary**

Defining assessment arrangements does not perform assurance or manage the governed activity. The obligations being assessed retain their authoritative source.</documentation>
