            <folder name="II.1.2.13.2 [CT2] Governance Framework Management" id="id-036d06d5b8884eb582377d84c91815a8">
              <folder name="II.1.2.13.2.1 [CT3] Authority &amp; Constraint Governance" id="id-f98c2bb27e4b43bfa931594c8670a5c2">
                <documentation>Continuum navigation coordinate: II.1.2.13.2.1. Navigation asserts no semantic containment. Occurrence: architectural; no additional architectural instance or semantic relationship. Canonical element directory: canonicalId=ad7f41dc48a046b185f044f0a24517ca; Exchange identifier=id-306f2ee359b85d3cbbf914f1d9920f5a. Existing governed hierarchy member; directory retained for leaves.</documentation>
                <element xsi:type="archimate:Capability" name="[CT3] Authority &amp; Constraint Governance" id="id-306f2ee359b85d3cbbf914f1d9920f5a">
                  <documentation>Establish who may make, approve or govern organisational decisions/artefacts and the bounds within which authority may be exercised.

This capability establishes who may make or approve organisational decisions and the bounds within which that authority applies. It complements obligation governance by distinguishing required outcomes from legitimate decision powers. A participant can therefore be responsible for acting within constraints without being authorised to redefine the governing requirement.

**Boundary**

Authority allocation does not itself perform an operational decision or a runtime access-control evaluation.</documentation>
