              <folder name="II.1.2.13.2.2 [CT3] Policy / Obligation Governance" id="id-02a0da26954c40d1adafd3da58c18d0a">
                <documentation>Continuum navigation coordinate: II.1.2.13.2.2. Navigation asserts no semantic containment. Occurrence: architectural; no additional architectural instance or semantic relationship. Canonical element directory: canonicalId=73c6e5b36bdf4bf0ad2b8b50c9b9a00b; Exchange identifier=id-8d31da82f9965bebbef788d003e2e3d8. Existing governed hierarchy member; directory retained for leaves.</documentation>
                <element xsi:type="archimate:Capability" name="[CT3] Policy / Obligation Governance" id="id-8d31da82f9965bebbef788d003e2e3d8">
                  <documentation>Identify, interpret, establish and maintain authoritative legislative, regulatory, policy, standards, guideline, contractual and other obligations, attributable and traceable to source authority.

Policy / Obligation Governance establishes and maintains the authoritative requirements under which the organisation operates. It interprets applicable legislative, regulatory, contractual, policy and other sources while preserving traceability to their authority. The purpose is a legitimate account of what must be satisfied, rather than an operational choice about how to satisfy it.

**Boundary**

Interpreting obligations does not acquire the regulator's authority or determine operational means.</documentation>
