              <documentation>Continuum navigation coordinate: II.1.2.13.2. Navigation asserts no semantic containment. Occurrence: architectural; no additional architectural instance or semantic relationship. Canonical element directory: canonicalId=b39f53b3ffb441f388a89b45cc517deb; Exchange identifier=id-cb87b0ba8417587ebc94321210dbc9cf. Existing governed hierarchy member; directory retained for leaves.</documentation>
              <element xsi:type="archimate:Capability" name="[CT2] Governance Framework Management" id="id-cb87b0ba8417587ebc94321210dbc9cf">
                <documentation>Establish the authoritative WHAT and legitimate working parameters.

Governance Framework Management establishes what must be satisfied and the legitimate authority and bounds for organisational decisions. Its two children separate obligations attributable to source authority from the allocation and limitation of decision authority. Together they supply the authoritative reference against which operational arrangements and compliance assessments can be considered.

**Intent**

Keep required outcomes and legitimate decision parameters distinguishable and traceable to their authority.

**Boundary**

Interpreting an external obligation or engaging with a regulator does not transfer that body's authority. Operational means remain with management.</documentation>
