              <documentation>Continuum navigation coordinate: II.1.2.14.3. Navigation asserts no semantic containment. Occurrence: architectural; no additional architectural instance or semantic relationship. Historical predecessor: R.2.37 [CT2] Individual Care Planning; canonicalId=574e61e230e643f78c58649adb4db313; Exchange identifier=id-ed8ad37da4e05146ad1598281861e454 Canonical element directory: canonicalId=f036a9866459429a8fb5f5e10727b5e8; Exchange identifier=id-e24ae17857c6529cb63c0c8d736ca5e7. Existing governed hierarchy member; directory retained for leaves.</documentation>
              <element xsi:type="archimate:Capability" name="[CT2] Individual Care Planning" id="id-e24ae17857c6529cb63c0c8d736ca5e7">
                <documentation>The capability to establish the intended clinical response to an individual's assessed and clinically interpreted health state, including the objectives, interventions and monitoring required to progress their care.

Individual Care Planning establishes the intended course of care in response to assessed and clinically interpreted health information. It connects clinical understanding to objectives, intended interventions and monitoring needs. Its outcome is an expression of what should happen, allowing intended care to remain distinguishable from requests, operational arrangements and actions subsequently performed.

**Intent**

Make the clinical response and its objectives explicit enough to guide care and later evaluate its effectiveness.

**Boundary**

Prescribing can express clinical intent without establishing dispensing or administration. Scheduling or allocating resources does not perform the planned intervention. No CT3 decomposition is established.

## Qualified relationship assertions

