              <folder name="II.1.2.14.4.2 [CT3] Care Effectiveness Review" id="id-2d3c64f943d64d22b0f4518666c3962e">
                <documentation>Continuum navigation coordinate: II.1.2.14.4.2. Navigation asserts no semantic containment. Occurrence: architectural; no additional architectural instance or semantic relationship. Historical predecessor: R.2.38 [CT3] Care Effectiveness Review; canonicalId=31f49cdea9f44f188459503580c2b86e; Exchange identifier=id-961ab14e4a355e7c9033ac9d149a198a Canonical element directory: canonicalId=79cfeaefeb174a54ba43343d37f035c1; Exchange identifier=id-ad157f6fab0a5a8f94826cbe973f4946. Existing governed hierarchy member; directory retained for leaves.</documentation>
                <element xsi:type="archimate:Capability" name="[CT3] Care Effectiveness Review" id="id-ad157f6fab0a5a8f94826cbe973f4946">
                  <documentation>Evaluate whether delivered care is achieving or has achieved its intended goals and outcomes.

Care Effectiveness Review evaluates delivered care against its intended goals and outcomes. It connects observed response to the reason the care was undertaken, making a judgement that monitoring alone does not supply. An effectiveness finding can inform review of appropriateness while preserving the possibility that a reasonable care choice has not achieved its objective.

**Boundary**

Observed improvement is not automatically proof that the intended objectives have been achieved or that continuing care is appropriate.

