                <documentation>Continuum navigation coordinate: II.1.2.14.5.1. Navigation asserts no semantic containment. Occurrence: architectural; no additional architectural instance or semantic relationship. Historical predecessor: R.2.41 [CT3] Clinical Examination; canonicalId=8bc15e2b8f114deebcbbe3f2013a8147; Exchange identifier=id-7f4dfd1742555c729739020b88325e4d Canonical element directory: canonicalId=8855d4d9e2954e0ab66ab65a556fc61a; Exchange identifier=id-abe9e3230f6d5577a13fca453e624a85. Existing governed hierarchy member; directory retained for leaves.</documentation>
                <element xsi:type="archimate:Capability" name="[CT3] Clinical Examination" id="id-abe9e3230f6d5577a13fca453e624a85">
                  <documentation>Establish health findings through clinical examination.

Clinical Examination establishes findings through examination of the individual. It distinguishes directly acquired clinical knowledge from the historical account and the measurement-focused contribution of its assessment siblings. Its outcome is a set of examination findings that can inform clinical interpretation, irrespective of the setting or profession exercising the ability.

**Boundary**

An examination finding is not itself a diagnosis, care plan or performed treatment.

