              <folder name="II.1.2.14.5.2 [CT3] Health History Assessment" id="id-2c0f918eab744a19842ffbb7860ad514">
                <documentation>Continuum navigation coordinate: II.1.2.14.5.2. Navigation asserts no semantic containment. Occurrence: architectural; no additional architectural instance or semantic relationship. Historical predecessor: R.2.42 [CT3] Health History Assessment; canonicalId=bcaacf446f45443eafd8e21a1fd74ee1; Exchange identifier=id-cbafdc119f6a513bb3fea09f88339fbe Canonical element directory: canonicalId=7ea7e3f74e2940a7934b588a1a038834; Exchange identifier=id-b003aaadcd6059e6b6ee2c683437017a. Existing governed hierarchy member; directory retained for leaves.</documentation>
                <element xsi:type="archimate:Capability" name="[CT3] Health History Assessment" id="id-b003aaadcd6059e6b6ee2c683437017a">
                  <documentation>Establish relevant health knowledge from the individual’s history and applicable historical/contextual information.

Health History Assessment establishes clinically relevant understanding from a person's history and its surrounding context. Within assessment it contributes knowledge that a current examination or measurement alone may not reveal, while requiring consideration of the relevance of historical information to the present situation. Access to previous records can assist, but the responsibility is the assessment of history rather than retrieval itself.

**Boundary**

Historical information does not become a current clinical conclusion merely because it is available; interpretation of the assessed findings remains Clinical Determination.

