              <folder name="II.1.2.14.5.3 [CT3] Health Status Measurement" id="id-b57ae0032e7c44f2a4e75801d1e5f2fa">
                <documentation>Continuum navigation coordinate: II.1.2.14.5.3. Navigation asserts no semantic containment. Occurrence: architectural; no additional architectural instance or semantic relationship. Historical predecessor: R.2.43 [CT3] Health Status Measurement; canonicalId=3717906f7f8840d3a8a3e3877543dd18; Exchange identifier=id-ecc73fa3f4385a05adc08b66033b1ade Canonical element directory: canonicalId=a796bfb3335d44f6aeb9970628ed8554; Exchange identifier=id-697b75a82c515e48b6ba8de37109dc7f. Existing governed hierarchy member; directory retained for leaves.</documentation>
                <element xsi:type="archimate:Capability" name="[CT3] Health Status Measurement" id="id-697b75a82c515e48b6ba8de37109dc7f">
                  <documentation>Establish individual health observations or measurements.

Health Status Measurement establishes observations or measurements of an individual's health. Its contribution to assessment is evidence about the measured state, with a purpose distinct from developing a view over time or deciding the clinical meaning of a result. Measurements can inform both present assessment and later monitoring without collapsing those abilities.

**Boundary**

Obtaining a value does not establish a temporal trend or the clinical significance of that value.

## ARB identity continuity

