                <documentation>Continuum navigation coordinate: II.1.2.14.6.1. Navigation asserts no semantic containment. Occurrence: architectural; no additional architectural instance or semantic relationship. Historical predecessor: R.2.45 [CT3] Care Response Monitoring; canonicalId=615f93d05fbb4a8481f07778bd4f4803; Exchange identifier=id-a4b1b25b3893529195ccb230921de502 Canonical element directory: canonicalId=d6951c9357fa40a4943cde581d95d5b1; Exchange identifier=id-e24ada9f97a351f09911b66311963637. Existing governed hierarchy member; directory retained for leaves.</documentation>
                <element xsi:type="archimate:Capability" name="[CT3] Care Response Monitoring" id="id-e24ada9f97a351f09911b66311963637">
                  <documentation>Scope that health-state view to a particular problem/condition and the treatment applied to it.

Care Response Monitoring considers the monitored health-state view in relation to a particular problem or condition and the treatment applied. It makes a response trajectory visible in its treatment context, helping distinguish a general change in health from a change relevant to the care being followed. It consumes the aggregate view established through Health State Monitoring.

**Boundary**

Identifying the response does not judge treatment effectiveness against objectives or determine a replacement treatment.

