              <documentation>Continuum navigation coordinate: II.1.2.14.6. Navigation asserts no semantic containment. Occurrence: architectural; no additional architectural instance or semantic relationship. Historical predecessor: R.2.47 [CT2] Individual Health Monitoring; canonicalId=31e7c27556314cafb74d040441d2dac6; Exchange identifier=id-67610b928dbe5690a2f089ecddd9963d Canonical element directory: canonicalId=c7d0e498e1ad44138df940af2f91cd2d; Exchange identifier=id-30d731a19ab6526386b64c335fe3f7fd. Existing governed hierarchy member; directory retained for leaves.</documentation>
              <element xsi:type="archimate:Capability" name="[CT2] Individual Health Monitoring" id="id-30d731a19ab6526386b64c335fe3f7fd">
                <documentation>The capability to observe and evaluate an individual's health state over time in order to identify clinically meaningful change, stability or deviation from an expected state or trajectory.

Monitoring develops a view of an individual's health over time so that change, stability or deviation can be recognised. Health State Monitoring establishes the aggregate temporally situated view; Care Response Monitoring considers that view in relation to a particular condition and treatment. Together they distinguish observation over time from a single measurement and from the clinical judgement prompted by a trend.

**Intent**

Make relevant trajectories visible while preserving what was observed and what still requires interpretation.

**Boundary**

Monitoring does not establish the clinical significance of a change or judge whether care achieved its objectives. Those responsibilities remain Clinical Determination and Individual Care Review respectively.

## Qualified relationship assertions

Original source predicates, evidence and qualifications remain in the metadata. The ARB has now adjudicated their native treatment; explicitly unestablished relationship existence remains excluded. Native representation does not promote source standing.

