          <folder name="II.1.2.15 [CT1] Population Health &amp; Health-System Planning" id="id-05a5d0ab337d4bec9aee4b6f85139180">
            <folder name="II.1.2.15.1 [CT2] Health-System Planning" id="id-0d92d483c54e400ab5cf01e6a6421f7a">
              <folder name="II.1.2.15.1.1 [CT3] Health Service Capacity Planning" id="id-1eeeb31308be4c2ea7817b3bbb47c3c4">
                <documentation>Continuum navigation coordinate: II.1.2.15.1.1. Navigation asserts no semantic containment. Occurrence: architectural; no additional architectural instance or semantic relationship. Canonical element directory: canonicalId=c1d1db0e2c854077a41721615e86119d; Exchange identifier=id-d1b5e21ef6a250eebd417930385e18f9. Existing governed hierarchy member; directory retained for leaves.</documentation>
                <element xsi:type="archimate:Capability" name="[CT3] Health Service Capacity Planning" id="id-d1b5e21ef6a250eebd417930385e18f9">
                  <documentation>Determine required strategic/tactical capacity to address assessed demand.

Health Service Capacity Planning determines the strategic or tactical capacity required to address assessed demand. It considers what should be available, preserving a distinction between requirement and the resources currently in service. Within Health-System Planning it gives demand a capacity response without performing operational allocation.

**Boundary**

Planned capacity is neither established resource availability nor the service's currently usable operational capacity.</documentation>
