              <folder name="II.1.2.15.1.3 [CT3] Health Service Distribution Planning" id="id-5fba2bc8e77344b687a25de5fa85d03a">
                <documentation>Continuum navigation coordinate: II.1.2.15.1.3. Navigation asserts no semantic containment. Occurrence: architectural; no additional architectural instance or semantic relationship. Canonical element directory: canonicalId=4fc525fccbe142a58ee43dcc58b11c92; Exchange identifier=id-f1cc8c768d9c5f1f87a6fb97c0e2a9b8. Existing governed hierarchy member; directory retained for leaves.</documentation>
                <element xsi:type="archimate:Capability" name="[CT3] Health Service Distribution Planning" id="id-f1cc8c768d9c5f1f87a6fb97c0e2a9b8">
                  <documentation>Determine the distribution of planned capacity across a geographical, organisational, site or service-network footprint.

Health Service Distribution Planning determines how planned capacity should be distributed across a geographical, organisational or service-network footprint. It addresses the placement of the planned response rather than only its aggregate scale. This allows the planning context to distinguish enough total capacity from capacity positioned where it is needed.

**Boundary**

A planned footprint does not establish recognised location records, identifiable offerings or actual resource deployment.</documentation>
