            <folder name="II.1.2.15.2 [CT2] Population Health Surveillance" id="id-fc2216a56bba4d6dabfef472e5824c1c">
              <folder name="II.1.2.15.2.1 [CT3] Notifiable Health Event Management" id="id-39f74d6ee992486596d056551e2982f2">
                <documentation>Continuum navigation coordinate: II.1.2.15.2.1. Navigation asserts no semantic containment. Occurrence: architectural; no additional architectural instance or semantic relationship. Canonical element directory: canonicalId=e605436254ed4dad819f452448e054a1; Exchange identifier=id-d43ba8c16bb956f2a856c80fed59e5c5. Existing governed hierarchy member; directory retained for leaves.</documentation>
                <element xsi:type="archimate:Capability" name="[CT3] Notifiable Health Event Management" id="id-d43ba8c16bb956f2a856c80fed59e5c5">
                  <documentation>Manage formal notification applicability, required information, recipient, status, submission, correction/supplementation and applicable follow-up.

Notifiable Health Event Management addresses the formal communication responsibilities applicable to a health event. It manages applicability, required information, recipient and submission status, including correction or supplementation where relevant. Its purpose is to make the notification obligation and its discharge distinguishable from both event identification and ordinary reporting.

**Boundary**

Notification management does not define the governing obligation or own the operational response to the event.</documentation>
