              <folder name="II.1.2.15.2.2 [CT3] Population Health Event Identification" id="id-08956d651f5a4336a2aefeb049452d4b">
                <documentation>Continuum navigation coordinate: II.1.2.15.2.2. Navigation asserts no semantic containment. Occurrence: architectural; no additional architectural instance or semantic relationship. Canonical element directory: canonicalId=e084ba370bb545d0a4c28c37e2e8e850; Exchange identifier=id-62f15df98fda5574a39e62b40dea0e22. Existing governed hierarchy member; directory retained for leaves.</documentation>
                <element xsi:type="archimate:Capability" name="[CT3] Population Health Event Identification" id="id-62f15df98fda5574a39e62b40dea0e22">
                  <documentation>Identify and characterise significant population-health events/patterns from applicable evidence.

Population Health Event Identification recognises and characterises a significant event or pattern from relevant evidence. It establishes the population-level concern rather than merely noting that observations changed. The resulting event context can inform notification or response decisions while retaining a separate responsibility for those decisions.

**Boundary**

An identified event is not automatically notifiable, and notifiability does not demonstrate that an obligation was discharged.</documentation>
