            <folder name="II.1.2.16.2 [CT2] Digital Identity &amp; Access Governance" id="id-dac0ee0d7fb34484bdca50759556f298">
              <folder name="II.1.2.16.2.1 [CT3] Access Control Assurance &amp; Reporting" id="id-03101cfe310f47269ef618cd46335e8e">
                <documentation>Continuum navigation coordinate: II.1.2.16.2.1. Navigation asserts no semantic containment. Occurrence: architectural; no additional architectural instance or semantic relationship. Canonical element directory: canonicalId=ba0bf23c2b5b4de1bdfbc5df90f57a2f; Exchange identifier=id-de17cc6571dc50e688259ca76c68c889. Existing governed hierarchy member; directory retained for leaves.</documentation>
                <element xsi:type="archimate:Capability" name="[CT3] Access Control Assurance &amp; Reporting" id="id-de17cc6571dc50e688259ca76c68c889">
                  <documentation>Establish organisational assurance/evidence of whether access-control arrangements are appropriately established and operating.

This capability establishes organisational evidence and assurance about whether access-control arrangements are appropriately established and operating. It makes control effectiveness a distinct concern from defining requirements or performing an individual enforcement action. Reporting communicates that established position without making an isolated successful check proof of end-to-end control.

**Boundary**

Subject-specific access-control assurance does not create another macro-level Health Service Assurance hierarchy.</documentation>
