              <folder name="II.1.2.16.2.2 [CT3] Access Control Collaboration" id="id-ed0ca6d67dab4cc991e8658019163ef3">
                <documentation>Continuum navigation coordinate: II.1.2.16.2.2. Navigation asserts no semantic containment. Occurrence: architectural; no additional architectural instance or semantic relationship. Canonical element directory: canonicalId=c1a39b83d27a4a148f997c0a709e82ac; Exchange identifier=id-8cdf0ba785ed5e63b1330b61fb25a7c2. Existing governed hierarchy member; directory retained for leaves.</documentation>
                <element xsi:type="archimate:Capability" name="[CT3] Access Control Collaboration" id="id-8cdf0ba785ed5e63b1330b61fb25a7c2">
                  <documentation>Coordinate arrangements across independently controlled domains/parties while retaining their control ownership.

Access Control Collaboration coordinates arrangements across parties or domains that retain independent control ownership. Its purpose is coherent cross-boundary control where a strong local arrangement alone cannot establish the whole result. Collaboration therefore concerns agreed control participation rather than silently centralising every participant's authority.

**Boundary**

Coordination does not transfer the parties' control ownership or guarantee identity quality across domains.</documentation>
