              <folder name="II.1.2.16.2.3 [CT3] Access Control Context Management" id="id-a68c9a366bb944a2b357ad683d6b7a56">
                <documentation>Continuum navigation coordinate: II.1.2.16.2.3. Navigation asserts no semantic containment. Occurrence: architectural; no additional architectural instance or semantic relationship. Canonical element directory: canonicalId=a51f7a8045d24d0f982320025ba3a6ae; Exchange identifier=id-ee4c4efdc81e5e7e99fb2d2d72895339. Existing governed hierarchy member; directory retained for leaves.</documentation>
                <element xsi:type="archimate:Capability" name="[CT3] Access Control Context Management" id="id-ee4c4efdc81e5e7e99fb2d2d72895339">
                  <documentation>Determine what information, functions, activities or other concerns require control, under what circumstances and how requirements are modelled.

Access Control Context Management establishes what requires control, the circumstances in which control applies and how those requirements are modelled. It gives access governance an explicit subject and context rather than reducing it to assembling runtime attributes. The responsibility can encompass information, functions and activities under physical, procedural or digital arrangements.

**Boundary**

Defining control context does not itself enforce the controls or establish that they operate effectively.</documentation>
                  <property key="v0.2 / Source Capture Key" value="business-capability:access-control-context-management"/>
                  <property key="v0.2 / Snapshot Reference ID" value="HCM-BC-access-control-context-management"/>
                  <property key="v0.2 / LaTeX Label" value="cap:bc-access-control-context-management"/>
                  <property key="v0.2 / Construct Type" value="capability"/>
                  <property key="v0.2 / Capability Tier" value="CT3"/>
                  <property key="v0.2 / Architectural Status" value="Canonical"/>
