              <folder name="II.1.2.16.2.6 [CT3] Identity Identification &amp; Authentication" id="id-46afd2bf72f7426eb7c9bd94823180df">
                <documentation>Continuum navigation coordinate: II.1.2.16.2.6. Navigation asserts no semantic containment. Occurrence: architectural; no additional architectural instance or semantic relationship. Canonical element directory: canonicalId=ba4ad62548984d63ad75da3561566431; Exchange identifier=id-b85ddc19dd4f5d808a7c7c0343f7ad86. Existing governed hierarchy member; directory retained for leaves.</documentation>
                <element xsi:type="archimate:Capability" name="[CT3] Identity Identification &amp; Authentication" id="id-b85ddc19dd4f5d808a7c7c0343f7ad86">
                  <documentation>Identify an actor and authenticate the asserted identity.

This capability identifies the acting participant and authenticates the asserted identity. It establishes who is acting under the applicable identity arrangements so that later control and accountability can be grounded in an identified actor. The outcome remains distinct from confidence established through identity evidence and from authority to access a controlled concern.

**Boundary**

Authentication neither establishes every required identity-quality condition nor authorises the requested activity.</documentation>
                  <property key="v0.2 / Source Capture Key" value="business-capability:identity-identification--authentication"/>
                  <property key="v0.2 / Snapshot Reference ID" value="HCM-BC-identity-identification-authentication"/>
