              <folder name="II.1.2.16.2.7 [CT3] Identity Modelling &amp; Interoperability" id="id-c1b276ee2eb54521af5f0fa0fc15eeaf">
                <documentation>Continuum navigation coordinate: II.1.2.16.2.7. Navigation asserts no semantic containment. Occurrence: architectural; no additional architectural instance or semantic relationship. Canonical element directory: canonicalId=c40a00b0fe56405d99b6bb6ede72e18e; Exchange identifier=id-d58022670433565e85886b12893bd691. Existing governed hierarchy member; directory retained for leaves.</documentation>
                <element xsi:type="archimate:Capability" name="[CT3] Identity Modelling &amp; Interoperability" id="id-d58022670433565e85886b12893bd691">
                  <documentation>Establish identity models and interoperability arrangements appropriate to organisational identity use.

This capability establishes identity models and arrangements through which identities can be understood across organisational use. It addresses the coherence needed when parties exchange or rely on identity information without assuming that their identity assertions have identical quality. Its purpose is meaningful interoperability, rather than a particular federation or Single Sign-On technology.

**Boundary**

Interoperability does not guarantee assurance quality or transfer each party's control ownership.</documentation>
