              <folder name="II.1.2.16.2.8 [CT3] Identity Qualification Control" id="id-69ea1a634d7c423ba48f4090d47f92eb">
                <documentation>Continuum navigation coordinate: II.1.2.16.2.8. Navigation asserts no semantic containment. Occurrence: architectural; no additional architectural instance or semantic relationship. Canonical element directory: canonicalId=3d53064f2fb7475b8f49fb58ec8ad4a5; Exchange identifier=id-c0a2dee48aae56eaaf4266358083da80. Existing governed hierarchy member; directory retained for leaves.</documentation>
                <element xsi:type="archimate:Capability" name="[CT3] Identity Qualification Control" id="id-c0a2dee48aae56eaaf4266358083da80">
                  <documentation>Determine whether presented identity characteristics, provenance and assurance quality are sufficient for its intended context.

Identity Qualification Control evaluates whether presented identity characteristics, provenance and assurance are sufficient for the intended context. It adds a contextual judgement beyond whether the actor can be authenticated. This permits an identity adequate for one purpose to remain insufficient for another without claiming that the identity is necessarily false.

**Boundary**

Identity qualification does not establish practitioner clinical qualification or a general permission to act.</documentation>
