              <folder name="II.1.2.16.3.1 [CT3] Health Information Access Monitoring" id="id-cdc11273d06d4f2fa204956118714a71">
                <documentation>Continuum navigation coordinate: II.1.2.16.3.1. Navigation asserts no semantic containment. Occurrence: architectural; no additional architectural instance or semantic relationship. Canonical element directory: canonicalId=01854c7311404bbf9f698fce4656b54d; Exchange identifier=id-08d64c8f005f5276b8bc96386f66dd19. Existing governed hierarchy member; directory retained for leaves.</documentation>
                <element xsi:type="archimate:Capability" name="[CT3] Health Information Access Monitoring" id="id-08d64c8f005f5276b8bc96386f66dd19">
                  <documentation>Evaluate actual organisational access/handling practice, including controls, accessibility, compartments, classification and physical/printed handling.

Health Information Access Monitoring evaluates actual access and handling practice across organisational circumstances. Digital audit information can contribute, but so can physical access, printed handling, compartments and classification practice. Its purpose is to understand what is happening in use rather than merely observe software events or assume configured controls describe reality.

**Boundary**

Evidence supply does not transfer business accountability, and observation is not automatically independent assurance.</documentation>
