              <folder name="II.1.2.16.3.2 [CT3] Health Information Classification Assurance" id="id-b4bf017c73454733a9d8556e57240a5d">
                <documentation>Continuum navigation coordinate: II.1.2.16.3.2. Navigation asserts no semantic containment. Occurrence: architectural; no additional architectural instance or semantic relationship. Canonical element directory: canonicalId=4a4a871081bf45829eab2a93c9d1c21f; Exchange identifier=id-98514bc9e1a85cc6a7cd787246610874. Existing governed hierarchy member; directory retained for leaves.</documentation>
                <element xsi:type="archimate:Capability" name="[CT3] Health Information Classification Assurance" id="id-98514bc9e1a85cc6a7cd787246610874">
                  <documentation>Assure appropriate classification according to sensitivity and potential consequences of exposure/mishandling.

This capability evaluates whether classification is appropriate to information sensitivity and the consequences of exposure or mishandling. It examines the application of classification rather than merely the presence of a label. The responsibility supports protection decisions while retaining the distinction between the classification basis and the control applied to a particular request.

**Boundary**

Classification assurance does not define compartment membership or grant permission to access classified information.</documentation>
