              <folder name="II.1.2.16.3.5 [CT3] Health Privacy Safeguard Management" id="id-65f29847285648ee95f1499005d009f1">
                <documentation>Continuum navigation coordinate: II.1.2.16.3.5. Navigation asserts no semantic containment. Occurrence: architectural; no additional architectural instance or semantic relationship. Canonical element directory: canonicalId=089cd8744ed6410388daeff463507fc1; Exchange identifier=id-1068c50d6b1e5f39954ada6935bea433. Existing governed hierarchy member; directory retained for leaves.</documentation>
                <element xsi:type="archimate:Capability" name="[CT3] Health Privacy Safeguard Management" id="id-1068c50d6b1e5f39954ada6935bea433">
                  <documentation>Establish organisational safeguards and assurance processes concerning privacy consequences of information supply, exposure or use.

This capability establishes safeguards and assurance arrangements concerning the privacy consequences of supplying, exposing or using information. It focuses on the effect on people and legitimate information use, distinguishing that concern from protection of the information estate itself. Technical access restrictions may contribute without exhausting the organisational privacy responsibility.

**Boundary**

Privacy safeguards do not replace broader estate resilience, access decisions or originating consent authority.</documentation>
