              <documentation>Continuum navigation coordinate: II.1.2.16.3. Navigation asserts no semantic containment. Occurrence: architectural; no additional architectural instance or semantic relationship. Canonical element directory: canonicalId=4ae0de8fa16840d09ab2ef3f5545a5e7; Exchange identifier=id-c9d1ebe2bd675841a70e6e3c1bb5a1d7. Existing governed hierarchy member; directory retained for leaves.</documentation>
              <element xsi:type="archimate:Capability" name="[CT2] Health Information Protection" id="id-c9d1ebe2bd675841a70e6e3c1bb5a1d7">
                <documentation>Govern privacy consequences and adequate protection of the information estate and its environment.

Health Information Protection governs the consequences of information exposure and the safeguards protecting information and its operating environment. Privacy safeguards, estate protection, access-practice monitoring, compartment assurance and classification assurance address different questions. Together they distinguish appropriate arrangements from evidence of how information is actually handled, including physical and printed handling.

**Intent**

Protect information and the people affected by its use, with an intelligible basis for evaluating protective arrangements.

**Boundary**

Compartment assurance does not decide access. Subject-specific protection assurance does not create additional macro-level Health Service Assurance trees.</documentation>
