          <folder name="II.1.2.17 [CT1] Standards, Semantics &amp; Reference Governance" id="id-accb89327012406a83c46d749dd7a710">
            <folder name="II.1.2.17.1 [CT2] Clinical Semantics Governance" id="id-b294b35e921543deacc2a18fc42094af">
              <folder name="II.1.2.17.1.1 [CT3] Classification Governance" id="id-8d25bdd394954ca8946209154a6854da">
                <documentation>Continuum navigation coordinate: II.1.2.17.1.1. Navigation asserts no semantic containment. Occurrence: architectural; no additional architectural instance or semantic relationship. Canonical element directory: canonicalId=4520ce37454e4de68580d75fdb08efe6; Exchange identifier=id-941e7bf5a59d53f38732a2dcbab6f79e. Existing governed hierarchy member; directory retained for leaves.</documentation>
                <element xsi:type="archimate:Capability" name="[CT3] Classification Governance" id="id-941e7bf5a59d53f38732a2dcbab6f79e">
                  <documentation>Govern applicable classification definitions and their organisational standing.

Classification Governance establishes the definitions and organisational standing of applicable classifications. In this governed context, classification concerns sensitivity and the consequences of exposure or mishandling, rather than the clinical meaning supplied by terminology. Its outcome supplies a basis for consistent application and protection considerations.

**Boundary**

Classification is orthogonal to contextual compartment membership and does not by itself determine an access decision.</documentation>
