              <folder name="II.1.2.17.1.3 [CT3] Semantic Mapping Governance" id="id-0e82392be249431e97b0181b91cf4608">
                <documentation>Continuum navigation coordinate: II.1.2.17.1.3. Navigation asserts no semantic containment. Occurrence: architectural; no additional architectural instance or semantic relationship. Canonical element directory: canonicalId=17dc6ab9f4394049a5327415d19628f2; Exchange identifier=id-570b32e283fd550887828703316f6fb9. Existing governed hierarchy member; directory retained for leaves.</documentation>
                <element xsi:type="archimate:Capability" name="[CT3] Semantic Mapping Governance" id="id-570b32e283fd550887828703316f6fb9">
                  <documentation>Govern mappings between applicable semantic artefacts without collapsing their source meanings or authorities.

Semantic Mapping Governance maintains mappings between applicable semantic artefacts while preserving the meaning and authority of each side. Its purpose is intelligible correspondence rather than assumed equivalence. A governed mapping can support exchange or interpretation without suggesting that the mapped artefacts have become the same concept or share one authority.

**Boundary**

A mapping does not erase source distinctions or give a consuming system authority to redefine either source.</documentation>
