              <folder name="II.1.2.17.1.4 [CT3] Terminology Governance" id="id-4f87ffbd696d4fd0a2397b200d9956a0">
                <documentation>Continuum navigation coordinate: II.1.2.17.1.4. Navigation asserts no semantic containment. Occurrence: architectural; no additional architectural instance or semantic relationship. Canonical element directory: canonicalId=e926a47881fa482088859f59fa6fe7e4; Exchange identifier=id-3eb94251dfaa56ca8f5d1988bec36b1c. Existing governed hierarchy member; directory retained for leaves.</documentation>
                <element xsi:type="archimate:Capability" name="[CT3] Terminology Governance" id="id-3eb94251dfaa56ca8f5d1988bec36b1c">
                  <documentation>Manage governed terminology/reference-set lifecycle and standing, including acceptance, release, update, supersession/retirement and authority/provider coordination.

Terminology Governance maintains the lifecycle and standing of terminology and reference sets used by the organisation. Acceptance, release, updates and retirement require coordination with the appropriate authority or provider so that a code's meaning is not treated as timeless or locally self-defined. This supplies a governed semantic basis for information bindings and knowledge associations.

**Boundary**

Governing terminology differs from binding a structure to it or overseeing its actual use.</documentation>
                  <property key="v0.2 / Source Capture Key" value="business-capability:terminology-governance"/>
