              <folder name="II.1.2.17.1.6 [CT3] Terminology Utilisation Oversight" id="id-ddc171e906e04589a2030429a96753e4">
                <documentation>Continuum navigation coordinate: II.1.2.17.1.6. Navigation asserts no semantic containment. Occurrence: architectural; no additional architectural instance or semantic relationship. Canonical element directory: canonicalId=4ca436cd90b745daa290b067c57a0450; Exchange identifier=id-b6de79dfa55b538c93287ca1a74034ac. Existing governed hierarchy member; directory retained for leaves.</documentation>
                <element xsi:type="archimate:Capability" name="[CT3] Terminology Utilisation Oversight" id="id-b6de79dfa55b538c93287ca1a74034ac">
                  <documentation>Oversee actual terminology/reference-set use and identify inappropriate, inconsistent or drifting usage.

Terminology Utilisation Oversight considers how terminology and reference sets are actually used. It identifies inappropriate application, inconsistency or semantic drift that the existence of an approved terminology does not prevent. Its purpose is to preserve coherent use without making each consuming capability the owner of terminology meaning.

**Boundary**

Use oversight does not redefine terminology or automatically authorise a local semantic variation.</documentation>
