              <folder name="II.1.2.17.2.2 [CT3] Information Model Compliance" id="id-5b7b4987f4ae44a0b4ada127d3929ecc">
                <documentation>Continuum navigation coordinate: II.1.2.17.2.2. Navigation asserts no semantic containment. Occurrence: architectural; no additional architectural instance or semantic relationship. Canonical element directory: canonicalId=160db14dbe5149db91223a93f6ee9102; Exchange identifier=id-c0e0f14c28af58bd82aabe9069cff26c. Existing governed hierarchy member; directory retained for leaves.</documentation>
                <element xsi:type="archimate:Capability" name="[CT3] Information Model Compliance" id="id-c0e0f14c28af58bd82aabe9069cff26c">
                  <documentation>Address organisational conformity to applicable information-model requirements.

Information Model Compliance addresses conformity to applicable model requirements. It makes actual organisational use accountable to the adopted semantic frame rather than treating model availability or user education as proof of conformity. Within standards governance it concerns the requirements for use, not the separate task of discovering or adopting models.

**Boundary**

Conformity does not redefine the model or absorb governance oversight of the wider adoption arrangements.</documentation>
