              <folder name="II.1.2.17.2.3 [CT3] Information Model Discovery" id="id-4e64e2eef4184057b491f84331785bbd">
                <documentation>Continuum navigation coordinate: II.1.2.17.2.3. Navigation asserts no semantic containment. Occurrence: architectural; no additional architectural instance or semantic relationship. Canonical element directory: canonicalId=f33dc5b8ba9643329bb7b9431e1f9a6f; Exchange identifier=id-4d9ce431849e5c9ea87fc5e7798bba22. Existing governed hierarchy member; directory retained for leaves.</documentation>
                <element xsi:type="archimate:Capability" name="[CT3] Information Model Discovery" id="id-4d9ce431849e5c9ea87fc5e7798bba22">
                  <documentation>Identify information models relevant to the organisation’s health-information needs.

Information Model Discovery identifies candidate models relevant to the organisation's health-information needs. It supports informed standards governance by making applicable possibilities visible before adoption. Its business purpose is finding suitable semantic frames rather than selecting a software representation or assuming every discovered model should be used.

**Boundary**

Discovery does not adopt a model, establish compliance or grant it organisational authority.</documentation>
