                <documentation>Continuum navigation coordinate: II.1.2.18.1.1. Navigation asserts no semantic containment. Occurrence: architectural; no additional architectural instance or semantic relationship. Canonical element directory: canonicalId=36d5bf4c19d34172b72f4b77099ff235; Exchange identifier=id-6939d843cca65044b94dbd9e33db979f. Existing governed hierarchy member; directory retained for leaves.</documentation>
                <element xsi:type="archimate:Capability" name="[CT3] Practitioner Engagement &amp; Privilege Management" id="id-6939d843cca65044b94dbd9e33db979f">
                  <documentation>Manage practitioners as service participants, their roles/capacities, applicable privileges and qualification context above ordinary HR employment administration.

This capability manages how practitioners participate in services and the privileges applicable to that participation. It connects professional standing with roles and permitted capacities in the service context, beyond ordinary employment administration. Separating engagement and privilege from qualification makes it possible to recognise a qualified practitioner who is not authorised for a particular service activity.

**Boundary**

Representation or consumption of privilege information does not transfer the underlying workforce decision authority to Harmonia.</documentation>
