              <folder name="II.1.2.18.1.3 [CT3] Workforce Service Coverage Management" id="id-a5f76aed40d149ebbb7e01b91a0a7ce1">
                <documentation>Continuum navigation coordinate: II.1.2.18.1.3. Navigation asserts no semantic containment. Occurrence: architectural; no additional architectural instance or semantic relationship. Canonical element directory: canonicalId=cfb04e13895745619171a3e8f15d349c; Exchange identifier=id-74d8c7e477725fdfbf88fada3bbf80d1. Existing governed hierarchy member; directory retained for leaves.</documentation>
                <element xsi:type="archimate:Capability" name="[CT3] Workforce Service Coverage Management" id="id-74d8c7e477725fdfbf88fada3bbf80d1">
                  <documentation>Observe whether required enterprise work/service obligations can be fulfilled, identify coverage gaps/risks and adjust coverage in response.

Workforce Service Coverage Management considers whether required enterprise work and service obligations can be fulfilled and how coverage should change when gaps or risks arise. Its concern is the adequacy of coverage, broader than the existence of a roster. This supplies a service-wide workforce view distinct from deploying a person to a particular care requirement.

**Boundary**

Coverage management is not individual support-work progression or automatic authority to assign clinical work.</documentation>
