            <folder name="II.1.2.18.2 [CT2] Healthcare Organisation &amp; Service Structure Management" id="id-af113812bde646af9f39ccd487ddcda1">
              <folder name="II.1.2.18.2.1 [CT3] Healthcare Location Definition Management" id="id-9397175dfb9342818d636dc2137e1235">
                <documentation>Continuum navigation coordinate: II.1.2.18.2.1. Navigation asserts no semantic containment. Occurrence: architectural; no additional architectural instance or semantic relationship. Canonical element directory: canonicalId=d77a5c8f1818465c98125acc4bc2ac81; Exchange identifier=id-c202cbbd5a9a5759bcd79a6c933da7a2. Existing governed hierarchy member; directory retained for leaves.</documentation>
                <element xsi:type="archimate:Capability" name="[CT3] Healthcare Location Definition Management" id="id-c202cbbd5a9a5759bcd79a6c933da7a2">
                  <documentation>Establish and manage recognised locations and their applicable business characteristics and relationships.

Healthcare Location Definition Management establishes recognised places and their business characteristics and relationships. It gives health-service activity an intelligible location context while remaining separate from maintaining the physical facilities. A defined location can be referenced in offerings and operational activity without implying that it is currently usable or ready for care.

**Boundary**

Location definition is not facilities operation, care-place readiness or service availability.</documentation>
