                  <property key="v0.2 / Source Locators" value="[{&quot;anchor&quot;:&quot;ct2--healthcare-organisation--service-structure-management&quot;,&quot;line&quot;:943,&quot;source&quot;:&quot;business&quot;,&quot;text&quot;:&quot;| Healthcare Location Definition Management | Establish and manage recognised locations and their applicable business characteristics and relationships. |&quot;},{&quot;anchor&quot;:&quot;ct2--healthcare-organisation--service-structure-management&quot;,&quot;line&quot;:938,&quot;source&quot;:&quot;business&quot;,&quot;text&quot;:&quot;**Decomposition assertion:** Each named child in this table is a CT3 Business Capability whose immediate CT2 parent is Healthcare Organisation &amp; Service Structure Management; that CT2 has the CT1 parent stated above.&quot;},{&quot;anchor&quot;:&quot;ct2--healthcare-organisation--service-structure-management&quot;,&quot;line&quot;:946,&quot;source&quot;:&quot;business&quot;,&quot;text&quot;:&quot;**Boundary:** Location definition is distinct from Facilities Management. Service exists ≠ offered here ≠ available at this time/context. Temporal/conditional availability is material: a walk-in offering may operate 06:00–22:00 while another pathway covers other hours. Offering availability does not establish collective operational readiness; OI-BC-002 remains unplaced. Organisation, location and practitioner associations do not substitute for material Healthcare Service context.&quot;}]"/>
