              <folder name="II.1.2.18.2.2 [CT3] Healthcare Organisation Identity &amp; Structure Management" id="id-c0f8235b550c4ab9847bbce43efe01c3">
                <documentation>Continuum navigation coordinate: II.1.2.18.2.2. Navigation asserts no semantic containment. Occurrence: architectural; no additional architectural instance or semantic relationship. Canonical element directory: canonicalId=4684348b4d144e61aa7dd203facfebdd; Exchange identifier=id-27d9f6f7925550e4974fd5cc00a6a523. Existing governed hierarchy member; directory retained for leaves.</documentation>
                <element xsi:type="archimate:Capability" name="[CT3] Healthcare Organisation Identity &amp; Structure Management" id="id-27d9f6f7925550e4974fd5cc00a6a523">
                  <documentation>Establish and manage identity and structural relationships of participating organisations and organisational units.

This capability establishes the identity and structural relationships of participating organisations and organisational units. It provides the business account of who the participants are and how they relate, which directory representations can then convey. The distinction matters because a represented hierarchy should not create organisational authority merely through document or interface nesting.

**Boundary**

Organisation identity does not substitute for location, practitioner or material Healthcare Service context.</documentation>
