              <folder name="II.1.2.18.2.3 [CT3] Healthcare Service Offering Management" id="id-6d6b3e7b9e054d13b24c9685b17fcd3b">
                <documentation>Continuum navigation coordinate: II.1.2.18.2.3. Navigation asserts no semantic containment. Occurrence: architectural; no additional architectural instance or semantic relationship. Canonical element directory: canonicalId=9fe177e4422b4853acb1dd0d0b74c4ba; Exchange identifier=id-02ef028b3b425b1c82aea9f84d2b6631. Existing governed hierarchy member; directory retained for leaves.</documentation>
                <element xsi:type="archimate:Capability" name="[CT3] Healthcare Service Offering Management" id="id-02ef028b3b425b1c82aea9f84d2b6631">
                  <documentation>Establish/manage what identifiable service is offered, by whom, where, when and under which availability conditions/constraints.

This capability establishes the identifiable service offered, including provider, place, timing and availability conditions. It makes a service discoverable as an offering rather than merely an abstract service idea. Temporal and conditional availability are material: an offering may exist but be unavailable in the present context, and another pathway may cover different hours.

**Boundary**

An available offering does not establish collective readiness to deliver it; organisation and location alone do not supply the service context.</documentation>
