            <folder name="II.1.3.1.4 [CT2] Care Fulfilment Administration Enablement [superseded]" id="id-1e86d035c3a84394a6f861a895095c36">
              <documentation>Continuum navigation coordinate: II.1.3.1.4. Navigation asserts no semantic containment. Occurrence: architectural; no additional architectural instance or semantic relationship. Canonical element directory: canonicalId=9f0f4379c1954524ba5e691d0c7d95ab; Exchange identifier=id-0ac4ff89dcdc5e7c951d67f06c504dd8. Existing governed hierarchy member; directory retained for leaves.</documentation>
              <element xsi:type="archimate:Capability" name="[CT2] Care Fulfilment Administration Enablement" id="id-0ac4ff89dcdc5e7c951d67f06c504dd8">
                <documentation>Maintain distinguishable care-episode, bounded fulfilment and delivered-activity information across performing systems.

**Overview**

Maintain distinguishable care-episode, bounded fulfilment and delivered-activity information across performing systems. Its constituent abilities distinguish Episode &amp; Encounter Administration; Order Administration; Diagnostic Administration; Medication Administration; Procedure Administration.

**Intent**

Maintain the link between a bounded care request, the relevant episode and the externally observed fulfilment outcome.

**Boundary**

Encounter progression, order outcome, diagnostic interpretation, medication events and procedure documentation retain different source authorities.</documentation>
