                <element xsi:type="archimate:Capability" name="[CT3] Care Plan Lifecycle &amp; Coordination" id="id-ab0baa5289245368afb3d9943f0dee5c">
                  <documentation>Administer received care plans, goals, revisions and cross-participant coordination while retaining clinical planning authority at its source.

**Overview**

Administer received care plans, goals, revisions and cross-participant coordination while retaining clinical planning authority at its source. The reviewed hierarchy assigns this enduring ability to its stated business-enabling context.

**Intent**

Administer received care plans, goals, revisions and cross-participant coordination while retaining clinical planning authority at its source.

**Boundary**

Information administration and coordination preserve the authority of the responsible source, clinical actor and governed domain; they confer no additional real-world management authority.

## ARB identity continuity

Historical identity [689bb3f8a24249b79f787e1f48eb268d](689bb3f8a24249b79f787e1f48eb268d.md) has direct correspondence with this capability under HCRL 1.1.5-002. Historical provenance and UUID reservation remain with that record; this resource retains its existing identity and independent standing.</documentation>
