                <folder name="II.1.3.1.11.1.2 [Feature] Acute Clinical State Event Capture" id="id-16171981cefd4bc38e58ca38322b429a">
                  <documentation>Continuum navigation coordinate: II.1.3.1.11.1.2. Navigation asserts no semantic containment. Occurrence: architectural; no additional architectural instance or semantic relationship. Canonical element directory: canonicalId=566f6934c9b04627b0876f91bedd8f30; Exchange identifier=id-ac6154860e0d561e83acf8b1bbb85fda. Existing governed hierarchy member; directory retained for leaves.</documentation>
                  <element xsi:type="archimate:Capability" name="[Feature] Acute Clinical State Event Capture" id="id-ac6154860e0d561e83acf8b1bbb85fda" profiles="id-1fcc283b6cc74eab958ce9580eacd631">
                    <documentation>Ingest clinical deterioration notifications and acute clinical status updates.

Acute-state capture records deterioration notifications and current clinical status as externally established information. Approved reusable clinical-information composition is sufficient for this responsibility; routing a critical-result alert does not become a specialised capture Function merely because both concern urgent care.</documentation>
