                <folder name="II.1.3.1.11.2.1 [Feature] Encounter Bed/Location Association" id="id-7a46c255a2b042448eceac6f52c5cba0">
                  <documentation>Continuum navigation coordinate: II.1.3.1.11.2.1. Navigation asserts no semantic containment. Occurrence: architectural; no additional architectural instance or semantic relationship. Canonical element directory: canonicalId=47f0fca36aa4454eae95f4b151c7076f; Exchange identifier=id-21972725cd225097acead1b4571b1a95. Existing governed hierarchy member; directory retained for leaves.</documentation>
                  <element xsi:type="archimate:Capability" name="[Feature] Encounter Bed/Location Association" id="id-21972725cd225097acead1b4571b1a95" profiles="id-1fcc283b6cc74eab958ce9580eacd631">
                    <documentation>Dynamically maintain the association between an encounter, care team, and physical bed or ward location.

Encounter association keeps the relevant place and care-team context aligned with the episode as the patient moves. Location changes are meaningful operational facts, but they do not themselves establish a transfer of clinical responsibility.</documentation>
