                <folder name="II.1.3.1.11.2.2 [Feature] Encounter Context Creation" id="id-c6e2cc48efdf414e8798a692e0f0ef00">
                  <documentation>Continuum navigation coordinate: II.1.3.1.11.2.2. Navigation asserts no semantic containment. Occurrence: architectural; no additional architectural instance or semantic relationship. Canonical element directory: canonicalId=817f1046d7e84699a2e2050b84285f95; Exchange identifier=id-4390e66b343d556f8649e5367a3502c7. Existing governed hierarchy member; directory retained for leaves.</documentation>
                  <element xsi:type="archimate:Capability" name="[Feature] Encounter Context Creation" id="id-4390e66b343d556f8649e5367a3502c7" profiles="id-1fcc283b6cc74eab958ce9580eacd631">
                    <documentation>Create and maintain authoritative encounter tracking contexts for hospital admissions, outpatient visits, and community contacts.

Encounter context creation supplies an identifiable frame for information concerning a particular admission, visit or contact. Its governed tracking authority concerns the encounter representation within Harmonia; it does not make Harmonia the originator of every clinical fact associated with that encounter.</documentation>
