                <folder name="II.1.3.1.11.2.3 [Feature] Encounter History Retrieval" id="id-30f48022061b4ed5bd13232271669bb4">
                  <documentation>Continuum navigation coordinate: II.1.3.1.11.2.3. Navigation asserts no semantic containment. Occurrence: architectural; no additional architectural instance or semantic relationship. Canonical element directory: canonicalId=4088e1408f554143a0f1469efd1b43a7; Exchange identifier=id-9240e1a4cc6f53c4b6f1b8d0b36a96db. Existing governed hierarchy member; directory retained for leaves.</documentation>
                  <element xsi:type="archimate:Capability" name="[Feature] Encounter History Retrieval" id="id-9240e1a4cc6f53c4b6f1b8d0b36a96db" profiles="id-1fcc283b6cc74eab958ce9580eacd631">
                    <documentation>Expose qualified episode, movement and encounter-history context.

**Overview**

Consumers need to interpret prior care-place and episode relationships, not just the latest encounter state; historical retrieval remains bounded by source attribution and access policy.

**Boundary**

A historical view does not retrospectively alter clinical events or acquire longitudinal-record ownership.</documentation>
