                <folder name="II.1.3.1.11.2.4 [Feature] Encounter State Progression" id="id-074995f8c55a492cac64f5cfa9b5726e">
                  <documentation>Continuum navigation coordinate: II.1.3.1.11.2.4. Navigation asserts no semantic containment. Occurrence: architectural; no additional architectural instance or semantic relationship. Canonical element directory: canonicalId=c049039bf57e4e4aa97aab5967196383; Exchange identifier=id-26d1c6dd72ab5d6198424ef2ad44a966. Existing governed hierarchy member; directory retained for leaves.</documentation>
                  <element xsi:type="archimate:Capability" name="[Feature] Encounter State Progression" id="id-26d1c6dd72ab5d6198424ef2ad44a966" profiles="id-1fcc283b6cc74eab958ce9580eacd631">
                    <documentation>Track encounter status transitions (PLANNED → ARRIVED → IN_PROGRESS → ON_LEAVE → DISCHARGED).

Encounter progression preserves the difference between planned, arrived, active, leave and discharged circumstances. These states make administrative activity interpretable without implying a clinical outcome. The source's ON_LEAVE transition detail remains incomplete in the corresponding Process and is not repaired here.</documentation>
                    <property key="v0.2 / Source Capture Key" value="feature:encounter-state-progression"/>
                    <property key="v0.2 / Snapshot Reference ID" value="FEAT-SA-09"/>
