            <folder name="II.1.3.1.12 [CT2] Funding &amp; Coverage Administration" id="id-0d583f320d9c4ebcbcecc87bfc212757">
              <documentation>Continuum navigation coordinate: II.1.3.1.12. Navigation asserts no semantic containment. Occurrence: architectural; no additional architectural instance or semantic relationship. Historical predecessor: R.2.62 [CT2] Funding &amp; Coverage Administration; canonicalId=58beafcbcd084331be710eb00d27f6cf; Exchange identifier=id-24f0d184ab385eb9a2fa8d8bc39ec06e Canonical element directory: canonicalId=640432d413cf47928ea2b3d221f92313; Exchange identifier=id-c2df74422094583c85e83601696f971f. Existing governed hierarchy member; directory retained for leaves.</documentation>
              <element xsi:type="archimate:Capability" name="[CT2] Funding &amp; Coverage Administration" id="id-c2df74422094583c85e83601696f971f">
                <documentation>Funding &amp; Coverage Administration represents externally supplied insurance coverage and eligibility flags needed as care context. It allows those administrative conditions to be available without implying that Harmonia determines entitlements. The established Adjacent standing and absence of Features bound the current responsibility to this information contribution.

**Overview**

Funding &amp; Coverage Administration represents externally supplied insurance coverage and eligibility flags needed as care context. It allows those administrative conditions to be available without implying that Harmonia determines entitlements. The established Adjacent standing and absence of Features bound the current responsibility to this information contribution.

**Intent**

Funding &amp; Coverage Administration represents externally supplied insurance coverage and eligibility flags needed as care context. It allows those administrative conditions to be available without implying that Harmonia determines entitlements. The established Adjacent standing and absence of Features bound the current responsibility to this information contribution.

**Boundary**

Information administration does not confer authority over the represented person, organisation, service, place, device or clinical activity.

---

## History

### Boundary — predecessor explanation

Coverage information is not claims adjudication, funding governance or a universal determination of care eligibility.

### Harmonia Architectural Relevance — predecessor explanation

Harmonia consumes the administrative context; it does not acquire the payer's authority or manage the underlying coverage arrangement.

## ARB identity continuity

Historical identity [58beafcbcd084331be710eb00d27f6cf](58beafcbcd084331be710eb00d27f6cf.md) has direct correspondence with this capability under HCRL 1.1.5-002. Historical provenance and UUID reservation remain with that record; this resource retains its existing identity and independent standing.</documentation>
