                <folder name="II.1.3.1.14.1.3 [Feature] Order Destination Resolution &amp; Routing" id="id-41b767f89c634e008f3ffa6356d3c47e">
                  <documentation>Continuum navigation coordinate: II.1.3.1.14.1.3. Navigation asserts no semantic containment. Occurrence: architectural; no additional architectural instance or semantic relationship. Canonical element directory: canonicalId=9f8f1542efc64e89ad226689291f2635; Exchange identifier=id-287eedd7878756b69cfff8e1b3783f6b. Existing governed hierarchy member; directory retained for leaves.</documentation>
                  <element xsi:type="archimate:Capability" name="[Feature] Order Destination Resolution &amp; Routing" id="id-287eedd7878756b69cfff8e1b3783f6b" profiles="id-1fcc283b6cc74eab958ce9580eacd631">
                    <documentation>Resolve fulfillment endpoints and reliably route orders to performing service systems.

Destination resolution connects an order with the service endpoint intended to fulfil it. Routing advances the request towards that destination without proving execution or changing the original clinical intent simply because a transport route was chosen.</documentation>
                    <property key="v0.2 / Source Capture Key" value="feature:order-destination-resolution--routing"/>
                    <property key="v0.2 / Snapshot Reference ID" value="FEAT-SA-12"/>
