                <folder name="II.1.3.1.14.1.5 [Feature] Order Request Ingestion" id="id-f7bda9c277434fdbbe1de9671be2c8c8">
                  <documentation>Continuum navigation coordinate: II.1.3.1.14.1.5. Navigation asserts no semantic containment. Occurrence: architectural; no additional architectural instance or semantic relationship. Canonical element directory: canonicalId=fc1f8168fd6949beb810e4ff57a2368e; Exchange identifier=id-54db6777e733549186d5ff73117ae94e. Existing governed hierarchy member; directory retained for leaves.</documentation>
                  <element xsi:type="archimate:Capability" name="[Feature] Order Request Ingestion" id="id-54db6777e733549186d5ff73117ae94e" profiles="id-1fcc283b6cc74eab958ce9580eacd631">
                    <documentation>Ingest clinical diagnostic, medication, and procedure order requests with validated ordering clinician context.

Order ingestion establishes the received bounded fulfilment request with its ordering-clinician context. It begins the information account needed for a closed loop while leaving the performing service's business acceptance and execution distinguishable from technical ingress acceptance.</documentation>
                    <property key="v0.2 / Source Capture Key" value="feature:order-request-ingestion"/>
                    <property key="v0.2 / Snapshot Reference ID" value="FEAT-SA-11"/>
