                <folder name="II.1.3.1.15.1.1 [Feature] Procedural Documentation Ingestion" id="id-18021b585929482abf2d74830fe80303">
                  <documentation>Continuum navigation coordinate: II.1.3.1.15.1.1. Navigation asserts no semantic containment. Occurrence: architectural; no additional architectural instance or semantic relationship. Canonical element directory: canonicalId=324aefc4578f4cae934101ae5ad74ff8; Exchange identifier=id-b2a05065d92758159716890b3d1a785c. Existing governed hierarchy member; directory retained for leaves.</documentation>
                  <element xsi:type="archimate:Capability" name="[Feature] Procedural Documentation Ingestion" id="id-b2a05065d92758159716890b3d1a785c" profiles="id-1fcc283b6cc74eab958ce9580eacd631">
                    <documentation>Ingest operative reports, anesthesia records, and post-procedure summaries.

Procedural documentation ingestion preserves the operative, anaesthetic and post-procedure account supplied by the clinical service. It connects performed-care documentation with the wider record without giving the integration process authority to originate or judge the clinical findings.</documentation>
                    <property key="v0.2 / Source Capture Key" value="feature:procedural-documentation-ingestion"/>
