                <folder name="II.1.3.1.16.1.1 [Feature] Referral Destination Coordination" id="id-0403d0ea085f438eaab1efa94e386c18">
                  <documentation>Continuum navigation coordinate: II.1.3.1.16.1.1. Navigation asserts no semantic containment. Occurrence: architectural; no additional architectural instance or semantic relationship. Canonical element directory: canonicalId=7d7ddffcda9d4854a02be5c3265ad775; Exchange identifier=id-d977b0b1376453b9ba66d44eb556c0e9. Existing governed hierarchy member; directory retained for leaves.</documentation>
                  <element xsi:type="archimate:Capability" name="[Feature] Referral Destination Coordination" id="id-d977b0b1376453b9ba66d44eb556c0e9" profiles="id-1fcc283b6cc74eab958ce9580eacd631">
                    <documentation>Coordinate qualified referral destination resolution and convey the request under its applicable disposition contract.

**Overview**

Referral intake and status capture leave a distinct routing responsibility: finding the intended service and preserving redirection without turning technical delivery into assumed care responsibility.

**Boundary**

Does not make clinical triage decisions or infer Transfer of Care from acceptance.</documentation>
