                <folder name="II.1.3.1.16.1.2 [Feature] Referral Document Ingestion" id="id-ccb9d6db329f4ca993b7ced0dd1db0e0">
                  <documentation>Continuum navigation coordinate: II.1.3.1.16.1.2. Navigation asserts no semantic containment. Occurrence: architectural; no additional architectural instance or semantic relationship. Canonical element directory: canonicalId=1d1c5f8e8ca1498fb68dba601a7079dc; Exchange identifier=id-e028948e45e9556e9ae39992ba4ae05f. Existing governed hierarchy member; directory retained for leaves.</documentation>
                  <element xsi:type="archimate:Capability" name="[Feature] Referral Document Ingestion" id="id-e028948e45e9556e9ae39992ba4ae05f" profiles="id-1fcc283b6cc74eab958ce9580eacd631">
                    <documentation>Ingest structured clinical referral messages across integration boundaries.

Referral ingestion establishes the received referral material within the integration boundary. It preserves the request for another participant's involvement without treating successful receipt as clinical acceptance, responsibility assumption or a promise that care will be delivered.</documentation>
