                <folder name="II.1.3.1.16.1.4 [Feature] Referral Supporting Information" id="id-86877899b4554205a0f67c595567adfb">
                  <documentation>Continuum navigation coordinate: II.1.3.1.16.1.4. Navigation asserts no semantic containment. Occurrence: architectural; no additional architectural instance or semantic relationship. Canonical element directory: canonicalId=c8a50c0e932847d7b7d0289101aacd98; Exchange identifier=id-41682f56954051209563bf1a3b4af863. Existing governed hierarchy member; directory retained for leaves.</documentation>
                  <element xsi:type="archimate:Capability" name="[Feature] Referral Supporting Information" id="id-41682f56954051209563bf1a3b4af863" profiles="id-1fcc283b6cc74eab958ce9580eacd631">
                    <documentation>Collate and associate supporting clinical documentation, diagnostic history, and patient context with referral requests.

Supporting information gives the referral its relevant history and clinical context. Association makes the material available for the recipient's consideration while preserving source provenance and the distinction between evidence supplied and the recipient's own clinical decision.</documentation>
                    <property key="v0.2 / Source Capture Key" value="feature:referral-supporting-information"/>
