            <element xsi:type="archimate:Capability" name="[CT1] Care Context Integration Enablement" id="id-994a0770b7fd5726a603f696f3dc4d1c">
              <documentation>Compose governed information and coordination behaviour for materially different care settings, continuity arrangements and specialist clinical purposes.

**Overview**

Emergency presentation, inpatient rounds and outreach visits need different contextual assemblies of the same underlying information. This frame retains those established setting-specific responsibilities as compositions rather than duplicate records or clinical execution authorities.

**Intent**

Give a care participant the appropriate information context for the particular integration purpose without duplicating general information responsibilities.

**Boundary**

Setting, care mode and specialty are overlapping contextual dimensions. These children are integration responsibilities, not a mutually exclusive taxonomy of patients or clinical care.</documentation>
