              <element xsi:type="archimate:Capability" name="[CT2] Acute Care" id="id-36aa4edb4b1557c7bb8fde88fa158486">
                <documentation>Identify and track the operational and infrastructure dependencies necessary for acute care services to function, retaining each dependency provider's responsibility.

**Overview**

Identify and track the operational and infrastructure dependencies necessary for acute care services to function, retaining each dependency provider's responsibility. The reviewed hierarchy assigns this enduring ability to its stated business-enabling context.

**Intent**

Identify and track the operational and infrastructure dependencies necessary for acute care services to function, retaining each dependency provider's responsibility.

**Boundary**

Information administration and coordination preserve the authority of the responsible source, clinical actor and governed domain; they confer no additional real-world management authority.

## ARB identity continuity

Historical identity [7b591957f7424424abc80f699e9f1960](7b591957f7424424abc80f699e9f1960.md) has direct correspondence with this capability under HCRL 1.1.5-002. Historical provenance and UUID reservation remain with that record; this resource retains its existing identity and independent standing.</documentation>
