                  <documentation>Continuum navigation coordinate: II.1.3.4.1.1.1. Navigation asserts no semantic containment. Occurrence: architectural; no additional architectural instance or semantic relationship. Canonical element directory: canonicalId=1c18e7c2ccf640c9afc2525503b505a6; Exchange identifier=id-94fde1c6f231504a8363a1b0e0a957da. Existing governed hierarchy member; directory retained for leaves.</documentation>
                  <element xsi:type="archimate:Capability" name="[Feature] Confidentiality Flag Enforcement" id="id-94fde1c6f231504a8363a1b0e0a957da" profiles="id-1fcc283b6cc74eab958ce9580eacd631">
                    <documentation>Enforce restricted access flags (e.g., VIP, sensitive diagnosis, restricted record) across query and presentation interfaces.

Confidentiality enforcement makes a restricted-record condition effective across discovery and presentation paths. Its purpose is consistent governed treatment of sensitive information, rather than a flag displayed in one interface while other paths disclose the same content without restriction.</documentation>
