              <folder name="II.1.3.4.1.4 [CT3] Person Identity Administration" id="id-98c9eb8737e747f8a5004ea676cc4e72">
                <folder name="II.1.3.4.1.4.1 [Feature] Cross-Authority Identifier Correlation" id="id-28f9448792ef4268b7ed4c38505c70ca">
                  <documentation>Continuum navigation coordinate: II.1.3.4.1.4.1. Navigation asserts no semantic containment. Occurrence: architectural; no additional architectural instance or semantic relationship. Canonical element directory: canonicalId=6d74d143c7454fa0bf30743ddf7ba094; Exchange identifier=id-d9272acdc675539cb441d2db9c5ad6e6. Existing governed hierarchy member; directory retained for leaves.</documentation>
                  <element xsi:type="archimate:Capability" name="[Feature] Cross-Authority Identifier Correlation" id="id-d9272acdc675539cb441d2db9c5ad6e6" profiles="id-1fcc283b6cc74eab958ce9580eacd631">
                    <documentation>Correlate disparate local identifiers (e.g., hospital MRN, clinic client ID, national IHI) belonging to the same individual.

Cross-authority correlation preserves the association between identifiers used for one person by different participants. It enables information to be related across regional systems without erasing the separate identifier namespaces or claiming that Harmonia originated the identity decision.</documentation>
                    <property key="v0.2 / Source Capture Key" value="feature:cross-authority-identifier-correlation"/>
                    <property key="v0.2 / Snapshot Reference ID" value="FEAT-EM-02"/>
