                <folder name="II.1.3.4.1.4.2 [Feature] Governed Identity Correction" id="id-b91bdf76024e4b348fc37243b6af74fe">
                  <documentation>Continuum navigation coordinate: II.1.3.4.1.4.2. Navigation asserts no semantic containment. Occurrence: architectural; no additional architectural instance or semantic relationship. Canonical element directory: canonicalId=f7ab7a24e8234129b2ab02e9abd4fba2; Exchange identifier=id-6f0bfe5e814c5734a7c530f2b7515666. Existing governed hierarchy member; directory retained for leaves.</documentation>
                  <element xsi:type="archimate:Capability" name="[Feature] Governed Identity Correction" id="id-6f0bfe5e814c5734a7c530f2b7515666" profiles="id-1fcc283b6cc74eab958ce9580eacd631">
                    <documentation>Apply administrative identity updates, linked-record corrections, and split/merge notifications propagated from authoritative sources.

Governed correction applies externally authoritative identity updates and their consequences to Harmonia-managed associations. Administrative review concerns the legitimate application of the source outcome; it does not grant Harmonia an EMPI merge engine or authority to select a golden person record.</documentation>
                    <property key="v0.2 / Source Capture Key" value="feature:governed-identity-correction"/>
