                <folder name="II.1.3.4.1.4.4 [Feature] Identifier Resolution" id="id-e3b30fd4e01a4429ab106cbcec83efe8">
                  <documentation>Continuum navigation coordinate: II.1.3.4.1.4.4. Navigation asserts no semantic containment. Occurrence: architectural; no additional architectural instance or semantic relationship. Canonical element directory: canonicalId=ae034169e1394ccdb3a2ce9651eaf305; Exchange identifier=id-f1e1928516765880955f638a7fec8c35. Existing governed hierarchy member; directory retained for leaves.</documentation>
                  <element xsi:type="archimate:Capability" name="[Feature] Identifier Resolution" id="id-f1e1928516765880955f638a7fec8c35" profiles="id-1fcc283b6cc74eab958ce9580eacd631">
                    <documentation>Ingest and resolve external identifiers against registered issuing authorities and namespace systems.

Identifier Resolution interprets an identifier in its issuing-authority and namespace context, so that the same local value is not assumed to identify the same person everywhere. It provides an identifiable subject reference without deciding an authoritative master-person match.</documentation>
