                <folder name="II.1.3.4.1.4.5 [Feature] Identity Alias Association" id="id-94301742f4b24290b42eec2584d695be">
                  <documentation>Continuum navigation coordinate: II.1.3.4.1.4.5. Navigation asserts no semantic containment. Occurrence: architectural; no additional architectural instance or semantic relationship. Canonical element directory: canonicalId=97721dbd017e4c2daa73e1e87a8499b9; Exchange identifier=id-28d7815137a05a2aab6d1684011dbbde. Existing governed hierarchy member; directory retained for leaves.</documentation>
                  <element xsi:type="archimate:Capability" name="[Feature] Identity Alias Association" id="id-28d7815137a05a2aab6d1684011dbbde" profiles="id-1fcc283b6cc74eab958ce9580eacd631">
                    <documentation>Maintain explicit associations between active identifiers and historical or demographic aliases without destructive overwriting.

Alias association keeps historical and demographic identity references navigable alongside active identifiers. The non-destructive relationship preserves how earlier information identified the person rather than rewriting that history whenever the current identity representation changes.</documentation>
