              <folder name="II.1.3.4.2.3 [CT3] Device Connectivity [superseded]" id="id-6f710a1baa334dbcaafc6dc8c2c121b4">
                <documentation>Continuum navigation coordinate: II.1.3.4.2.3. Navigation asserts no semantic containment. Occurrence: architectural; no additional architectural instance or semantic relationship. Canonical element directory: canonicalId=658d4b6770a943bcb5801fb7ca9b47be; Exchange identifier=id-e0d0c691e440506bbcfd8980ffdbc1ea. Existing governed hierarchy member; directory retained for leaves.</documentation>
                <element xsi:type="archimate:Capability" name="[CT3] Device Connectivity" id="id-e0d0c691e440506bbcfd8980ffdbc1ea">
                  <documentation>Registering communication protocols and network endpoints for medical devices.

**Overview**

A device communication binding identifies the protocol and endpoint through which its feed can participate. Connectivity metadata supports routing without owning authentication issuance, payload semantics or physiological interpretation.

**Intent**

Make a device feed reachable through its registered communication binding.

**Boundary**

Represents communication bindings; it does not acquire authentication credential issuance or telemetry interpretation.</documentation>
