                <folder name="II.1.3.4.2.7.1 [Feature] Device Association Lineage" id="id-d0e79f6abde44f84952f7097a4d19938">
                  <documentation>Continuum navigation coordinate: II.1.3.4.2.7.1. Navigation asserts no semantic containment. Occurrence: architectural; no additional architectural instance or semantic relationship. Canonical element directory: canonicalId=849889c1a9e4495c86a6b32e49c449e3; Exchange identifier=id-d754effb7cca5cbea74d760acd8501cc. Existing governed hierarchy member; directory retained for leaves.</documentation>
                  <element xsi:type="archimate:Capability" name="[Feature] Device Association Lineage" id="id-d754effb7cca5cbea74d760acd8501cc" profiles="id-1fcc283b6cc74eab958ce9580eacd631">
                    <documentation>Preserve the attributed history and effective basis of device-to-subject/place associations.

**Overview**

A telemetry record needs to be interpreted against the association applicable when it arose, rather than the device current location alone.

**Boundary**

Association history does not interpret physiological observations or prove clinical correctness.</documentation>
