                <folder name="II.1.3.4.2.7.2 [Feature] Device-Patient/Location Assignment" id="id-f89eeefb35884104ba5c99468ddfadd2">
                  <documentation>Continuum navigation coordinate: II.1.3.4.2.7.2. Navigation asserts no semantic containment. Occurrence: architectural; no additional architectural instance or semantic relationship. Canonical element directory: canonicalId=891ed75bdd3c490296e5f0b7cacf6c87; Exchange identifier=id-773a1d80395252f492cecaced4054bf3. Existing governed hierarchy member; directory retained for leaves.</documentation>
                  <element xsi:type="archimate:Capability" name="[Feature] Device-Patient/Location Assignment" id="id-773a1d80395252f492cecaced4054bf3" profiles="id-1fcc283b6cc74eab958ce9580eacd631">
                    <documentation>Track dynamic association between a telemetry monitor, patient, and physical bed.

Dynamic device association preserves which patient or physical place a device is linked to as assignments change. This is essential context for interpreting telemetry: a stable device identity does not imply that every observation concerns the same patient over time.</documentation>
