                <folder name="II.1.3.4.4.1.4 [Feature] Service-Location-Provider Binding" id="id-b03b072d1c8049c38b1971ffbda6bc16">
                  <documentation>Continuum navigation coordinate: II.1.3.4.4.1.4. Navigation asserts no semantic containment. Occurrence: architectural; no additional architectural instance or semantic relationship. Canonical element directory: canonicalId=37188bb916244f41b1b7d988ad52a2eb; Exchange identifier=id-e4106c09a78d572987a147ae86fef3ca. Existing governed hierarchy member; directory retained for leaves.</documentation>
                  <element xsi:type="archimate:Capability" name="[Feature] Service-Location-Provider Binding" id="id-e4106c09a78d572987a147ae86fef3ca" profiles="id-1fcc283b6cc74eab958ce9580eacd631">
                    <documentation>Correlate which organization provides a named health service at which physical location with which practitioner roles.

Service-location-provider binding explains which participant provides an identifiable service in which place and acting capacities. The mapping associations belong to Health Service Administration, while the organisations, locations and practitioner entities retain their own information responsibility.</documentation>
