## ARB identity continuity

Historical identity [f1ab1258cf2944efb50105e7885f8027](f1ab1258cf2944efb50105e7885f8027.md) has direct correspondence with this capability under HCRL 1.1.5-002. Historical provenance and UUID reservation remain with that record; this resource retains its existing identity and independent standing.

## ARB source correspondence

Scope/anti-responsibility and clinical/operational meaning establish the responsible Capability; descriptive ledger/registry/asset labels do not establish a separately bounded formal Information Concept. Preserve non-transfer and source authority.

Source: `docs/markdown/03-business-architecture/information-responsibility/information-responsibility.md` — information responsibility row 8. Standing: Established Business responsibility only; formal information identity/lifecycle not inferred.

```text
| **Health Service Administration** | **Service Catalogue &amp; Service/Location/Provider Map** | Healthcare service definitions, clinical specialty taxonomy, service availability schedules, eligibility rules, and the multi-dimensional mapping matrix: $\text{Service} \leftrightarrow \text{Provider} \leftrightarrow \text{Location} \leftrightarrow \text{Practitioner}$. | Owns the *mapping associations*; does not own the mapped Provider, Location, or Practitioner entities. |
```</documentation>
