                <folder name="II.1.3.4.5.2.2 [Feature] Physical Hierarchy Modeling" id="id-a240577681dd41d588d7c7109a87a8c1">
                  <documentation>Continuum navigation coordinate: II.1.3.4.5.2.2. Navigation asserts no semantic containment. Occurrence: architectural; no additional architectural instance or semantic relationship. Canonical element directory: canonicalId=6166149dbd7b431985063d92e78ecdb7; Exchange identifier=id-f80fcd4209065e388707071708a9fdf7. Existing governed hierarchy member; directory retained for leaves.</documentation>
                  <element xsi:type="archimate:Capability" name="[Feature] Physical Hierarchy Modeling" id="id-f80fcd4209065e388707071708a9fdf7" profiles="id-1fcc283b6cc74eab958ce9580eacd631">
                    <documentation>Represent campus, building, wing, floor, and ward architectural relationships.

Physical hierarchy modelling relates a care environment to its campus, building, floor or ward context. The relationships describe where places sit physically; they do not automatically reproduce organisational hierarchy, service responsibility or operational capacity.</documentation>
