                <folder name="II.1.3.4.6.1.2 [Feature] Hierarchical Structure Navigation" id="id-55a68e96e92d4c4aad78ab3801565eaf">
                  <documentation>Continuum navigation coordinate: II.1.3.4.6.1.2. Navigation asserts no semantic containment. Occurrence: architectural; no additional architectural instance or semantic relationship. Canonical element directory: canonicalId=7ded6f7865294fb2a696a58160d577f7; Exchange identifier=id-d7bdfa04e6145465a17f0e9a96432259. Existing governed hierarchy member; directory retained for leaves.</documentation>
                  <element xsi:type="archimate:Capability" name="[Feature] Hierarchical Structure Navigation" id="id-d7bdfa04e6145465a17f0e9a96432259" profiles="id-1fcc283b6cc74eab958ce9580eacd631">
                    <documentation>Model, traverse, and resolve nested departmental, divisional, and regional healthcare networks.

Hierarchy navigation makes departmental, divisional and network relationships usable without flattening them into unrelated organisations. Traversal reflects established structure; it does not create corporate authority or infer responsibility from the way a directory happens to display a tree.</documentation>
                    <property key="v0.2 / Source Capture Key" value="feature:hierarchical-structure-navigation"/>
                    <property key="v0.2 / Snapshot Reference ID" value="FEAT-EM-19"/>
                    <property key="v0.2 / LaTeX Label" value="feature:feat-em-19"/>
