                <folder name="II.1.3.4.7.1.1 [Feature] National Practitioner Verification" id="id-faf534e1bc0b45359579e7f8d7a18300">
                  <documentation>Continuum navigation coordinate: II.1.3.4.7.1.1. Navigation asserts no semantic containment. Occurrence: architectural; no additional architectural instance or semantic relationship. Canonical element directory: canonicalId=12c5a17dcc564619a6a9222dd2e15528; Exchange identifier=id-b753aaf91c785bd998ff94d0ee413dac. Existing governed hierarchy member; directory retained for leaves.</documentation>
                  <element xsi:type="archimate:Capability" name="[Feature] National Practitioner Verification" id="id-b753aaf91c785bd998ff94d0ee413dac" profiles="id-1fcc283b6cc74eab958ce9580eacd631">
                    <documentation>Ingest, validate, and verify national practitioner identifiers (e.g., HPI-I) and professional registration status.

National verification connects practitioner identifiers and registration information to their recognised source context. It helps distinguish an identifiable professional from an unverified directory assertion without implying that verification alone grants local clinical privileges.</documentation>
