                <folder name="II.1.3.4.7.2.1 [Feature] Electronic Endpoint Binding" id="id-7d3da9bf18c2487d88c1bcd2ea826116">
                  <documentation>Continuum navigation coordinate: II.1.3.4.7.2.1. Navigation asserts no semantic containment. Occurrence: architectural; no additional architectural instance or semantic relationship. Canonical element directory: canonicalId=5dc3a424e68d47aea64ec573dc4b1225; Exchange identifier=id-fecc304d80685084bf190ebdd1a0dc6c. Existing governed hierarchy member; directory retained for leaves.</documentation>
                  <element xsi:type="archimate:Capability" name="[Feature] Electronic Endpoint Binding" id="id-fecc304d80685084bf190ebdd1a0dc6c" profiles="id-1fcc283b6cc74eab958ce9580eacd631">
                    <documentation>Associate validated communication endpoints (secure messaging addresses, direct routing queues) with specific practitioner roles.

Endpoint binding makes a verified communication destination specific to the practitioner's acting role. It supports routing to the intended professional capacity rather than assuming that every address attached to the person is interchangeable across organisations and services.</documentation>
