            <element xsi:type="archimate:Capability" name="[CT1] Entity Information Enablement" id="id-4726f9b8f6015e019238b5a8cc596c7c">
              <documentation>Administer identifying, descriptive and qualified relationship information concerning healthcare participants, organisations, locations, services, materiel and devices.

**Overview**

Administer identifying, descriptive and qualified relationship information concerning healthcare participants, organisations, locations, services, materiel and devices.

**Intent**

Administer identifying, descriptive and qualified relationship information concerning healthcare participants, organisations, locations, services, materiel and devices.

**Boundary**

Registry information does not establish clinical privilege, service readiness, occupancy or originating national identity authority.

## ARB identity continuity

Historical identity [e4d959d6c71d498c9ce00d2be4c048e3](e4d959d6c71d498c9ce00d2be4c048e3.md) has direct correspondence with this capability under HCRL 1.1.5-002. Historical provenance and UUID reservation remain with that record; this resource retains its existing identity and independent standing.</documentation>
