                  <documentation>Continuum navigation coordinate: II.1.3.6.1.1.1. Navigation asserts no semantic containment. Occurrence: architectural; no additional architectural instance or semantic relationship. Canonical element directory: canonicalId=7c61f21e558c44ab92c267a781116d1d; Exchange identifier=id-37a284c316fd590991cc54279e766af4. Existing governed hierarchy member; directory retained for leaves.</documentation>
                  <element xsi:type="archimate:Capability" name="[Feature] Bed Availability Tracking" id="id-37a284c316fd590991cc54279e766af4" profiles="id-1fcc283b6cc74eab958ce9580eacd631">
                    <documentation>Maintain operational status of all registered beds and care-places (VACANT, OCCUPIED, BLOCKED, RESERVED, DIRTY, CLEANING, CLEAN).

Availability tracking preserves the operational distinctions among vacancy, occupancy, reservation, blockage and cleaning conditions. These states support meaningful care-place coordination without equating an unoccupied bed with a ready place or usable service capacity.</documentation>
