              <folder name="II.1.3.6.3.2 [CT3] Service Offering Readiness Coordination" id="id-6d14170c88354c119ad63c298999de88">
                <folder name="II.1.3.6.3.2.1 [Feature] Service Readiness Dependency Assessment" id="id-6928d24bae5245949dc787eec6e2e5b6">
                  <documentation>Continuum navigation coordinate: II.1.3.6.3.2.1. Navigation asserts no semantic containment. Occurrence: architectural; no additional architectural instance or semantic relationship. Canonical element directory: canonicalId=4d917929d5cf43218049a84cf46662b0; Exchange identifier=id-eea28ef3bab358869d143da0c838865a. Existing governed hierarchy member; directory retained for leaves.</documentation>
                  <element xsi:type="archimate:Capability" name="[Feature] Service Readiness Dependency Assessment" id="id-eea28ef3bab358869d143da0c838865a" profiles="id-1fcc283b6cc74eab958ce9580eacd631">
                    <documentation>Associate time- and context-qualified dependency evidence to establish a bounded readiness view for an offering.

**Overview**

An offering may be in operating hours but not deliverable because staffing, equipment, materials or supporting services are missing. A readiness view retains insufficiency and the owners of those dependency assertions.

**Boundary**

Readiness evidence does not originate clinical clearance or transfer resource management.</documentation>
                    <property key="v0.2 / Source Capture Key" value="proposal:feature-service-readiness-dependency-assessment"/>
