            <folder name="II.1.3.6.5 [CT2] Clinic &amp; Practice Operations" id="id-068271ad9bb44ea19824cc078f916667">
              <folder name="II.1.3.6.5.1 [CT3] Session &amp; Queue Coordination" id="id-2bd1d3a013ec4329b7a721ef55761154">
                <folder name="II.1.3.6.5.1.1 [Feature] Clinic Session Capacity Management" id="id-4423e48590504e0abc9ac3446d1f682c">
                  <documentation>Continuum navigation coordinate: II.1.3.6.5.1.1. Navigation asserts no semantic containment. Occurrence: architectural; no additional architectural instance or semantic relationship. Canonical element directory: canonicalId=02bdd6a6f22e47f5a29d722ab57f9915; Exchange identifier=id-a766049417a05c75815f7dc20c247bb3. Existing governed hierarchy member; directory retained for leaves.</documentation>
                  <element xsi:type="archimate:Capability" name="[Feature] Clinic Session Capacity Management" id="id-a766049417a05c75815f7dc20c247bb3" profiles="id-1fcc283b6cc74eab958ce9580eacd631">
                    <documentation>Represent available, committed and utilised session capacity under clinic-specific constraints.

**Overview**

Clinic capacity depends on session staffing and service mix as well as places; queue progression alone is insufficient.

**Boundary**

Local responsibility retains its capacity meaning; Service Capacity Management consumes it without acquiring ownership or imposing one common capacity model.</documentation>
                    <property key="v0.2 / Source Capture Key" value="proposal:feature-clinic-session-capacity-management"/>
