              <documentation>Continuum navigation coordinate: II.1.3.6.6. Navigation asserts no semantic containment. Occurrence: architectural; no additional architectural instance or semantic relationship. Historical predecessor: R.2.124 [CT2] Clinical Competency Administration; canonicalId=8a4b918e1c9d47bb99daf2b42008ab39; Exchange identifier=id-d8818559ec0550c99acef678cd553252 Canonical element directory: canonicalId=8a99f4a6e5054d6c997bacec04805c01; Exchange identifier=id-e9ea67f4568d5b698a547301aa89e4bd. Existing governed hierarchy member; directory retained for leaves.</documentation>
              <element xsi:type="archimate:Capability" name="[CT2] Clinical Competency Administration" id="id-e9ea67f4568d5b698a547301aa89e4bd">
                <documentation>Administer information about what clinical capability an organisation can provide and what a practitioner is competent to perform.

**Overview**

Administer information about what clinical capability an organisation can provide and what a practitioner is competent to perform.

**Intent**

Administer information about what clinical capability an organisation can provide and what a practitioner is competent to perform.

**Boundary**

Information administration does not confer authority over the represented person, organisation, service, place, device or clinical activity.

---

## History

### Capability Overview — predecessor explanation

Clinical Competency Management is retained as a Reference context concerning practitioner competence. It is distinguishable from checking supplied qualification or competency evidence before specialised work. The model does not establish that representing evidence makes Harmonia the authority that assesses or grants competence.

### Boundary — predecessor explanation

No atomic Features or competency-assessment authority are allocated to this context.

### Harmonia Architectural Relevance — predecessor explanation

The formal Reference classification remains separate from the relevance of operational qualification checking elsewhere.

## ARB identity continuity

Historical identity [8a4b918e1c9d47bb99daf2b42008ab39](8a4b918e1c9d47bb99daf2b42008ab39.md) has direct correspondence with this capability under HCRL 1.1.5-002. Historical provenance and UUID reservation remain with that record; this resource retains its existing identity and independent standing.</documentation>
