                <element xsi:type="archimate:Capability" name="[CT3] Specimen Metadata Management" id="id-e58d7bdb27f95fb396623167a677a5ba">
                  <documentation>Manage the identifying, descriptive, custody and relevant handling information needed to interpret a transported specimen.

**Overview**

Manage the identifying, descriptive, custody and relevant handling information needed to interpret a transported specimen. The reviewed hierarchy assigns this enduring ability to its stated business-enabling context.

**Intent**

Manage the identifying, descriptive, custody and relevant handling information needed to interpret a transported specimen.

**Boundary**

Information administration and coordination preserve the authority of the responsible source, clinical actor and governed domain; they confer no additional real-world management authority.

## ARB identity continuity

Historical identity [3b000d3712534d16a48470f79df8e33a](3b000d3712534d16a48470f79df8e33a.md) has direct correspondence with this capability under HCRL 1.1.5-002. Historical provenance and UUID reservation remain with that record; this resource retains its existing identity and independent standing.</documentation>
