                <folder name="II.1.3.6.15.1.1 [Feature] Emergency Care Cross-Facility Correlation" id="id-a532cef89c39491d8dcc22c4311f6cbe">
                  <documentation>Continuum navigation coordinate: II.1.3.6.15.1.1. Navigation asserts no semantic containment. Occurrence: architectural; no additional architectural instance or semantic relationship. Canonical element directory: canonicalId=6140586e2b18424d845a1f07018e6b49; Exchange identifier=id-026b3d0ebfee56b5b32f4cbba982a4a8. Existing governed hierarchy member; directory retained for leaves.</documentation>
                  <element xsi:type="archimate:Capability" name="[Feature] Emergency Care Cross-Facility Correlation" id="id-026b3d0ebfee56b5b32f4cbba982a4a8" profiles="id-1fcc283b6cc74eab958ce9580eacd631">
                    <documentation>Correlate incoming emergency presentations with recent regional admissions, prior discharge summaries, and known allergy profiles.

Cross-facility correlation connects an emergency presentation with relevant recent history and allergy information. It supports situational understanding across institutional boundaries without deciding the clinical significance of the combined evidence or assigning emergency treatment.</documentation>
