                <folder name="II.1.3.6.16.1.1 [Feature] Mobile Service Capacity Management" id="id-b1bda129b56e4e99be68cb70c9c29145">
                  <documentation>Continuum navigation coordinate: II.1.3.6.16.1.1. Navigation asserts no semantic containment. Occurrence: architectural; no additional architectural instance or semantic relationship. Canonical element directory: canonicalId=abdcb95b3725405f878f199b07779d19; Exchange identifier=id-56e5d0861bcd5ac2a6bf3e2206be9623. Existing governed hierarchy member; directory retained for leaves.</documentation>
                  <element xsi:type="archimate:Capability" name="[Feature] Mobile Service Capacity Management" id="id-56e5d0861bcd5ac2a6bf3e2206be9623" profiles="id-1fcc283b6cc74eab958ce9580eacd631">
                    <documentation>Represent mobile service capacity with travel, coverage, work commitment and availability context.

**Overview**

Mobile availability cannot be interpreted as a simple on-duty count because distance, assignments and suitable skills affect deliverability.

**Boundary**

Local responsibility retains its capacity meaning; Service Capacity Management consumes it without acquiring ownership or imposing one common capacity model.</documentation>
