              <documentation>Continuum navigation coordinate: II.1.3.6.16. Navigation asserts no semantic containment. Occurrence: architectural; no additional architectural instance or semantic relationship. Historical predecessor: R.2.144 [CT2] Mobile Staff Management; canonicalId=32118856636f400a95fc28daacea61c8; Exchange identifier=id-859c08b9ae82509bb2b1fea5d5f6d121 Canonical element directory: canonicalId=79a4a48fddf74c69acf7e16404d06ea5; Exchange identifier=id-bfbdb4730780550e884dabf485f6cc6f. Existing governed hierarchy member; directory retained for leaves.</documentation>
              <element xsi:type="archimate:Capability" name="[CT2] Mobile Staff Management" id="id-bfbdb4730780550e884dabf485f6cc6f">
                <documentation>Mobile Staff Management integrates with external business mobile-work mechanisms and receives visit progression and safety milestones. Its established dispatch Feature exchanges assignment, dispatch and status information with the relevant worker context. This is an information integration boundary around mobile activity, rather than a platform claim to decide the clinician's work.

**Overview**

Mobile Staff Management integrates with external business mobile-work mechanisms and receives visit progression and safety milestones. Its established dispatch Feature exchanges assignment, dispatch and status information with the relevant worker context. This is an information integration boundary around mobile activity, rather than a platform claim to decide the clinician's work.

**Intent**

Mobile Staff Management integrates with external business mobile-work mechanisms and receives visit progression and safety milestones. Its established dispatch Feature exchanges assignment, dispatch and status information with the relevant worker context. This is an information integration boundary around mobile activity, rather than a platform claim to decide the clinician's work.

**Boundary**

Information administration does not confer authority over the represented person, organisation, service, place, device or clinical activity.

---

## History

### Boundary — predecessor explanation

Harmonia does not determine clinical allocation, handover or EMR worklists. External work/task language does not redefine the internal Synthetic Task.

### Harmonia Architectural Relevance — predecessor explanation

Mobile assignment and progression exchanges materially connect roving activity to the wider care environment within that bounded integration role.

