                <element xsi:type="archimate:Capability" name="[CT3] Outpatient Flow Coordination" id="id-4595d9da485357d4b4d5ab830b5ad0a1">
                  <documentation>Coordinate outpatient arrival, clinic flow, follow-up requirements and context-specific outpatient capacity information.

**Overview**

Coordinate outpatient arrival, clinic flow, follow-up requirements and context-specific outpatient capacity information. The reviewed hierarchy assigns this enduring ability to its stated business-enabling context.

**Intent**

Coordinate outpatient arrival, clinic flow, follow-up requirements and context-specific outpatient capacity information.

**Boundary**

Information administration and coordination preserve the authority of the responsible source, clinical actor and governed domain; they confer no additional real-world management authority.

## ARB identity continuity

Historical identity [e6c59c7b72fe44169a5fdfd08a5e91c4](e6c59c7b72fe44169a5fdfd08a5e91c4.md) has direct correspondence with this capability under HCRL 1.1.5-002. Historical provenance and UUID reservation remain with that record; this resource retains its existing identity and independent standing.</documentation>
