                <folder name="II.1.3.6.20.1.2 [Feature] Transport Request Ingestion" id="id-1455aea5d0494ff68c3b8ca8cb6ffedc">
                  <documentation>Continuum navigation coordinate: II.1.3.6.20.1.2. Navigation asserts no semantic containment. Occurrence: architectural; no additional architectural instance or semantic relationship. Canonical element directory: canonicalId=7104472d065840eb91ae4cb7a3a0cb43; Exchange identifier=id-8b229766078a5e849660abdac36a765b. Existing governed hierarchy member; directory retained for leaves.</documentation>
                  <element xsi:type="archimate:Capability" name="[Feature] Transport Request Ingestion" id="id-8b229766078a5e849660abdac36a765b" profiles="id-1fcc283b6cc74eab958ce9580eacd631">
                    <documentation>Ingest internal (portering) and external (ambulance, inter-hospital) patient transfer requests with clinical mobility requirements.

Transport ingestion establishes the requested movement and applicable clinical mobility constraints. It gives operational coordination the context needed to arrange transit without making the request itself a departure, arrival or accepted care transition.</documentation>
                    <property key="v0.2 / Source Capture Key" value="feature:transport-request-ingestion"/>
