                <folder name="II.1.3.6.21.1.1 [Feature] Operational Capacity Metric Aggregation" id="id-dffd9f1d7af84881aeb48dfea5ee4ed8">
                  <documentation>Continuum navigation coordinate: II.1.3.6.21.1.1. Navigation asserts no semantic containment. Occurrence: architectural; no additional architectural instance or semantic relationship. Canonical element directory: canonicalId=1fe9199a49744eeaa5d063d7a84544ea; Exchange identifier=id-4a05f5487a135f89a097d6c3664a4506. Existing governed hierarchy member; directory retained for leaves.</documentation>
                  <element xsi:type="archimate:Capability" name="[Feature] Operational Capacity Metric Aggregation" id="id-4a05f5487a135f89a097d6c3664a4506" profiles="id-1fcc283b6cc74eab958ce9580eacd631">
                    <documentation>Aggregate operational capacity telemetry (occupancy rates, wait times, diversion status) across facilities.

Capacity aggregation combines occupancy, waiting and diversion context across facilities. The higher-order view must retain the originating service-specific capacity meaning; a shared metric does not transfer clinic, ward or theatre capacity responsibility to the aggregator.</documentation>
