              <element xsi:type="archimate:Capability" name="[CT2] Service Establishment Support" id="id-1ae0ff5d6b3b54deb3f9a0832045bcf5">
                <documentation>Support the information needed to establish a health service in its intended operating context.

**Overview**

Support the information needed to establish a health service in its intended operating context. The reviewed hierarchy assigns this enduring ability to its stated business-enabling context.

**Intent**

Support the information needed to establish a health service in its intended operating context.

**Boundary**

Information administration and coordination preserve the authority of the responsible source, clinical actor and governed domain; they confer no additional real-world management authority.

## ARB identity continuity

Historical identity [8a63b08f34fa42c5bda2a3e12b9ecd55](8a63b08f34fa42c5bda2a3e12b9ecd55.md) has direct correspondence with this capability under HCRL 1.1.5-002. Historical provenance and UUID reservation remain with that record; this resource retains its existing identity and independent standing.</documentation>
