                  <documentation>Continuum navigation coordinate: II.1.3.6.23.1.1. Navigation asserts no semantic containment. Occurrence: architectural; no additional architectural instance or semantic relationship. Canonical element directory: canonicalId=2fd65f09f7384f0486280e56ec5a9e84; Exchange identifier=id-b0e1921663045bf5a2297d507ff219fc. Existing governed hierarchy member; directory retained for leaves.</documentation>
                  <element xsi:type="archimate:Capability" name="[Feature] Operating Theatre Case Progression" id="id-b0e1921663045bf5a2297d507ff219fc" profiles="id-1fcc283b6cc74eab958ce9580eacd631">
                    <documentation>Track surgical case state transitions (CALLED → IN_THEATRE → ANAESTHETISED → INCISION → CLOSED → RECOVERY).

Case progression records externally established surgical milestones in an operationally meaningful sequence. It makes the theatre situation visible without authorising or performing the clinical acts denoted by anaesthesia, incision, closure or recovery.</documentation>
