                <folder name="II.1.3.6.23.1.2 [Feature] Perioperative Resource Notification" id="id-ede1769f746247cab7c047915bf5135b">
                  <documentation>Continuum navigation coordinate: II.1.3.6.23.1.2. Navigation asserts no semantic containment. Occurrence: architectural; no additional architectural instance or semantic relationship. Canonical element directory: canonicalId=1f2446ccc59348a6bc54d8268ef4e6e1; Exchange identifier=id-48c0126f15ab5a2cbfceae72f135688a. Existing governed hierarchy member; directory retained for leaves.</documentation>
                  <element xsi:type="archimate:Capability" name="[Feature] Perioperative Resource Notification" id="id-48c0126f15ab5a2cbfceae72f135688a" profiles="id-1fcc283b6cc74eab958ce9580eacd631">
                    <documentation>Dispatch alerts to portering, sterilization, and recovery teams based on surgical case progression milestones.

Perioperative notification connects relevant case milestones with portering, sterilisation and recovery participants. Observation alone does not realise the Feature's dispatch responsibility; the established case-progression behaviour includes the required alerts without adding another Function or Service.</documentation>
