                <folder name="II.1.3.6.24.2.1 [Feature] Clinical Handover Context Assembly" id="id-4841054aac674a129d2729a99a7e5725">
                  <documentation>Continuum navigation coordinate: II.1.3.6.24.2.1. Navigation asserts no semantic containment. Occurrence: architectural; no additional architectural instance or semantic relationship. Canonical element directory: canonicalId=f8c748aa08444723b784887174831d51; Exchange identifier=id-7323852ae9465ec8ab0f39be5f2fbf0a. Existing governed hierarchy member; directory retained for leaves.</documentation>
                  <element xsi:type="archimate:Capability" name="[Feature] Clinical Handover Context Assembly" id="id-7323852ae9465ec8ab0f39be5f2fbf0a" profiles="id-1fcc283b6cc74eab958ce9580eacd631">
                    <documentation>Collate current ward patient lists, active medical concerns, and pending tasks for nursing shift handovers.

Handover context assembly brings patient lists, current concerns and pending tasks together for the participants conducting a shift handover. Assembly is the established responsibility: it does not perform clinical review, decide pending clinical work or manage the handover itself.</documentation>
