                <folder name="II.1.3.6.24.2.2 [Feature] Ward Care Capacity Management" id="id-6704a327fcfc4bf0ad2e4aa4734fc147">
                  <documentation>Continuum navigation coordinate: II.1.3.6.24.2.2. Navigation asserts no semantic containment. Occurrence: architectural; no additional architectural instance or semantic relationship. Canonical element directory: canonicalId=0d45b0afc0584afba4bd0414f5f10e37; Exchange identifier=id-93de013fe0b75f5cbaf7a4275539eb93. Existing governed hierarchy member; directory retained for leaves.</documentation>
                  <element xsi:type="archimate:Capability" name="[Feature] Ward Care Capacity Management" id="id-93de013fe0b75f5cbaf7a4275539eb93" profiles="id-1fcc283b6cc74eab958ce9580eacd631">
                    <documentation>Represent ward care capacity in relation to staffing, care-place suitability and patient dependency.

**Overview**

A clean bed can remain unusable when staffing or patient needs constrain the ward; source clinical facts remain attributed.

**Boundary**

Local responsibility retains its capacity meaning; Service Capacity Management consumes it without acquiring ownership or imposing one common capacity model.</documentation>
                    <property key="v0.2 / Source Capture Key" value="proposal:feature-ward-care-capacity-management"/>
