                <folder name="II.1.3.6.25.1.2 [Feature] Work Item Instantiation" id="id-f85cd16baa4847c6beda0ccb27aeab96">
                  <documentation>Continuum navigation coordinate: II.1.3.6.25.1.2. Navigation asserts no semantic containment. Occurrence: architectural; no additional architectural instance or semantic relationship. Canonical element directory: canonicalId=321fa656c71f4019842b5b991dbc9ff4; Exchange identifier=id-f63d1e9808aa5ac78f8aab1e05fbb7d0. Existing governed hierarchy member; directory retained for leaves.</documentation>
                  <element xsi:type="archimate:Capability" name="[Feature] Work Item Instantiation" id="id-f63d1e9808aa5ac78f8aab1e05fbb7d0" profiles="id-1fcc283b6cc74eab958ce9580eacd631">
                    <documentation>Instantiate operational units of work from clinical triggers (e.g., bed cleaning required, specimen transport required).

Work-item instantiation gives an authorised operational requirement an identifiable unit of work. It distinguishes recognising that support activity is needed from assigning it, dispatching it and recording its completion; a clinical trigger does not make the resulting support item clinical work authority.</documentation>
