                  <documentation>Continuum navigation coordinate: II.1.3.6.25.1.4. Navigation asserts no semantic containment. Occurrence: architectural; no additional architectural instance or semantic relationship. Canonical element directory: canonicalId=caac8a83dc974cdb9c9bc1b778b9cee7; Exchange identifier=id-109077f750945afeb4ab67ed67f204f0. Existing governed hierarchy member; directory retained for leaves.</documentation>
                  <element xsi:type="archimate:Capability" name="[Feature] Worker Matching &amp; Allocation" id="id-109077f750945afeb4ab67ed67f204f0" profiles="id-1fcc283b6cc74eab958ce9580eacd631">
                    <documentation>Match work items against available staff roles, credentials, and locations based on allocation policies.

Worker matching relates an operational requirement to eligible roles, credentials, locations and availability under policy. It consumes those constraints rather than changing their authoritative records, and does not turn operational allocation into permission to decide clinical work.</documentation>
