                  <documentation>Continuum navigation coordinate: II.1.3.7.2.1.1. Navigation asserts no semantic containment. Occurrence: architectural; no additional architectural instance or semantic relationship. Canonical element directory: canonicalId=bdfaeebab74e4d4d96a5e3799a3aa07b; Exchange identifier=id-337f8c9d1cb75bd19fc27f6b3cacb703. Existing governed hierarchy member; directory retained for leaves.</documentation>
                  <element xsi:type="archimate:Capability" name="[Feature] Entity Behaviour Failure &amp; Recovery Governance" id="id-337f8c9d1cb75bd19fc27f6b3cacb703" profiles="id-1fcc283b6cc74eab958ce9580eacd631">
                    <documentation>Apply explicit behaviour-failure dispositions and controlled, authorised resumption for entity-relative processing.

**Overview**

Failure may stop a behaviour, an input or the entity progression and may leave effects uncertain. Resumption must preserve that distinction rather than imply rollback or automatic safe retry.

**Boundary**

Recovery cannot silently declare no effects, bypass governance or resume a halted entity automatically.</documentation>
