                <documentation>Continuum navigation coordinate: II.1.3.7.2.1. Navigation asserts no semantic containment. Occurrence: architectural; no additional architectural instance or semantic relationship. Canonical element directory: canonicalId=9f0c1429b64f4f88982fbbda6eaec233; Exchange identifier=id-90f67ae80f4e599eb3a922a46aa46139. Existing governed hierarchy member; directory retained for leaves.</documentation>
                <element xsi:type="archimate:Capability" name="[CT3] Entity-Specific Operational Coordination" id="id-90f67ae80f4e599eb3a922a46aa46139">
                  <documentation>Coordinate governed operational progression relative to one represented entity, including interested behaviour participation and controlled recovery.

**Overview**

Activity concerning the same patient, practitioner or bed needs a coherent entity-relative frame. Interest fan-out, serial progression, fresh information context and uncertain effects remain distinguishable from generic multi-work-unit progression.

**Intent**

Keep the progression of one represented entity coherent across interested operational behaviours.

**Boundary**

Entity coordination does not own all entity information, determine clinical work or become the source of clinical decisions. No Twin component allocation follows from this proposal.

## Qualified relationship assertions

Original source predicates, evidence and qualifications remain in the metadata. The ARB has now adjudicated their native treatment; explicitly unestablished relationship existence remains excluded. Native representation does not promote source standing.

| Source predicate | Target element | Source standing / currentness | ARB native treatment |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| enterprise_enabled_by | [[CT3] Entity-Relative Operational Progression](69c82474fb534152b151c92f706197d0.md) | Proposed / preserved historical assertion | Serving (reverse) — `id-962aa74f06475024b564156a80125b8b` |</documentation>
