                <element xsi:type="archimate:Capability" name="[CT3] Governed Operational Activity Design" id="id-e285e2523d1f5fe488af1b4735d4a49b">
                  <documentation>Define the information context, expected outcomes, continuation conditions and housekeeping of governed operational activity.

**Overview**

An activity needs a fulfilment definition even when only one bounded execution unit is involved. This capability specifies its semantic envelope while execution and event delivery remain separate responsibilities.

**Intent**

Make the expected information and fulfilment basis of an undertaking explicit before it executes.

**Boundary**

An activity definition is neither an orchestrator nor a choreographer. It does not choose clinical care or dynamically invent execution logic.

## Qualified relationship assertions

Original source predicates, evidence and qualifications remain in the metadata. The ARB has now adjudicated their native treatment; explicitly unestablished relationship existence remains excluded. Native representation does not promote source standing.

| Source predicate | Target element | Source standing / currentness | ARB native treatment |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| enterprise_enabled_by | [[CT3] Operational Fulfilment Definition](2b52c0de17b146da962f303e99f90a4a.md) | Proposed / preserved historical assertion | Serving (reverse) — `id-ee56316e519559ac819240e63fb2d17b` |
| enterprise_enabled_by | [[CT3] Governed Activity Execution Control](1e351cdfdc1045e384c3bd768eed8e80.md) | Proposed / preserved historical assertion | Serving (reverse) — `id-1b4d2b793b805b0bb6227c270b895e40` |</documentation>
