                <folder name="II.1.3.7.2.3.1 [Feature] Controlled Administrative Recovery" id="id-a1f3f7d0c7094b789550ca4c4bb9713a">
                  <documentation>Continuum navigation coordinate: II.1.3.7.2.3.1. Navigation asserts no semantic containment. Occurrence: architectural; no additional architectural instance or semantic relationship. Canonical element directory: canonicalId=21d0601a852043a4b0b1d4fe841108d2; Exchange identifier=id-14f2b94d4e9551c6b3d19b26aa56aa16. Existing governed hierarchy member; directory retained for leaves.</documentation>
                  <element xsi:type="archimate:Capability" name="[Feature] Controlled Administrative Recovery" id="id-14f2b94d4e9551c6b3d19b26aa56aa16" profiles="id-1fcc283b6cc74eab958ce9580eacd631">
                    <documentation>Perform authorised recovery as identifiable governed activity through normal execution and evidence boundaries.

**Overview**

Operators may need to resume, reconcile or repair an operational concern. That is first-class work with permission and outcome standing, rather than direct mutation through a console.

**Boundary**

Administrative interaction grants no raw cache/database or subsystem-internal bypass.</documentation>
