                <folder name="II.1.3.7.2.3.4 [Feature] Uncertain Activity Outcome Reconciliation" id="id-427478a499bf4c6a996c06900ba4ecc8">
                  <documentation>Continuum navigation coordinate: II.1.3.7.2.3.4. Navigation asserts no semantic containment. Occurrence: architectural; no additional architectural instance or semantic relationship. Canonical element directory: canonicalId=eb06ecc956404d0397701ceafb5fbd46; Exchange identifier=id-00706dca11295d44b01a89f0e66c83d2. Existing governed hierarchy member; directory retained for leaves.</documentation>
                  <element xsi:type="archimate:Capability" name="[Feature] Uncertain Activity Outcome Reconciliation" id="id-00706dca11295d44b01a89f0e66c83d2" profiles="id-1fcc283b6cc74eab958ce9580eacd631">
                    <documentation>Reconcile indeterminate activity effects through authoritative observation before establishing a safe next disposition.

**Overview**

A timeout or absent response leaves a materially significant outcome unknown. Reconciliation can confirm an effect, establish absence or retain uncertainty without automatically retrying the original work.

**Boundary**

Execution uncertainty differs from insufficient assurance evidence; a retry does not prove the earlier attempt had no effect.</documentation>
