            <element xsi:type="archimate:Capability" name="[CT1] Independent Assurance Enablement" id="id-7045e58c19235175b54f5d054232b883">
              <documentation>Enable assurance specification and independent review of the assurance service while preserving the distinct Canonical responsibility for assurance against a governed subject.

**Overview**

Enable assurance specification and independent review of the assurance service while preserving the distinct Canonical responsibility for assurance against a governed subject.

**Intent**

Enable assurance specification and independent review of the assurance service while preserving the distinct Canonical responsibility for assurance against a governed subject.

**Boundary**

Assurance cannot manage, remediate or approve its subject merely because it observes it. Clinical adequacy, financial governance and source-information authority remain outside this mandate.

## ARB identity continuity

Historical identity [88bf57b7a92c4c1da1b5f0a67d3ebd82](88bf57b7a92c4c1da1b5f0a67d3ebd82.md) has direct correspondence with this capability under HCRL 1.1.5-002. Historical provenance and UUID reservation remain with that record; this resource retains its existing identity and independent standing.</documentation>
