                <folder name="II.1.3.9.1.1.2 [Feature] Temporal Event Correlation" id="id-0fe5552ef98c4726a7138f593e32b24a">
                  <documentation>Continuum navigation coordinate: II.1.3.9.1.1.2. Navigation asserts no semantic containment. Occurrence: architectural; no additional architectural instance or semantic relationship. Canonical element directory: canonicalId=05e1c23baf1c47fbac8457f991efa2be; Exchange identifier=id-4aeda5a5e90752788a66aa0fd3628ed3. Existing governed hierarchy member; directory retained for leaves.</documentation>
                  <element xsi:type="archimate:Capability" name="[Feature] Temporal Event Correlation" id="id-4aeda5a5e90752788a66aa0fd3628ed3" profiles="id-1fcc283b6cc74eab958ce9580eacd631">
                    <documentation>Correlate incoming clinical events with scheduled appointments and operational calendar milestones.

Temporal correlation relates incoming events to the relevant appointment or calendar milestone. Association provides context for interpretation and coordination without assuming that temporal proximity proves attendance, fulfilment or the clinical outcome expected at that time.</documentation>
