                  <documentation>Continuum navigation coordinate: II.1.3.9.2.1.4. Navigation asserts no semantic containment. Occurrence: architectural; no additional architectural instance or semantic relationship. Canonical element directory: canonicalId=87e9246c944a40d9af5c4d0a3a7d4e9a; Exchange identifier=id-1f6e2bc8338f5658869a5957b235f40f. Existing governed hierarchy member; directory retained for leaves.</documentation>
                  <element xsi:type="archimate:Capability" name="[Feature] Zero-PHI Collaboration Metadata Governance" id="id-1f6e2bc8338f5658869a5957b235f40f" profiles="id-1fcc283b6cc74eab958ce9580eacd631">
                    <documentation>Ensure collaboration channel titles, topics, and aliases use opaque identifiers free of patient names, MRNs, or sensitive details.

Metadata governance keeps patient names, identifiers and sensitive detail out of collaboration titles, topics and aliases. Opaque references preserve useful contextual association without placing PHI in broadly visible channel metadata or diagnostic surfaces.</documentation>
