                <documentation>Continuum navigation coordinate: II.1.3.9.3.1. Navigation asserts no semantic containment. Occurrence: architectural; no additional architectural instance or semantic relationship. Canonical element directory: canonicalId=8c850faafb334f97a81a0b4cd8fdb65f; Exchange identifier=id-b78f67bb04765785bb46be9e9c5427d3. Existing governed hierarchy member; directory retained for leaves.</documentation>
                <element xsi:type="archimate:Capability" name="[CT3] Information Authority Representation" id="id-b78f67bb04765785bb46be9e9c5427d3">
                  <documentation>Represent the source, credibility and qualified authority standing of competing health-information assertions.

**Overview**

A persisted assertion may be authoritative, informational or anecdotal. This ability carries that standing into interpretation without treating transport reliability, freshness or successful commit as proof of credibility.

**Intent**

Keep an assertion technical acceptance separate from the standing of the source that asserted it.

**Boundary**

Classification does not originate clinical facts or universally adjudicate conflicts. Policy determines how qualified assertions are used.

## Qualified relationship assertions

Original source predicates, evidence and qualifications remain in the metadata. The ARB has now adjudicated their native treatment; explicitly unestablished relationship existence remains excluded. Native representation does not promote source standing.

| Source predicate | Target element | Source standing / currentness | ARB native treatment |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| enterprise_enabled_by | [[CT2] Information Authority Qualification](cbba9984dd404deabed41fdcc96088b1.md) | Proposed / preserved historical assertion | Serving (reverse) — `id-b0cce339e3ce59d99feeef2959d1cd7d` |</documentation>
