                <folder name="II.1.3.9.4.2.2 [Feature] Clinical Concept Resolution" id="id-44a06b2d3abb4be3b3af0fd03849db3f">
                  <documentation>Continuum navigation coordinate: II.1.3.9.4.2.2. Navigation asserts no semantic containment. Occurrence: architectural; no additional architectural instance or semantic relationship. Canonical element directory: canonicalId=30cdb9b2a810467c9b56e9870de4367e; Exchange identifier=id-e97a4d5858585c9a89e93fb9321aba7c. Existing governed hierarchy member; directory retained for leaves.</documentation>
                  <element xsi:type="archimate:Capability" name="[Feature] Clinical Concept Resolution" id="id-e97a4d5858585c9a89e93fb9321aba7c" profiles="id-1fcc283b6cc74eab958ce9580eacd631">
                    <documentation>Resolve local clinical codes against standard terminologies (SNOMED CT, LOINC, ICD-10).

Concept resolution makes a coded clinical reference interpretable against its governed terminology. It validates the reference context without making a recognised code proof of clinical truth or giving the consuming system authority to redefine the concept.</documentation>
