              <element xsi:type="archimate:Capability" name="[CT2] Health Information Communication" id="id-5004f4019d1059108356b6ee7cfcaa8e">
                <documentation>Enable patient notifications, patient task communication, patient self-service and access to a patient health library under applicable information-use controls.

**Overview**

Enable patient notifications, patient task communication, patient self-service and access to a patient health library under applicable information-use controls. The reviewed hierarchy assigns this enduring ability to its stated business-enabling context.

**Intent**

Enable patient notifications, patient task communication, patient self-service and access to a patient health library under applicable information-use controls.

**Boundary**

Information administration and coordination preserve the authority of the responsible source, clinical actor and governed domain; they confer no additional real-world management authority.

## ARB identity continuity

Historical identity [bcefb378424842fcb6d703208c3f8773](bcefb378424842fcb6d703208c3f8773.md) has direct correspondence with this capability under HCRL 1.1.5-002. Historical provenance and UUID reservation remain with that record; this resource retains its existing identity and independent standing.</documentation>
