              <folder name="II.1.3.9.9.4 [Feature] Governed Policy Assignment &amp; Revocation" id="id-4454ffccb8bd402ab0c0ca897b2910ba">
                <documentation>Continuum navigation coordinate: II.1.3.9.9.4. Navigation asserts no semantic containment. Occurrence: architectural; no additional architectural instance or semantic relationship. Canonical element directory: canonicalId=d6c271ae95ea44449c5e22665d1d9bc2; Exchange identifier=id-c0ee6896b3d759a9980c2a79ad7c3e53. Existing governed hierarchy member; directory retained for leaves.</documentation>
                <element xsi:type="archimate:Capability" name="[Feature] Governed Policy Assignment &amp; Revocation" id="id-c0ee6896b3d759a9980c2a79ad7c3e53" profiles="id-1fcc283b6cc74eab958ce9580eacd631">
                  <documentation>Manage approved permission criteria and identity/role assignments, including temporal applicability and revocation.

**Overview**

An assignment becoming inapplicable by expiry differs from an explicit revocation; both must affect the effective authority used for operations.

**Boundary**

Management does not grant unconstrained administrative authority or derive permission from resource tags.</documentation>
