              <folder name="II.1.3.9.9.5 [Feature] Non-PHI Compliance Auditing" id="id-6fdd7732b0274c1cbb1be34dec6062cf">
                <documentation>Continuum navigation coordinate: II.1.3.9.9.5. Navigation asserts no semantic containment. Occurrence: architectural; no additional architectural instance or semantic relationship. Canonical element directory: canonicalId=08e37326908a49988dfb787f68df840a; Exchange identifier=id-134a61003723533683cb931b9231dd3f. Existing governed hierarchy member; directory retained for leaves.</documentation>
                <element xsi:type="archimate:Capability" name="[Feature] Non-PHI Compliance Auditing" id="id-134a61003723533683cb931b9231dd3f" profiles="id-1fcc283b6cc74eab958ce9580eacd631">
                  <documentation>Generate tamper-evident, verifiable audit records of security-significant events without emitting unmasked PHI.

---

## History

### Feature Overview — predecessor explanation

Security-significant audit evidence makes governed actions attributable and verifiable while respecting PHI restrictions. The record concerns meaningful security facts under policy rather than routine implementation events, and recording it does not independently establish an assurance conclusion.</documentation>
