              <folder name="II.1.3.9.9.6 [Feature] Operation-Bound Authorisation Enforcement" id="id-9c51539efb0a4ef09925b2c90bd148eb">
                <documentation>Continuum navigation coordinate: II.1.3.9.9.6. Navigation asserts no semantic containment. Occurrence: architectural; no additional architectural instance or semantic relationship. Canonical element directory: canonicalId=3b7dcee7d58d4d1c960dc92abd58b4c3; Exchange identifier=id-edcdc7b12cc25092aee8b7c197674755. Existing governed hierarchy member; directory retained for leaves.</documentation>
                <element xsi:type="archimate:Capability" name="[Feature] Operation-Bound Authorisation Enforcement" id="id-edcdc7b12cc25092aee8b7c197674755" profiles="id-1fcc283b6cc74eab958ce9580eacd631">
                  <documentation>Apply effective policy at the governed action boundary and reject actions lacking sufficient authority.

**Overview**

Consistent enforcement is required across mutation, access, execution and administration rather than relying on each caller to voluntarily invoke a check.

**Boundary**

Consumes trusted identity and criteria; it does not authenticate or establish clinical privilege from directory roles.</documentation>
