              <folder name="II.1.3.9.9.7 [Feature] Security Context Propagation" id="id-b30349e9d6f8473590ca9ba6d53d1eb1">
                <documentation>Continuum navigation coordinate: II.1.3.9.9.7. Navigation asserts no semantic containment. Occurrence: architectural; no additional architectural instance or semantic relationship. Canonical element directory: canonicalId=2b071c4fb10c4f61afecd18d09387214; Exchange identifier=id-7e3672f150a85990ba602078b3393205. Existing governed hierarchy member; directory retained for leaves.</documentation>
                <element xsi:type="archimate:Capability" name="[Feature] Security Context Propagation" id="id-7e3672f150a85990ba602078b3393205" profiles="id-1fcc283b6cc74eab958ce9580eacd631">
                  <documentation>Propagate tamper-evident, attributable security context across asynchronous processing boundaries.

---

## History

### Feature Overview — predecessor explanation

Security-context propagation carries attributable operational authority across asynchronous boundaries. Its responsibility is preservation of established context, distinct from evaluating a consent constraint; shared security subject matter is insufficient to assign that Function to this Feature.</documentation>
