                <property key="v0.2 / Snapshot Record JSON" value="{&quot;ancestry_status&quot;:&quot;proposed&quot;,&quot;architectural_status&quot;:&quot;Canonical&quot;,&quot;baseline_description&quot;:{&quot;Boundary&quot;:&quot;Security context is operational context and does not automatically become resource content. Security-context validation has no invented one-to-one mapping to propagation, and audit recording is not an assurance conclusion.&quot;,&quot;Capability Overview&quot;:&quot;Health Information Control establishes the policy and security basis for governed information operations. Default-deny authority evaluation, consent constraints, security-context propagation and security-significant evidence have distinct purposes: deciding permission, retaining restrictions, carrying attributable operational context and preserving required evidence. The capability makes security intrinsic to the operation rather than optional presentation behaviour.&quot;,&quot;Harmonia Architectural Relevance&quot;:&quot;Assigned policy enforcement and attributable context are substantive Core responsibilities across managed operations.&quot;},&quot;baseline_placement&quot;:{&quot;canonical_id&quot;:null,&quot;owner_key&quot;:null,&quot;parent_key&quot;:null,&quot;tier&quot;:null},&quot;baseline_unresolved&quot;:[&quot;tier&quot;,&quot;root_status&quot;,&quot;ancestry&quot;,&quot;canonical_id&quot;,&quot;code_allocation&quot;],&quot;baseline_version&quot;:&quot;0.1&quot;,&quot;boundary&quot;:&quot;Information administration does not confer authority over the represented person, organisation, service, place, device or clinical activity. Client consent directives remain owned by Client Privacy Guardrail Management (FEAT-EM-09); this capability references and respects those determinations without defining a second consent owner.&quot;,&quot;canonical_id&quot;:&quot;CT1-BEC-GOVERNED-HEALTH-INFORMATION-ENABLEMENT.CT2-BEC-HEALTH-INFORMATION-CONTROL&quot;,&quot;canonical_name&quot