                <folder name="II.1.3.9.10.2.1 [Feature] Addressed Clinical Distribution" id="id-79d4095e3ffb44d5898ad2fb381080af">
                  <documentation>Continuum navigation coordinate: II.1.3.9.10.2.1. Navigation asserts no semantic containment. Occurrence: architectural; no additional architectural instance or semantic relationship. Canonical element directory: canonicalId=b476c86edab644c394da33d3de7bd0bd; Exchange identifier=id-58f6fa48f0e35e7dab2554c31ac16497. Existing governed hierarchy member; directory retained for leaves.</documentation>
                  <element xsi:type="archimate:Capability" name="[Feature] Addressed Clinical Distribution" id="id-58f6fa48f0e35e7dab2554c31ac16497" profiles="id-1fcc283b6cc74eab958ce9580eacd631">
                    <documentation>Fan out clinical events and diagnostic reports to designated external and internal recipients with per-destination delivery tracking.

Addressed distribution sends information to explicitly designated recipients and tracks each destination's delivery separately. This preserves partial outcomes in a fan-out rather than collapsing several deliveries into a single success that hides a missing recipient.</documentation>
