                <folder name="II.1.3.9.10.2.3 [Feature] Direct Submission Ingestion &amp; Delivery" id="id-63ba5fc40f0f481e8e2b55b8f65f427c">
                  <documentation>Continuum navigation coordinate: II.1.3.9.10.2.3. Navigation asserts no semantic containment. Occurrence: architectural; no additional architectural instance or semantic relationship. Canonical element directory: canonicalId=e8bfad88315c4833b6772ef580ca55a5; Exchange identifier=id-faf9309586445b52ad791069de388e1a. Existing governed hierarchy member; directory retained for leaves.</documentation>
                  <element xsi:type="archimate:Capability" name="[Feature] Direct Submission Ingestion &amp; Delivery" id="id-faf9309586445b52ad791069de388e1a" profiles="id-1fcc283b6cc74eab958ce9580eacd631">
                    <documentation>Support push submissions of clinical documents and messages across boundaries.

Direct submission supports a sender's deliberate push of information across an exchange boundary. It preserves the distinction between ingress or delivery acceptance and the recipient's business handling, under the actual contract rather than an assumed meaning of transport success.</documentation>
                    <property key="v0.2 / Source Capture Key" value="feature:direct-submission-ingestion--delivery"/>
