                  <element xsi:type="archimate:Capability" name="[Feature] Population Notification Obligation Tracking" id="id-b4ddb18a42815f51909df742fbb3f753" profiles="id-1fcc283b6cc74eab958ce9580eacd631">
                    <documentation>Track the relation between an applicable notification obligation, the supplied source evidence and observed notification disposition.

**Overview**

Sending a required notification and discharging the governing obligation are different assertions. This Feature keeps the explicit contract and indeterminate responses visible.

**Boundary**

Does not define notifiability, author statutory rules or own public-health response.

## Qualified relationship assertions

Original source predicates, evidence and qualifications remain in the metadata. The ARB has now adjudicated their native treatment; explicitly unestablished relationship existence remains excluded. Native representation does not promote source standing.

| Source predicate | Target element | Source standing / currentness | ARB native treatment |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| purpose_context | [[CT2] Population Health Information Reporting](../2135b45eab034370b0063b20e821985d.md) | Proposed / current | Association — `id-028a6c6895375c1ab108237b62dc7328` |</documentation>
