                <folder name="II.1.3.9.13.1.3 [Feature] Information Standards &amp; Semantic Governance" id="id-097e8d7864374e65a4a8eabd415ed432">
                  <documentation>Continuum navigation coordinate: II.1.3.9.13.1.3. Navigation asserts no semantic containment. Occurrence: architectural; no additional architectural instance or semantic relationship. Canonical element directory: canonicalId=af5d5249302f47ebb393c91afcc60392; Exchange identifier=id-40a0a237e02e58769e19d6c4f13cdf8d. Existing governed hierarchy member; directory retained for leaves.</documentation>
                  <element xsi:type="archimate:Capability" name="[Feature] Information Standards &amp; Semantic Governance" id="id-40a0a237e02e58769e19d6c4f13cdf8d" profiles="id-1fcc283b6cc74eab958ce9580eacd631">
                    <documentation>Govern canonical clinical data definitions, terminology bindings, and exchange profiles across regional systems.

Semantic governance provides canonical definitions, bindings and profiles through which regional representations can be understood consistently. Its purpose concerns meaning and constraints rather than a particular schema technology, and consuming a definition does not transfer its governing authority.</documentation>
                    <property key="v0.2 / Source Capture Key" value="feature:information-standards--semantic-governance"/>
                    <property key="v0.2 / Snapshot Reference ID" value="FEAT-ISE-27"/>
                    <property key="v0.2 / LaTeX Label" value="feature:feat-ise-27"/>
                    <property key="v0.2 / Construct Type" value="feature"/>
                    <property key="v0.2 / Capability Tier" value="FT"/>
                    <property key="v0.2 / Architectural Status" value="Canonical"/>
                    <property key="v0.2 / Record State" value="current"/>
