                <folder name="II.1.3.9.13.1.4 [Feature] Terminology Binding Governance" id="id-4f4921ae4d9f4028949879f3483fa462">
                  <documentation>Continuum navigation coordinate: II.1.3.9.13.1.4. Navigation asserts no semantic containment. Occurrence: architectural; no additional architectural instance or semantic relationship. Canonical element directory: canonicalId=b999df692ca64010b4adeedbcb0d3a5a; Exchange identifier=id-ebc8336c54825ec881877a648f360f9e. Existing governed hierarchy member; directory retained for leaves.</documentation>
                  <element xsi:type="archimate:Capability" name="[Feature] Terminology Binding Governance" id="id-ebc8336c54825ec881877a648f360f9e" profiles="id-1fcc283b6cc74eab958ce9580eacd631">
                    <documentation>Govern how information definitions are bound to applicable terminology and value sets.

**Overview**

Binding a data element to a vocabulary is distinct from resolving a patient code or changing the runtime membership of a dataset.

**Boundary**

Definition of a binding does not take external ontology authority or execute policy.</documentation>
