## ARB identity continuity

Historical identity [0bdd7f8c0cd74d9fabc49801af037fc2](0bdd7f8c0cd74d9fabc49801af037fc2.md) has direct correspondence with this capability under HCRL 1.1.5-002. Historical provenance and UUID reservation remain with that record; this resource retains its existing identity and independent standing.

## ARB source correspondence

Scope/anti-responsibility and clinical/operational meaning establish the responsible Capability; descriptive ledger/registry/asset labels do not establish a separately bounded formal Information Concept. Preserve non-transfer and source authority.

Source: `docs/markdown/03-business-architecture/information-responsibility/information-responsibility.md` — information responsibility row 37. Standing: Established Business responsibility only; formal information identity/lifecycle not inferred.

```text
| **Information Design Governance** | **Canonical Semantic Models &amp; Conformance Schemas** | Enterprise canonical semantic model definitions, data element dictionaries, terminology binding rules, exchange profiles, and semantic conformance constraint sets. | Does not own runtime instances of data. |
```</documentation>
