              <element xsi:type="archimate:Capability" name="[CT2] Information Protection &amp; Accountability Enablement" id="id-c72a309296ec5da68e55dc8ba1f8fcb7">
                <documentation>Apply information-use policy and preserve the accountability context needed for governed health-information activity.

**Overview**

Apply information-use policy and preserve the accountability context needed for governed health-information activity. Its constituent abilities distinguish Health Information Control.

**Intent**

Make information use both governed and explainable through policy, attributable rules and significant evidence.

**Boundary**

Patient directives remain with Client Privacy; runtime authorisation does not become external authentication or clinical authority.</documentation>
