                <element xsi:type="archimate:Capability" name="[CT3] Linked Information Curation" id="id-baf9aba95d5c539bab7fc75f6861f176">
                  <documentation>Curate associations to information and binary content needed to interpret and use a clinical record, retaining custody and source-authority distinctions.

**Overview**

Curate associations to information and binary content needed to interpret and use a clinical record, retaining custody and source-authority distinctions.

**Intent**

Curate associations to information and binary content needed to interpret and use a clinical record, retaining custody and source-authority distinctions.

**Boundary**

Association is not physical custody. Persistence authority, source clinical meaning and external repository authority remain separate.

## Qualified relationship assertions

Original source predicates, evidence and qualifications remain in the metadata. The ARB has now adjudicated their native treatment; explicitly unestablished relationship existence remains excluded. Native representation does not promote source standing.

| Source predicate | Target element | Source standing / currentness | ARB native treatment |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| enterprise_enabled_by | [[CT3] Binary Content Association &amp; Resolution](5314959509dc4b558711ec169ddee5a0.md) | Proposed / current | Serving (reverse) — `id-e74d7ffc670353ca825b78f774bb54ff` |

## ARB identity continuity

Historical identity [9d0925bb39664a5985cacf3cea7442d1](9d0925bb39664a5985cacf3cea7442d1.md) has direct correspondence with this capability under HCRL 1.1.5-002. Historical provenance and UUID reservation remain with that record; this resource retains its existing identity and independent standing.</documentation>
