                <element xsi:type="archimate:Capability" name="[CT3] Longitudinal Clinical Record Administration" id="id-dbb8a6f722f756808d5022cbd06aec85">
                  <documentation>Administer longitudinal record assembly, active clinical summaries and durable received/managed history with source attribution and supersession.

**Overview**

Administer longitudinal record assembly, active clinical summaries and durable received/managed history with source attribution and supersession. The reviewed hierarchy assigns this enduring ability to its stated business-enabling context.

**Intent**

Administer longitudinal record assembly, active clinical summaries and durable received/managed history with source attribution and supersession.

**Boundary**

Information administration and coordination preserve the authority of the responsible source, clinical actor and governed domain; they confer no additional real-world management authority.

## ARB identity continuity

Historical identity [bd91d848cf424c42bec7c80cd32edd28](bd91d848cf424c42bec7c80cd32edd28.md) has direct correspondence with this capability under HCRL 1.1.5-002. Historical provenance and UUID reservation remain with that record; this resource retains its existing identity and independent standing.</documentation>
