              <folder name="II.1.3.9.15.4 [CT3] Remote Patient Monitoring" id="id-cf560e58cf5447bebc57ec01ec23d396">
                <folder name="II.1.3.9.15.4.1 [Feature] Remote Telemetry Ingestion" id="id-8a32f30a73b74df996589796c03bfcc0">
                  <documentation>Continuum navigation coordinate: II.1.3.9.15.4.1. Navigation asserts no semantic containment. Occurrence: architectural; no additional architectural instance or semantic relationship. Canonical element directory: canonicalId=969dde193fab4c5d82d7dc210c7f5a71; Exchange identifier=id-67a6a7c637b55190abfa3b66d9cbdd28. Existing governed hierarchy member; directory retained for leaves.</documentation>
                  <element xsi:type="archimate:Capability" name="[Feature] Remote Telemetry Ingestion" id="id-67a6a7c637b55190abfa3b66d9cbdd28" profiles="id-1fcc283b6cc74eab958ce9580eacd631">
                    <documentation>Ingest home patient monitoring data, biometric telemetry, and patient-reported outcome measures (PROMs).

Remote telemetry ingestion accepts measurements and patient-reported contributions from outside the usual care site. The information can inform subsequent monitoring and interpretation, but acquisition alone does not establish clinical significance or authorise an intervention.</documentation>
