                <folder name="II.1.3.9.15.4.2 [Feature] Virtual Care Session Context Binding" id="id-bd76594c39e541cea993746e621d1cd3">
                  <documentation>Continuum navigation coordinate: II.1.3.9.15.4.2. Navigation asserts no semantic containment. Occurrence: architectural; no additional architectural instance or semantic relationship. Canonical element directory: canonicalId=c25d66fd6aff4299857eadc7c0243544; Exchange identifier=id-3135686eb16c5fabacc1675448e54251. Existing governed hierarchy member; directory retained for leaves.</documentation>
                  <element xsi:type="archimate:Capability" name="[Feature] Virtual Care Session Context Binding" id="id-3135686eb16c5fabacc1675448e54251" profiles="id-1fcc283b6cc74eab958ce9580eacd631">
                    <documentation>Associate synchronous virtual/telehealth consultations with the longitudinal health record and active care episode.

Virtual-session binding associates a consultation with the enduring record and the relevant episode. It preserves the clinical context across delivery modes without turning the communication session itself into proof of clinical conclusions or adequacy of care.</documentation>
