              <element xsi:type="archimate:Capability" name="[CT2] Workflow &amp; Activity Coordination" id="id-36d21ea7e98b5e1bbbddad25ba53cd4e">
                <documentation>Coordinate tasks entering or leaving the Harmonia execution boundary and work undertaken by other systems, with responsibility/destination routing, external status/traceability and governance of the completion bridge.

**Overview**

Coordinate tasks entering or leaving the Harmonia execution boundary and work undertaken by other systems, with responsibility/destination routing, external status/traceability and governance of the completion bridge. The reviewed hierarchy assigns this enduring ability to its stated business-enabling context.

**Intent**

Coordinate tasks entering or leaving the Harmonia execution boundary and work undertaken by other systems, with responsibility/destination routing, external status/traceability and governance of the completion bridge.

**Boundary**

External means outside Harmonia execution, potentially inside the same health organisation. Work coordination includes completion responsibilities and traceability; it is not generic interoperability or message routing.

## ARB identity continuity

Historical identity [4422d865978c4353ad575759c6026d27](4422d865978c4353ad575759c6026d27.md) has direct correspondence with this capability under HCRL 1.1.5-002. Historical provenance and UUID reservation remain with that record; this resource retains its existing identity and independent standing.

## ARB source correspondence

Scope/anti-responsibility and clinical/operational meaning establish the responsible Capability; descriptive ledger/registry/asset labels do not establish a separately bounded formal Information Concept. Preserve non-transfer and source authority.

Source: `docs/markdown/03-business-architecture/information-responsibility/information-responsibility.md` — information responsibility row 34. Standing: Established Business responsibility only; formal information identity/lifecycle not inferred.

```text
| **Workflow &amp; Activity Coordination** | **Generic Activity Instance Registry &amp; Timers** | Generic task state progression graphs, timer triggers, deadline escalation rules, and worklist queues across Work Orders, To Dos, and Synthetic Tasks. | Owns generic coordination semantics; does not own business meaning or clinical outcome. |
```</documentation>
