              <folder name="III.4.4.8.2.1 Integrate Mobile Work Management" id="id-1b87b8000ab4472f946a36e37e6c7c3e">
                <documentation>Continuum navigation coordinate: III.4.4.8.2.1. Navigation asserts no semantic containment. Occurrence: architectural; no additional architectural instance or semantic relationship. Canonical element directory: canonicalId=81f97ad819da48f09f26029066550e08; Exchange identifier=id-547d48631fb55c009ddbda0680ab5941. Existing governed hierarchy member; directory retained for leaves.</documentation>
                <element xsi:type="archimate:BusinessFunction" name="Integrate Mobile Work Management" id="id-547d48631fb55c009ddbda0680ab5941">
                  <documentation>Exchanges externally established work/assignment, dispatch and operational progression/status information, with applicable worker/context information, between mobile work-management mechanisms and Harmonia operational coordination.

Derivation and boundary: The human adjudication of FEAT-HSO-16 establishes integration with mobile work/task management. This responsibility is absent from presence observation and visit-specific milestone ingestion. It does not determine, allocate or manage the underlying clinical work, clinical handover or EMR worklists. Work Allocation &amp; Dispatch retains non-clinical operational Work Order responsibility.

