                <element xsi:type="archimate:BusinessService" name="Mandatory Audit Evidence Capture" id="id-94caf7d1a6c85f7a86c64db72c8cc84e">
                  <documentation>Allow governed-operation boundaries to require authoritative capture of significant activity evidence.

**Overview**

The client contract distinguishes confirmed capture from inability to capture, allowing required operations to fail closed.

**Boundary**

The exposed boundary does not permit callers to assign themselves audit platform authority.

## Qualified relationship assertions

Original source predicates, evidence and qualifications remain in the metadata. The ARB has now adjudicated their native treatment; explicitly unestablished relationship existence remains excluded. Native representation does not promote source standing.

| Source predicate | Target element | Source standing / currentness | ARB native treatment |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| uses_function | [Capture Required Significant Audit Evidence](../business-function/c8e614257cf14bd1878df894455f21fb.md) | Proposed / preserved historical assertion | Serving (reverse) — `id-bbd5d87ea1e65963a3e17979465cb4b0` |</documentation>
