            <folder name="IV.1.1.3.2 [Topic] OrganisationalUnit" id="id-60b7abe760b44eb6a353e5c1d27a2ae6">
              <documentation>Continuum navigation coordinate: IV.1.1.3.2. Navigation asserts no semantic containment. Occurrence: architectural; no additional architectural instance or semantic relationship. Canonical element directory: canonicalId=2c884cdd6a4b41a184818e3a7e540897; Exchange identifier=id-0235e0eaeafd42b683a53bacd2e40939. Existing governed hierarchy member; directory retained for leaves.</documentation>
              <element xsi:type="archimate:DataObject" name="[Topic] OrganisationalUnit" id="id-0235e0eaeafd42b683a53bacd2e40939" profiles="id-a8def6185ec847d6a729560440adb050">
                <documentation>**Description**
Information describing a defined subdivision of an organisation and its position within the organisation's structural context.

- **Semantic Classification**: `Entity / Administrative Subdivision`
- **Definition**: An identifiable internal division, clinical directorate, operational department, or specialty unit within a healthcare organisation (e.g. *Division of Surgery*, *Department of Cardiology*, *Pharmacy Department*).
- **Architectural Scope**: Represents structured administrative subdivisions that manage resources, staff, and services under the umbrella of the parent organisation.

Source standing: Established Package1 conceptual information meaning; residual qualifications in selected section remain unchanged.</documentation>
