            <folder name="IV.1.1.11.2 [Topic] Practitioner" id="id-dde0f1f0eeb74ce69a919b3728eae92f">
              <documentation>Continuum navigation coordinate: IV.1.1.11.2. Navigation asserts no semantic containment. Occurrence: architectural; no additional architectural instance or semantic relationship. Canonical element directory: canonicalId=4e8f2bd581a5418889813cf7ee414750; Exchange identifier=id-95d2d62cef524640b2be13f60236e2d6. Existing governed hierarchy member; directory retained for leaves.</documentation>
              <element xsi:type="archimate:DataObject" name="[Topic] Practitioner" id="id-95d2d62cef524640b2be13f60236e2d6" profiles="id-a8def6185ec847d6a729560440adb050">
                <documentation>**Definition**: An identifiable individual healthcare workforce or professional entity.

**Description**: Information describing an individual participating professionally in healthcare, independent of a particular organisational position, assignment or service context.

**Semantic Classification**: `Entity`

**Architectural Scope**: Represents the individual professional independently of statutory registration status. A `Practitioner` may be known to Harmonia prior to verification, when registration is pending or not applicable (e.g. unregistered healthcare workers, support staff), or when registration is externally authoritative.

**Boundary Rule**: $\text{Practitioner} \neq \text{Professional Registration}$. Registration is a governed assertion concerning a Practitioner, not the definition of the Practitioner entity itself.

Source standing: Established Package1 conceptual information meaning; residual qualifications in selected section remain unchanged.</documentation>
