            <folder name="IV.1.1.11.3 [Topic] PractitionerRole" id="id-2dd27d74f32a46b9bc38b2c3d2960024">
              <documentation>Continuum navigation coordinate: IV.1.1.11.3. Navigation asserts no semantic containment. Occurrence: architectural; no additional architectural instance or semantic relationship. Canonical element directory: canonicalId=cb7ac98f62aa4599ba57263338cb8b3c; Exchange identifier=id-5cd100ca4e5846df934b20e77c862c46. Existing governed hierarchy member; directory retained for leaves.</documentation>
              <element xsi:type="archimate:DataObject" name="[Topic] PractitionerRole" id="id-5cd100ca4e5846df934b20e77c862c46" profiles="id-a8def6185ec847d6a729560440adb050">
                <documentation>**Definition**: The contextual binding of a `Practitioner` to a specific clinical capacity, service, facility, or department within an organisation (e.g. *Specialist Physician in Cardiology Department*, *On-Call Registrar*).

**Description**: Information describing the contextual relationship between a practitioner and the organisation, service, location or role through which they participate in healthcare delivery.

**Semantic Classification**: `Contextual Binding`

**Key Characteristics**: Contextual title/role, participating organisation, participating healthcare service, physical practice locations, active schedule, and linked communication endpoints.

Source standing: Established Package1 conceptual information meaning; residual qualifications in selected section remain unchanged.</documentation>
                <property key="Baseline / Source Path" value="docs/markdown/04-information-architecture/information-families/practitioner.md"/>
                <property key="Baseline / Source Section" value="### 3.6 Practitioner Role Binding"/>
