              <documentation>- **Role/responsibility:** management/governance of foundational models, definitions
  and mutable datasets, including first-class Security and Assurance Nomenclature
  and authoritative review of ontology sets for Harmonia use. [U13](../../../../docs/markdown/05-information-systems-architecture/sources.md#u13),
  [canonical Calliope view](../../../../docs/markdown/05-information-systems-architecture/calliope-models-and-datasets.md).
- **Distinct submodules:** **Calliope-Models C41** supplies design/build-time
  Models, Metadata Types, Criteria Definitions, Topics, Filter Types, Filter Elements,
  core Harmonia element libraries and security/assurance definitions.
  **Calliope-DataSets C42** manages runtime mutable ValueSets, CodeSets, Structured
  Metadata and applicable governed ontology content. No common lifecycle or
  undifferentiated metadata repository is inferred.
- **Authority:** development representations support type-safe human/IDE/AI-assisted
  programming; current membership/content uses runtime authority. Models/build
  definitions establish structural access contracts; DataSets do not bootstrap them.
  Definition ownership confers neither runtime execution nor originating clinical authority.
- **Persistence/collaboration:** DataSets uses established Mneme/Mnemosyne
  responsibilities; Calliope is not a Persistence Manager. Governed workflow may
  reuse Ponos/Ergo/Praxis, without another engine or detailed management UI.
  Themis decides/enforces, Dokimasia assures and Kleio audits.
- **Standing:** U13 settles the two responsibilities, not their packaging, runtime
  ontology boundary or representation/workflow mechanisms (CDG-24/49). Existing
  pure-library dependency constraints apply to Models; U15 resolves the
  [realisation boundary](../../../../docs/markdown/05-information-systems-architecture/calliope-models-and-datasets.md#calliope-realisation).
  General converter-support
  versus activity allocation remains CDG-05; no terminology product is selected.

&lt;a id=&quot;authorisation-nomenclature&quot;>&lt;/a>

#### Controlled authorisation nomenclature

[U12](../../../../docs/markdown/05-information-systems-architecture/sources.md#u12) establishes these **release-bounded ValueSets**:

| ValueSet | Architectural shorthand / meaning |
| :--- | :--- |
| `Application.Function.AuthorisationPoint.Names` | **Function.Name**: architecturally significant application AuthorisationPoints at which enforcement is meaningful. An AuthorisationPoint identifies a governed function; it is not itself a permission. |
| `Application.Function.AllowedAction.Names` | **Function.Scope**: the bounded set of actions applicable at AuthorisationPoints. Existing concepts include **ACCESS**, **CHANGE** and **FORWARD**; these are not asserted to be the complete final ValueSet. |
| `Information.Compartments` | Governed information compartments; an applicable dimension is expressed as **Information.Compartment**. |
| `Information.Classification` | Governed information classifications. |

`Application.Function.AuthorisationPoint.Names` SHALL be comprehensive enough
to satisfy business security requirements for the release while constrained
enough to avoid unnecessary management, development and support burden.
Complete release-specific contents remain [deferred](../../../../docs/markdown/05-information-systems-architecture/gaps.md#identity-deferred-design).

**Calliope defines/governs the nomenclature. Themis owns policy association,
resolution and enforcement.** ValueSet membership alone grants no authority
and does not establish every Cartesian combination as meaningful or permitted.

The controlled vocabularies fall within [Calliope-DataSets](466ad8f75a954c0581b5bba090443849.md);
their structural definitions/contracts belong to Calliope-Models. This allocation
does not reopen U12 or permit unrestricted runtime changes to release-bounded
content; detailed release/change rules remain deferred.

## Source-qualified contribution

Source: `docs/markdown/05-information-systems-architecture/context-and-persistence-management.md` — ## Calliope and Pylai use of established responsibilities. Standing: Candidate — adjudicated Domain05 Step-B baseline; final Solution Architecture unapproved.

[Calliope-DataSets](53bf6815c7a54ed0abde9b1aad311843.md) owns governed
mutable content and uses established Mneme/Mnemosyne access/persistence; this
adds no persistence manager or Mneme service. Models/build definitions supply
structural contracts independently of runtime DataSet availability.

[PylaiServer READ/SEARCH](../../../../docs/markdown/05-information-systems-architecture/pylai-external-interoperability.md#pylai-server-controller)
uses Diadromí-Controller → Mneme Adhoc Resource Access / Adhoc Search → Mnemosyne
as needed. Mneme remains the Context and Pragma Manager with four exposed services,
not a generic Information Manager or external interoperability service. No
ActionableTask/Praxis/Ergon is fabricated for this read-oriented pattern.

[PylaiPathway ingress](../../../../docs/markdown/05-information-systems-architecture/pylai-external-interoperability.md#pylai-pathway-ingress)
establishes initial Task.input/Context through a specialised Ergo ContextLoader;
semantic mapping remains in BusinessLogic. EgressHoros returns communication
state/outcome before ContextUnloader completes. Neither Loader/Unloader nor Pylai
establishes durable truth. Protocol success, engine success and authoritative
Harmonia persistence outcome remain distinct, including uncertainty.

## Source-qualified contribution

Source: `docs/markdown/05-information-systems-architecture/calliope-models-and-datasets.md` — ## Responsibility and decomposition. Standing: Candidate — adjudicated Domain05 Step-B baseline; final Solution Architecture unapproved.

Calliope manages and governs Harmonia's foundational Models, Metadata Types,
Criteria Definitions, Topics, Filter Types, Filter Elements, ValueSets, CodeSets,
Structured Metadata, core Harmonia element libraries, and Security and Assurance
Nomenclature. It also owns authoritative review/governance of ontology sets for
Harmonia use. That review does not make Harmonia the originating authority for
externally governed ontologies.

The B1 conceptual
[`Metabolē.Context.ActivityContext` vocabulary](../../business/business-object/c34b4929f71946708d37dbe6c1da920a.md)
is governed consistently with this shared definition/model/nomenclature
responsibility. It classifies the broad activity, separately from a request action
or authorisation permission. The initial examples are not an exhaustive enum;
this establishes no physical Models/DataSets allocation. Runtime policy
resolution, authorisation decisions and enforcement remain Themis responsibilities.

```text
Calliope
  +-- Calliope-Models     design/build-time governed knowledge
  `-- Calliope-DataSets   runtime management of mutable governed content
```

These are distinct logical submodules with different lifecycles and dependency
characteristics. They SHALL NOT be collapsed into one undifferentiated metadata
repository. Their names establish no Maven artefacts, processes, databases or
deployment boundaries. The [realisation boundary](../../../../docs/markdown/05-information-systems-architecture/calliope-models-and-datasets.md#calliope-realisation) separates
Models' library dependencies from DataSets' runtime collaboration.

&lt;a id=&quot;calliope-realisation&quot;>&lt;/a>

### Library dependency and runtime management

> **Calliope-Models provides development/build-time library dependencies.
> Calliope-DataSets provides runtime management and authoritative access to
> mutable governed datasets.**

The existence of DataSets does not alter Models' library/dependency semantics
and does not make Calliope a persistence manager. Repository pure-library and
zero-higher-layer-dependency constraints apply to Models; they do not restrict
all logical Calliope responsibilities to libraries. DataSets collaborates through
established Mneme/Mnemosyne access and persistence. No new static dependency or
physical allocation is inferred from that runtime collaboration.

```text
Calliope
  +-- Calliope-Models
  |     design / code / build-time model and library dependency
  `-- Calliope-DataSets
        runtime governed dataset management / authoritative content access
          ↓
        Mneme / Mnemosyne access and persistence

Concept / structural contract       → Calliope-Models
Current governed membership/content → Calliope-DataSets
```

> **Build-time representation and runtime authority are complementary, not
> competing, responsibilities.**

Strategy's library/local-evaluation statements concern Models. Calliope is not
a mandatory mediator of every runtime transaction; current governed content may
require DataSets runtime resolution. Packaging, APIs and other mechanisms remain
[deferred](../../../../docs/markdown/05-information-systems-architecture/gaps.md#calliope-contracts).

## Source-qualified contribution

Source: `docs/markdown/05-information-systems-architecture/calliope-models-and-datasets.md` — ## Build-time knowledge and runtime authority. Standing: Candidate — adjudicated Domain05 Step-B baseline; final Solution Architecture unapproved.

> **Build-time Calliope knowledge assists software development; runtime Calliope
> authority determines validity and current governed membership/content.**

Calliope SHALL provide development-time representations of known runtime-managed
DataSets, CodeSets and ValueSets sufficient for efficient human, IDE-assisted and
AI-assisted software development. Such representations can support type safety,
code completion, documentation, static analysis and testing, with stable identity,
meaning, constraints, known build-time values and runtime-resolution contracts.

> **Development-time knowledge SHALL NOT be treated as authoritative evidence of
> current runtime membership or content.**

> **Development-time representation SHALL NOT require developers to sacrifice
> normal type-safe/code-assisted programming merely because a dataset is runtime
> mutable.**

A runtime value is not invalid merely because an earlier build did not know it.
Conversely, earlier software need not contain value-specific business behaviour
for later additions. Validation/membership uses current governed runtime authority;
the generated-code, IDE, AI-tooling and runtime access mechanisms remain deferred.

Structural contracts for accessing/managing DataSets SHALL derive from
Calliope-Models and the software build/deployment lifecycle. Runtime DataSets
provide mutable content under those contracts; they SHALL NOT bootstrap the
structural contracts required for their own access. This separates foundational
software dependency from runtime collaboration with Mneme, Mnemosyne and Ponos.

## Source-qualified contribution

Source: `docs/markdown/05-information-systems-architecture/calliope-models-and-datasets.md` — ## Security and Assurance Nomenclature. Standing: Candidate — adjudicated Domain05 Step-B baseline; final Solution Architecture unapproved.

Calliope has first-class responsibility for the definition, governance and
authoritative representation of shared security, privacy, policy, audit and
assurance nomenclature. This is broader than incidental storage of security
ValueSets.

```text
Calliope    defines / governs nomenclature
Themis      decides / enforces
Dokimasia   assures
Kleio       audits
```

| Calliope-Models illustrative definitions | Calliope-DataSets illustrative governed content |
| :--- | :--- |
| SecurityClassificationType | SecurityClassification ValueSet |
| CompartmentMetadataType | Compartment CodeSet / ValueSet |
| AssuranceFindingType | AssuranceFindingCategory ValueSet |
| CriteriaDefinition / DecisionReasonType | DisclosurePurpose CodeSet / AssuranceSeverity ValueSet |

Examples do not establish a final catalogue, schema or release inventory.
The four [U12 release-bounded authorisation ValueSets](../../../../docs/markdown/05-information-systems-architecture/component-register.md#authorisation-nomenclature)
are Calliope-controlled vocabularies:

- `Application.Function.AuthorisationPoint.Names`;
- `Application.Function.AllowedAction.Names`;
- `Information.Compartments`;
- `Information.Classification`.

Their controlled content belongs to the DataSets responsibility, while their
structural definitions/contracts belong to Models. Release-bounded scope does
not establish unrestricted runtime mutation of these particular ValueSets;
release-specific contents and detailed change/version rules remain deferred.
Themis owns their authorisation-policy association, role/Criteria resolution and
enforcement. Membership alone grants no authority. U12's Criterion conjunction,
additive UNION grants, temporal/revocation and local PEP semantics remain intact.
Calliope does not acquire policy decisions, assurance assessment or Audit Capture.
Kleio's [mandatory capture authority](../../../../docs/markdown/05-information-systems-architecture/component-register.md#kleio-capture-authority)
is governed intrinsic platform authority, separate from the originating
Identity's authorisation and from nomenclature ownership.

## Source-qualified contribution

Source: `docs/markdown/05-information-systems-architecture/calliope-models-and-datasets.md` — ## Deferred design and review boundary. Standing: Candidate — adjudicated Domain05 Step-B baseline; final Solution Architecture unapproved.

The exact runtime ontology-management boundary, originating terminology-authority
relationships, ontology-review/update/synchronisation lifecycle, DataSet lifecycle,
version/effective-date and historical retention rules remain unresolved. So do
the relationship of historical Context to later DataSet versions, detailed
DataSet workflow, human-management UI, exact development representations/tooling,
runtime APIs, physical packaging, caching, persistence structures and final
security/assurance catalogue. Complete release-specific ValueSet contents remain
deferred under U12.

[CDG-24/49](../../../../docs/markdown/05-information-systems-architecture/gaps.md#calliope-contracts) distinguishes the now-established runtime
management responsibility from these open details and from proposed clinical
terminology/authoring services. Domain03 clinical-knowledge behaviour is not
automatically allocated wholesale to Calliope. No Domain04 Information Family or
capability coverage is inferred by this consolidation.

