## ARB DesignNote assertion contributions

These bounded source assertions are reconciled under the cited U-decisions and ARB release Praxis. They retain the source's candidate, scope and detailed-design qualifications. They do not accept the whole Domain05 candidate or create a new element per paragraph. Later-corrected assertions are retained in the disposition evidence instead of being restored here.

### DesignNote-Digital-Twin-Behaviour-and-Execution-Semantics — original lines 211-212

Source: `docs/markdown/05-information-systems-architecture/design-notes/DesignNote-Digital-Twin-Behaviour-and-Execution-Semantics.md`; U19; source-qualified assertion, current subject standing unchanged.

Each Behaviour has its own **Praxis-defined Context requirements**. Mneme loads
Context fresh when that Behaviour begins, and manages its Context Save:

### DesignNote-Digital-Twin-Behaviour-and-Execution-Semantics — original lines 222-227

Source: `docs/markdown/05-information-systems-architecture/design-notes/DesignNote-Digital-Twin-Behaviour-and-Execution-Semantics.md`; U19; source-qualified assertion, current subject standing unchanged.

On the normal path, Behaviour B's Context is loaded **after A has completed and
saved its information consequences**; C's is loaded after B, and so forth.
Progression after failure remains subject to section 10. Later Behaviours may
therefore observe authoritative information consequences established by earlier Behaviours.
There is **no single immutable input-level Context snapshot** shared by all
interested Behaviours.

### DesignNote-Digital-Twin-Behaviour-and-Execution-Semantics — original lines 229-235

Source: `docs/markdown/05-information-systems-architecture/design-notes/DesignNote-Digital-Twin-Behaviour-and-Execution-Semantics.md`; U19; source-qualified assertion, current subject standing unchanged.

Praxis defines required Context; Mneme retains Context management, materialisation
and save. Normal [Loader/Unloader versus Load/Save boundaries](../../../../docs/markdown/05-information-systems-architecture/context-and-persistence-management.md#ergon-information-access)
apply. Mnemosyne alone establishes authoritative durable state; working changes
and Context Save invocation do not manufacture confirmed persistence outcomes.
Existing exceptional harmonisation and AX-15 uncertainty semantics remain intact.
This note adds no cross-Behaviour transaction, universal globally consistent
snapshot or conflict-resolution mechanism.

