### DesignNote-Digital-Twin-Behaviour-and-Execution-Semantics — original lines 122-125

Source: `docs/markdown/05-information-systems-architecture/design-notes/DesignNote-Digital-Twin-Behaviour-and-Execution-Semantics.md`; U19; source-qualified assertion, current subject standing unchanged.

Ordinary Ergon processing matches semantic interest in an ActionableTask and
establishes a separate FulfillmentTask for each interested Ergon undertaking.
Twin processing analogously matches Behaviour interest and derives the
corresponding BehaviourStimulus or BehaviourEffector.

### DesignNote-Digital-Twin-Behaviour-and-Execution-Semantics — original lines 143-146

Source: `docs/markdown/05-information-systems-architecture/design-notes/DesignNote-Digital-Twin-Behaviour-and-Execution-Semantics.md`; U19; source-qualified assertion, current subject standing unchanged.

**Diagram A:** fan-out shows semantic interest and Behaviour realisation, not
concurrent execution. The equivalence is semantic and architectural. It implies
neither inheritance nor identical information types, and does not establish
Stimulus/Effector processing through ActionableTask/FulfillmentTask.

### DesignNote-Energeia-DigitalTwin-Dokimasia-Specialisation — original lines 21-21

Source: `docs/markdown/05-information-systems-architecture/design-notes/DesignNote-Energeia-DigitalTwin-Dokimasia-Specialisation.md`; U02/U06/U19; source-qualified assertion, current subject standing unchanged.

**Ergo** establishes the reusable conceptual activity pattern and platform-integration contract for conforming Ergon. This includes Context Loading/Unloading and standard integration points/placeholders for Petasos adapters, assurance services, logging/observability, checkpoints and other platform integration. Ergo is not the execution framework; Ponos is.

### DesignNote-Energeia-DigitalTwin-Dokimasia-Specialisation — original lines 23-23

Source: `docs/markdown/05-information-systems-architecture/design-notes/DesignNote-Energeia-DigitalTwin-Dokimasia-Specialisation.md`; U02/U06/U19; source-qualified assertion, current subject standing unchanged.

**Ergon** is a single, well-defined software component encapsulating a bounded, fine-grained task-completion activity set. It supplies specialised activity/business behaviour within the Ergo boundary and is executed/managed through Ponos. An Ergon has no discrete Information Architecture representation merely because it is an Ergon.

### DesignNote-Energeia-DigitalTwin-Dokimasia-Specialisation — original lines 25-25

Source: `docs/markdown/05-information-systems-architecture/design-notes/DesignNote-Energeia-DigitalTwin-Dokimasia-Specialisation.md`; U02/U06/U19; source-qualified assertion, current subject standing unchanged.

**Erga** is a meaningful collection of Ergon for: (a) collating components into executable hubs; (b) capturing/observing activity where multiple concurrent Ergon, including instances of the same type, may execute; and (c) libraries of conceptually related Ergon suitably constrained for coherent change-management, testing, versioning and release. Erga is not merely an informal plural or List&lt;Ergon>.

### DesignNote-Energeia-DigitalTwin-Dokimasia-Specialisation — original lines 63-63

Source: `docs/markdown/05-information-systems-architecture/design-notes/DesignNote-Energeia-DigitalTwin-Dokimasia-Specialisation.md`; U02/U06/U19; source-qualified assertion, current subject standing unchanged.

