        <element xsi:type="archimate:Driver" name="Durable Clinical Information Independence" id="id-78d8fa44cc7452fea57041c8a2b8b102">
          <documentation>### Context &amp; Pressure
Clinical information must remain intelligible, authoritative, and actionable across a patient's entire lifetime (often 80+ years). In contrast, commercial Electronic Medical Record (EMR) software products, proprietary database schemas, and integration broker technologies have commercial lifecycles of only 5 to 10 years.

When healthcare networks store longitudinal patient data exclusively inside proprietary EMR schemas, they suffer severe vendor lock-in, exorbitant data extraction fees, and the perpetual risk of data obsolescence during vendor transitions.

### Architectural Imperative
Harmonia must establish durable clinical information independence. Patient health data managed by Harmonia must exist as a vendor-neutral, sovereign regional asset. The clinical representation must outlive the commercial life of any individual software vendor, database engine, or middleware framework.

- **Primary Stakeholders**: [Clinicians &amp; Care Teams](../../../../docs/markdown/01-motivation/stakeholders/enterprise-stakeholders.md), [Healthcare Delivery Organizations](../../../../docs/markdown/01-motivation/stakeholders/enterprise-stakeholders.md)
- **Associated Goal**: [Vendor-Independent Longitudinal Clinical Information Coherence](../../../../docs/markdown/01-motivation/goals-outcomes/strategic-goals.md)
- **Governing Axioms**: [AX-01 (Health-Information Centricity)](../principle/e9bd61acaaea4577bc4086a5639e52c3.md), [AX-06 (Explicit Information Authority)](../principle/952c3b6148ce4fce94b69f99a0c2fec7.md)</documentation>
          <property key="Baseline / Record State" value="current"/>
          <property key="Baseline / Architectural Status" value="Agreed"/>
          <property key="Baseline / Source Path" value="docs/markdown/01-motivation/drivers-assessments/drivers.md"/>
