        <element xsi:type="archimate:Principle" name="Separation of Transport from Business Logic" id="id-3c030f45802c59fc9991284d29cb5808">
          <documentation>The messaging framework (Petasos) treats all payloads as opaque byte arrays. Transport routes are unaware of clinical schemas. Transformation logic is strictly isolated in modular task activities (Erga).

## ARB source correspondence

Catalogue explicitly classifies transport/business separation as Application Layering Pattern. Historical opaque-Petasos/modular-Erga principle records this bounded concern; no new Requirement is allocated or current Principle approval inferred.

Source: `docs/markdown/01-motivation/requirements-constraints/master-requirements-catalogue.md` — catalogue row APP-SEP-001. Standing: Candidate handoff; Historical / Reclassified pattern retained.

```text
| **APP-SEP-001** | Transport / Business Separation | Domain 05 (App) / Domain 06 (Integration) | [AX-02](../../governance/architectural-axioms.md#ax-02), [AX-04](../../governance/architectural-axioms.md#ax-04) | [Clinical Interoperability](../drivers-assessments/drivers.md) | Application Layering Pattern | **Candidate** |
```</documentation>
