\section{Consent and unresolved conflicts}
Preserved; restriction/filter/disclosure references the existing client-associated responsibility. No duplicate consent capability introduced. \nameref{cap:bec-client-privacy}.


HUMAN ADJUDICATION REQUIRED: reviewed name Health Information Exchange duplicates the Canonical BC name under CM-R05. The existing BEC display qualification is retained; reviewed\_name records the exact task wording. Identities and BC/\allowbreak{}BEC semantics remain distinct.

\par\textbf{HUMAN ADJUDICATION REQUIRED:} \nameref{cap:bec-credential-management} (p.\,\pageref{cap:bec-credential-management}). Canonical operational badges/physical-access credentials are distinct from reviewed clinical-service credential definitions.
\par\textbf{HUMAN ADJUDICATION REQUIRED:} \nameref{cap:bec-health-information-communication} (p.\,\pageref{cap:bec-health-information-communication}). Canonical boundary protocol mediation and technical transmission are distinct from reviewed patient-facing communication.
\par\textbf{HUMAN ADJUDICATION REQUIRED:} \nameref{cap:bec-workflow-activity-coordination} (p.\,\pageref{cap:bec-workflow-activity-coordination}). Canonical internal Work Order, To Do and synthetic Task progression is broader than the reviewed external execution-boundary bridge.
\par\textbf{HUMAN ADJUDICATION REQUIRED:} \nameref{cap:bec-governed-assurance} (p.\,\pageref{cap:bec-governed-assurance}). Canonical assurance against a governed subject is not independent review of the assurance service itself.
\par\textbf{HUMAN ADJUDICATION REQUIRED:} \nameref{cap:bec-independent-assurance-evaluation-enablement} (p.\,\pageref{cap:bec-independent-assurance-evaluation-enablement}). The previous grouping frames Canonical subject-assurance execution; it cannot be equated with review of the assurance service itself.
\par\textbf{HUMAN ADJUDICATION REQUIRED:} \nameref{cap:bec-information-authority-representation} (p.\,\pageref{cap:bec-information-authority-representation}). Source credibility and authority standing require an explicit home; information-asset tags alone do not establish that responsibility.
\par\textbf{HUMAN ADJUDICATION REQUIRED:} \nameref{cap:bec-significant-activity-audit-capture} (p.\,\pageref{cap:bec-significant-activity-audit-capture}). The reviewed hierarchy does not allocate general mandatory authoritative audit capture; disclosure or provenance alone is not an equivalent responsibility.
\par\textbf{HUMAN ADJUDICATION REQUIRED:} \nameref{cap:bec-governance-requirement-publication-support} (p.\,\pageref{cap:bec-governance-requirement-publication-support}). Requirement publication/authority is not assurance-service review or information-model design; the reviewed hierarchy does not allocate a home.
\par\textbf{HUMAN ADJUDICATION REQUIRED:} \nameref{cap:bec-entity-specific-operational-coordination} (p.\,\pageref{cap:bec-entity-specific-operational-coordination}). Internal entity-relative progression is not the reviewed external work bridge; a current BEC destination has not been adjudicated.
\par\textbf{HUMAN ADJUDICATION REQUIRED:} \nameref{cap:bec-governed-operational-activity-design} (p.\,\pageref{cap:bec-governed-operational-activity-design}). Internal execution-envelope design is distinct from governance of work across an external execution boundary.
\par\textbf{HUMAN ADJUDICATION REQUIRED:} \nameref{cap:bec-service-offering-readiness-coordination} (p.\,\pageref{cap:bec-service-offering-readiness-coordination}). Dependency evidence material retained at the out-of-scope CT1. A proposed determination of collective go/no-go readiness is not inherited as authority by dependency tracking.
\section{Complete predecessor ledger}
Identity-level decisions, predecessor identities, semantic distributions, every changed structural ID and direct alias, and Feature/behaviour ancestry changes are retained in bec-reconciliation-ledger.json and the task report. The historical entries preserve their exact pre-review records.
