\cataloguefield{subsubsection}{Capability Overview}

Care-Team Coordination maintains the participating team context and collaboration around care. It supports continuity by making participation intelligible across people and organisational boundaries, without assuming that membership itself assigns every clinical responsibility. Within Care Coordination \&amp; Transition it concerns collaboration around care rather than proof of a responsibility handoff.


\cataloguefield{subsubsection}{Definition / governed semantic detail}

Coordinate participating care-team context and collaboration around care.


\cataloguefield{subsubsection}{Boundary}

Harmonia's support for team information and collaboration does not confer management of clinical handover or clinical worklists.


\Needspace{8\baselineskip}
