\cataloguefield{subsubsection}{Capability Overview}

Collective readiness is an access prerequisite and has a coherent proposed preparedness frame; it is not reduced to capacity, resource state or service alignment.


\cataloguefield{subsubsection}{Semantic elaboration — Proposed}

Establish collective operational readiness of a service offering in a site or session context from its applicable dependencies.


\cataloguefield{subsubsection}{Boundary — v0.1 explanation}

Tier, parent and CT1 ancestry remain unresolved. Site-level and session-level exercises do not establish separate capabilities, and no convenient parent is allocated here.


\cataloguefield{subsubsection}{Boundary}

The element remains Candidate. The definition/\allowbreak{}placement elaboration is Proposed and does not adjudicate the unresolved RAD question or transfer source-domain authority.


\cataloguefield{subsubsection}{Alternative Considered / Review Note}

Health Service Direction \&amp; Stewardship is plausible for standing site/\allowbreak{}service readiness; access-oriented placement is chosen to retain the deliverability question.


\cataloguefield{subsubsection}{Review Confidence}
Low; applies to the proposal, not to preserved canonical meaning.
\cataloguefield{subsubsection}{Preserved v0.1 Review Matters}

OI-BC-002: collective service-readiness meaning is identified, but tier/\allowbreak{}CT2 parent/\allowbreak{}CT1 ancestry and placement remain unresolved.


