\cataloguefield{subsubsection}{Capability Overview}

Maintenance/\allowbreak{}restoration is materially distinct from overall lifecycle disposition and monitoring; include the Candidate concern as a proposed eighth CT3.


\cataloguefield{subsubsection}{Semantic elaboration — Proposed}

Maintain or restore acceptable device condition through testing, calibration, inspection, maintenance and repair.


\cataloguefield{subsubsection}{Boundary — v0.1 explanation}

Membership, tier and ancestry require adjudication; this description does not establish an eighth Clinical Technology Management child.


\cataloguefield{subsubsection}{Boundary}

The element remains Candidate. The definition/\allowbreak{}placement elaboration is Proposed and does not adjudicate the unresolved RAD question or transfer source-domain authority.


\cataloguefield{subsubsection}{Alternative Considered / Review Note}

The seven-child adjudicated set omits it. Membership remains Candidate rather than silently amending that approved set.


\cataloguefield{subsubsection}{Review Confidence}
Low; applies to the proposal, not to preserved canonical meaning.
\cataloguefield{subsubsection}{Preserved v0.1 Review Matters}

DN-BC-015 defines maintenance separately but omits it from its explicit seven-child CT3 set; inclusion/\allowbreak{}tier/\allowbreak{}ancestry requires adjudication.


