\cataloguefield{subsubsection}{Capability Overview}

Clinical Knowledge Publication \&amp; Sharing makes approved knowledge available to applicable authorised consumers and contexts. It preserves the standing and limits under which knowledge was approved rather than reducing publication to unrestricted dissemination. Its contribution is availability for appropriate use, distinct from both approval and the individual clinical application that may follow.


\cataloguefield{subsubsection}{Definition / governed semantic detail}

Make approved knowledge available to applicable authorised consumers and use contexts.


\cataloguefield{subsubsection}{Boundary}

Published knowledge is not a patient-specific conclusion, decision or instruction merely because a clinician can access it.


\chapter{BC CT1: Standards, Semantics \&amp; Reference Governance}
\label{cap:bc-standards-semantics-reference-governance}
