\cataloguefield{section}{Capability Overview}

This capability establishes confidence in identity, coherent control of access, protection of information and accountability for its use. Its three branches distinguish identity/\allowbreak{}access governance, protection and privacy, and attribution/\allowbreak{}accountability. The scope includes physical and procedural arrangements as well as digital controls, preventing a software authorisation check from standing in for the organisation's whole trust responsibility.


\cataloguefield{section}{Definition / governed semantic detail}

Establish adequate identity confidence, coherent access controls, privacy/\allowbreak{}protection safeguards, governed activity attribution and accountability for security-relevant activity and information use.


\cataloguefield{section}{Intent}

Support information use and governed activity within legitimate identity, authority, privacy and protection constraints.


\cataloguefield{section}{Boundary}

Identifying an actor, permitting an action, recording participation and judging appropriateness are different outcomes. Evidence production is not itself independent assurance.


\cataloguefield{section}{Harmonia Architectural Relevance}

Security and governance are intrinsic to Harmonia-managed operations. The Core classification concerns assigned platform controls and evidence; it does not acquire every organisational security or privacy responsibility.


\cataloguefield{section}{Scope / Contained Elements}
