\cataloguefield{subsubsection}{Capability Overview}

Governed Activity Attribution preserves who participated and in what acting capacity, together with the relevant permission, authority and constraint context. It makes conduct explainable beyond a bare actor identifier and timestamp. Within Digital Accountability \&amp; Trust, this supplies the contextual record needed to distinguish participation from entitlement.


\cataloguefield{subsubsection}{Definition / governed semantic detail}

Preserve who participated, what was done, the attributable person/\allowbreak{}role/\allowbreak{}unit/\allowbreak{}organisation capacity and applicable permission/\allowbreak{}authority/\allowbreak{}constraint context.


\cataloguefield{subsubsection}{Boundary — v0.1 explanation}

Attributing an action to a person or role does not establish that the action was permitted or appropriate.


