\cataloguefield{section}{Capability Overview}

This capability frames the deliberately bounded research and innovation responsibilities material to Harmonia's R1/\allowbreak{}R2 architecture. Research Information Support concerns provision of existing information for authorised research; Health Innovation concerns evaluation of proposed or emerging innovation. These establish useful enterprise context without implying a complete research organisation or innovation lifecycle.


\cataloguefield{section}{Definition / governed semantic detail}

Provide existing health information for authorised research under applicable constraints and evaluate health innovation; deliberately under-decomposed for R1/\allowbreak{}R2.


\cataloguefield{section}{Intent}

Support legitimate research information needs and informed consideration of changes to health-service or clinical practice.


\cataloguefield{section}{Boundary}

Information provision does not own trials, ethics approval or specialist research analysis. Evaluating innovation does not authorise adoption or implementation.


\cataloguefield{section}{Harmonia Architectural Relevance}

Governed provision of existing information materially enables authorised research. Innovation evaluation has no separate platform assignment; the CT1 classification must not be inherited by each descendant.


