\cataloguefield{subsubsection}{Capability Overview}

Policy /\allowbreak{} Obligation Governance establishes and maintains the authoritative requirements under which the organisation operates. It interprets applicable legislative, regulatory, contractual, policy and other sources while preserving traceability to their authority. The purpose is a legitimate account of what must be satisfied, rather than an operational choice about how to satisfy it.


\cataloguefield{subsubsection}{Definition / governed semantic detail}

Identify, interpret, establish and maintain authoritative legislative, regulatory, policy, standards, guideline, contractual and other obligations, attributable and traceable to source authority.


\cataloguefield{subsubsection}{Boundary}

Interpreting obligations does not acquire the regulator's authority or determine operational means.


\Needspace{8\baselineskip}
