\cataloguefield{subsubsection}{Capability Overview}

This capability specifies where adherence must be checked and what governance or compliance information must be reported. It gives the governance framework observable expectations without treating reporting requirements as completed reporting. Within Compliance Governance it complements the assessment basis by making checking and communication obligations explicit.


\cataloguefield{subsubsection}{Definition / governed semantic detail}

Establish where/\allowbreak{}how adherence is checked and what governance/\allowbreak{}compliance information must be reported.


\cataloguefield{subsubsection}{Boundary}

Defining a checkpoint does not perform the check or take over progression of the governed operation.


\chapter{BC CT1: Health Service Assurance}
\label{cap:bc-health-service-assurance}
\index{Health Service Assurance}
\begingroup\small\setlength{\TableWidth}{\dimexpr\linewidth-6\tabcolsep-4\arrayrulewidth\relax}
\begin{longtable}{|>{\raggedright\arraybackslash}p{0.2\TableWidth}|>{\raggedright\arraybackslash}p{0.48\TableWidth}|>{\raggedright\arraybackslash}p{0.32\TableWidth}|}
