\cataloguefield{subsection}{Capability Overview}

Client Administration provides the representation and demographic context needed to recognise individuals receiving care. It brings identity, healthcare-subject context, relationships and privacy into the same administrative frame while preserving their different responsibilities. The established partial chain to Person Identity is retained; the catalogue's other contextual descriptions do not supply a complete capability hierarchy.


\cataloguefield{subsection}{Definition — Reviewed candidate}

Client Administration provides the representation and demographic context needed to recognise individuals receiving care. It brings identity, healthcare-subject context, relationships and privacy into the same administrative frame while preserving their different responsibilities. The established partial chain to Person Identity is retained; the catalogue's other contextual descriptions do not supply a complete capability hierarchy.


\cataloguefield{subsection}{Intent — retained v0.1 source explanation}

Keep the individual and the circumstances of their representation intelligible across care information and operational activity.


\cataloguefield{subsection}{Boundary — retained v0.1 source explanation}

R1/\allowbreak{}R2 identifier correlation and administrative correction do not make Harmonia the authoritative clinical EMPI. Probabilistic matching and master identity merge/\allowbreak{}unmerge remain an uncommitted roadmap candidate.


\cataloguefield{subsection}{Boundary}

Information administration does not confer authority over the represented person, organisation, service, place, device or clinical activity.


\cataloguefield{subsection}{Proposed Placement Rationale}

Responsibility-preserving placement under the human-reviewed BEC hierarchy; the structural assertion remains Proposed.


\cataloguefield{subsection}{Reviewed reconciliation provenance}
Reconciliation against the explicit human-reviewed BEC candidate hierarchy. Bounded semantic reconciliation; no unconstrained synthesis \hyperref[evidence:405e9742dcba8b45]{reviewed-bec-hierarchy.json:2}
