\cataloguefield{paragraph}{Feature Overview}

Identifier correlations can change when an upstream authority corrects a relationship. Reviewers must be able to distinguish the source decision, its effective standing and the managed links affected.


\cataloguefield{paragraph}{Definition — Proposed}

Retain source-attributed identity assertions and externally decided correction history.


\cataloguefield{paragraph}{Boundary}

No probabilistic matching, golden-record selection or autonomous merge authority.


\cataloguefield{paragraph}{Proposed Placement Rationale}

This behaviour changes or exposes the bounded concern of Person Identity, rather than inheriting an adjacent responsibility.


\cataloguefield{paragraph}{Derivation Provenance}
Inferred from capability-specific behaviour, v0.3 inspection and current architectural evidence. AI architectural synthesis under the explicitly authorised Step 2 task \hyperref[evidence:be61392fefb4bb10]{information-responsibility.md:10}
