\cataloguefield{subsubsection}{Capability Overview}

Administer practitioner roles, specialties, organisational affiliations, operational capacities and recognised role endpoints.


\cataloguefield{subsubsection}{Definition — Reviewed candidate}

Administer practitioner roles, specialties, organisational affiliations, operational capacities and recognised role endpoints.


\cataloguefield{subsubsection}{Boundary}

Role, specialty, capacity and endpoint information supply context; they do not constitute a privilege determination.


\cataloguefield{subsubsection}{Proposed Placement Rationale}

Responsibility-preserving placement under the human-reviewed BEC hierarchy; the structural assertion remains Proposed.


\cataloguefield{subsubsection}{Derivation Provenance}
Inferred from bounded responsibilities and their semantic decomposition. AI architectural synthesis under the explicitly authorised Step 2 task \hyperref[evidence:e01893359d483acf]{business-enabling-capabilities.md:145}; \hyperref[evidence:be61392fefb4bb10]{information-responsibility.md:10}
\cataloguefield{subsubsection}{Reviewed reconciliation provenance}
Reconciliation against the explicit human-reviewed BEC candidate hierarchy. Bounded semantic reconciliation; no unconstrained synthesis \hyperref[evidence:405e9742dcba8b45]{reviewed-bec-hierarchy.json:2}
\cataloguefield{subsubsection}{Pre-review semantics — historical}

Exact prior assertions are retained as reconciliation evidence, rather than descriptions of the current reviewed capability.


\textbf{Previous definition:} Modeling the formal role, specialty, and operational capacity of a practitioner at a given organisation or location.


\textbf{Previous overview:} The same practitioner may act in different specialties, organisations and operational capacities. Role-specific associations and communication endpoints make that participation intelligible without converting a directory role into permission or professional privilege.


\textbf{Previous intent:} Make the capacity and organisational context of a practitioner interaction explicit.


\cataloguefield{subsubsection}{Consolidated / decomposed predecessors}
\nameref{cap:bec-practitioner-role} (p.\,\pageref{cap:bec-practitioner-role}); \nameref{cap:bec-provider-relationship} (p.\,\pageref{cap:bec-provider-relationship})
\cataloguefield{subsubsection}{Prior Candidate Derivation}
\hyperref[model:reconciliation]{v0.3 reconciliation}: \texttt{\seqsplit{BEC-2DEC073A}} (line 3099). Working locators are not identity aliases.
