\cataloguefield{subsubsection}{Capability Overview}

Administer service definitions, provision relationships, defined availability and eligibility information describing offered healthcare services.


\cataloguefield{subsubsection}{Definition — Reviewed candidate}

Administer service definitions, provision relationships, defined availability and eligibility information describing offered healthcare services.


\cataloguefield{subsubsection}{Boundary}

Defined availability is not dynamic operational capacity, collective readiness or authority to accept clinical care.


\cataloguefield{subsubsection}{Proposed Placement Rationale}

Responsibility-preserving placement under the human-reviewed BEC hierarchy; the structural assertion remains Proposed.


\cataloguefield{subsubsection}{Derivation Provenance}
Inferred from bounded responsibilities and their semantic decomposition. AI architectural synthesis under the explicitly authorised Step 2 task \hyperref[evidence:e01893359d483acf]{business-enabling-capabilities.md:192}; \hyperref[evidence:be61392fefb4bb10]{information-responsibility.md:10}
\cataloguefield{subsubsection}{Reviewed reconciliation provenance}
Reconciliation against the explicit human-reviewed BEC candidate hierarchy. Bounded semantic reconciliation; no unconstrained synthesis \hyperref[evidence:405e9742dcba8b45]{reviewed-bec-hierarchy.json:2}
\cataloguefield{subsubsection}{Pre-review semantics — historical}

Exact prior assertions are retained as reconciliation evidence, rather than descriptions of the current reviewed capability.


\textbf{Previous definition:} Specifying clinical and administrative health services offered to the public or clinical referrers.


\textbf{Previous overview:} An offered service has an identifiable clinical or administrative purpose, specialty and published intake description. That definition is distinct from the provider/\allowbreak{}location binding through which the service can be delivered.


\textbf{Previous intent:} Make the purpose and published offering of a healthcare service recognisable independently of its current delivery arrangement.


\textbf{Previous boundary:} Defines what is offered; offering existence does not establish current availability or collective readiness.


\cataloguefield{subsubsection}{Consolidated / decomposed predecessors}
\nameref{cap:bec-healthcare-service-definition} (p.\,\pageref{cap:bec-healthcare-service-definition}); \nameref{cap:bec-service-provision-relationship} (p.\,\pageref{cap:bec-service-provision-relationship}); \nameref{cap:bec-service-availability-definition} (p.\,\pageref{cap:bec-service-availability-definition}); \nameref{cap:bec-service-eligibility-definition} (p.\,\pageref{cap:bec-service-eligibility-definition})
\cataloguefield{subsubsection}{Prior Candidate Derivation}
\hyperref[model:reconciliation]{v0.3 reconciliation}: \texttt{\seqsplit{BEC-1864D570}} (line 3872). Working locators are not identity aliases.
