\cataloguefield{subsubsection}{Pre-review semantics — historical}

Exact prior assertions are retained as reconciliation evidence, rather than descriptions of the current reviewed capability.


\textbf{Previous definition:} Classification of pharmaceutical and consumable products.


\textbf{Previous overview:} Medication, blood-product, implant and consumable descriptions provide reference context for care information. Product identity and classification are retained without turning this reference responsibility into procurement or prescribing.


\textbf{Previous intent:} Provide interpretable product context for health information without acquiring product-management authority.


\cataloguefield{subsubsection}{Prior Candidate Derivation}
\hyperref[model:reconciliation]{v0.3 reconciliation}: \texttt{\seqsplit{BEC-1BE2ADD6}} (line 4188). Working locators are not identity aliases.
