\cataloguefield{paragraph}{Feature Overview}

Case progression records externally established surgical milestones in an operationally meaningful sequence. It makes the theatre situation visible without authorising or performing the clinical acts denoted by anaesthesia, incision, closure or recovery.


\cataloguefield{paragraph}{Definition / governed semantic detail}

Track surgical case state transitions (\texttt{\seqsplit{CALLED}} → \texttt{\seqsplit{IN\_THEATRE}} → \texttt{\seqsplit{ANAESTHETISED}} → \texttt{\seqsplit{INCISION}} → \texttt{\seqsplit{CLOSED}} → \texttt{\seqsplit{RECOVERY}}).


\cataloguefield{paragraph}{Proposed Placement Rationale}

Meaningful reviewed CT3 framing selected for the existing Feature semantics; established responsibility provenance is preserved.


