\cataloguefield{subsubsection}{Definition / governed semantic detail}

Understands and manages available, committed and utilised ED capacity in relation to care-place availability, demand, patient presence/\allowbreak{}progression, acuity and operational constraints; retains waiting room occupancy, resuscitation bay availability and time-to-triage metrics.


\emph{Capacity boundary}: Existing departmental capacity responsibility is clarified, not duplicated. Care-place state contributes to service capacity; capacity coordination neither performs clinical triage nor establishes clinical acuity assertions.


