\cataloguefield{subsection}{Capability Overview}

Bed \&amp; Care-Place Management maintains operational place state and the turnover progression that makes a place usable again. Vacancy, reservation, cleaning and readiness must remain distinguishable so that an empty bed is not automatically treated as available for allocation. Notifications expose meaningful readiness changes to the responsible operational participants.


\cataloguefield{subsection}{Definition — Reviewed candidate}

Bed \&amp; Care-Place Management maintains operational place state and the turnover progression that makes a place usable again. Vacancy, reservation, cleaning and readiness must remain distinguishable so that an empty bed is not automatically treated as available for allocation. Notifications expose meaningful readiness changes to the responsible operational participants.


\cataloguefield{subsection}{Intent — retained v0.1 source explanation}

Support credible care-place decisions using governed state rather than physical presence alone.


\cataloguefield{subsection}{Boundary — retained v0.1 source explanation}

A ready bed does not establish service-level capacity or collective readiness, and place state does not determine clinical suitability or care responsibility.


\cataloguefield{subsection}{Harmonia Architectural Relevance — retained v0.1 source explanation}

Governed place-state progression and operational notification are substantive assigned platform responsibilities.


\cataloguefield{subsection}{Boundary}

Information administration does not confer authority over the represented person, organisation, service, place, device or clinical activity.


\cataloguefield{subsection}{Proposed Placement Rationale}

Responsibility-preserving placement under the human-reviewed BEC hierarchy; the structural assertion remains Proposed.


