\cataloguefield{paragraph}{Feature Overview}

Availability tracking preserves the operational distinctions among vacancy, occupancy, reservation, blockage and cleaning conditions. These states support meaningful care-place coordination without equating an unoccupied bed with a ready place or usable service capacity.


\cataloguefield{paragraph}{Definition / governed semantic detail}

Maintain operational status of all registered beds and care-places (\texttt{\seqsplit{VACANT}}, \texttt{\seqsplit{OCCUPIED}}, \texttt{\seqsplit{BLOCKED}}, \texttt{\seqsplit{RESERVED}}, \texttt{\seqsplit{DIRTY}}, \texttt{\seqsplit{CLEANING}}, \texttt{\seqsplit{CLEAN}}).


\cataloguefield{paragraph}{Proposed Placement Rationale}

Meaningful reviewed CT3 framing selected for the existing Feature semantics; established responsibility provenance is preserved.


