\cataloguefield{section}{Pre-review semantics — historical}

Exact prior assertions are retained as reconciliation evidence, rather than descriptions of the current reviewed capability.


\textbf{Previous definition:} Preserve, find, exchange, qualify and protect health information and the governed definitions needed to interpret it.


\textbf{Previous overview:} This frame makes a managed record usable over time and across authorised purposes. It separates clinical synthesis, binary-content association, external exchange, semantic definitions, privacy and evidence so that none becomes an undifferentiated information utility.


\textbf{Previous intent:} Keep managed health information usable and attributable across time, boundaries and authorised purposes.


