\cataloguefield{subsection}{Capability Overview}

As a BEC, Health Information Exchange provides reusable information-movement enablement through submission, retrieval mediation, addressed distribution and syndication. The models distinguish sending to a participant, requesting information, deliberately distributing to named recipients and publishing changes to matching subscribers. Their common responsibility is the exchange context, including routing and delivery state, rather than the business meaning of every payload.


\cataloguefield{subsection}{Definition — Reviewed candidate}

As a BEC, Health Information Exchange provides reusable information-movement enablement through submission, retrieval mediation, addressed distribution and syndication. The models distinguish sending to a participant, requesting information, deliberately distributing to named recipients and publishing changes to matching subscribers. Their common responsibility is the exchange context, including routing and delivery state, rather than the business meaning of every payload.


\cataloguefield{subsection}{Boundary — retained v0.1 source explanation}

The capability owns exchange transaction state without acquiring clinical-document ownership. Its name collision with the BC remains unresolved; exchange egress ends management of the emitted representation.


\cataloguefield{subsection}{Harmonia Architectural Relevance — retained v0.1 source explanation}

Multi-party exchange and per-destination delivery tracking are substantive Core responsibilities, bounded by the external contract and originating information authority.


\cataloguefield{subsection}{Boundary}

Information administration does not confer authority over the represented person, organisation, service, place, device or clinical activity.


\cataloguefield{subsection}{Proposed Placement Rationale}

Responsibility-preserving placement under the human-reviewed BEC hierarchy; the structural assertion remains Proposed.


\cataloguefield{subsection}{Proposed Naming Decision}

HUMAN ADJUDICATION REQUIRED: reviewed name Health Information Exchange duplicates the Canonical BC name under CM-R05. The existing BEC display qualification is retained; reviewed\_name records the exact task wording. Identities and BC/\allowbreak{}BEC semantics remain distinct.


\cataloguefield{subsection}{Reviewed reconciliation provenance}
Reconciliation against the explicit human-reviewed BEC candidate hierarchy. Bounded semantic reconciliation; no unconstrained synthesis \hyperref[evidence:405e9742dcba8b45]{reviewed-bec-hierarchy.json:2}
