\cataloguefield{paragraph}{Feature Overview}

A consumer should be able to explain which source assertions contributed to a managed representation and what significant transformation occurred.


\cataloguefield{paragraph}{Definition — Proposed}

Record meaningful source-to-derived information relationships and transformation attribution.


\cataloguefield{paragraph}{Boundary}

Routine cache reconstruction, retries and diagnostics do not automatically become permanent lineage.


\cataloguefield{paragraph}{Proposed Placement Rationale}

This behaviour changes or exposes the bounded concern of Information Lineage Stewardship, rather than inheriting an adjacent responsibility.


\cataloguefield{paragraph}{Derivation Provenance}
Inferred from capability-specific behaviour, v0.3 inspection and current architectural evidence. AI architectural synthesis under the explicitly authorised Step 2 task \hyperref[evidence:be61392fefb4bb10]{information-responsibility.md:10}
