\cataloguefield{section}{Capability Overview}

Establish and govern semantically meaningful health-information assets suitable for downstream research, population-health reporting and service planning in an adjacent analytical environment.


\cataloguefield{section}{Definition — Reviewed candidate}

Establish and govern semantically meaningful health-information assets suitable for downstream research, population-health reporting and service planning in an adjacent analytical environment.


\cataloguefield{section}{Boundary}

Harmonia is adjacent to a Big Data/\allowbreak{}analytical environment. It establishes governed assets and reporting inputs; it does not become that analytical platform.


\cataloguefield{section}{Proposed Placement Rationale}

Responsibility-preserving placement under the human-reviewed BEC hierarchy; the structural assertion remains Proposed.


\cataloguefield{section}{Review Confidence}
Medium; applies to the proposal, not to preserved canonical meaning.
\cataloguefield{section}{Derivation Provenance}
Inferred from bounded responsibilities and their semantic decomposition. AI architectural synthesis under the explicitly authorised Step 2 task \hyperref[evidence:4bac85accd34ce0b]{business-architecture-metamodel.md:49}; \hyperref[evidence:be61392fefb4bb10]{information-responsibility.md:10}
\cataloguefield{section}{Reviewed reconciliation provenance}
Reconciliation against the explicit human-reviewed BEC candidate hierarchy. Bounded semantic reconciliation; no unconstrained synthesis \hyperref[evidence:405e9742dcba8b45]{reviewed-bec-hierarchy.json:2}
\cataloguefield{section}{Pre-review semantics — historical}

Exact prior assertions are retained as reconciliation evidence, rather than descriptions of the current reviewed capability.


\textbf{Previous definition:} Provide existing health information for authorised research, required population notification and service planning purposes.


\textbf{Previous overview:} Provide existing health information for authorised research, required population notification and service planning purposes. Its constituent abilities distinguish .


\textbf{Previous intent:} Preserve the particular authorised purpose and obligation when clinical information is used beyond individual care delivery.


\textbf{Previous boundary:} Each purpose has different release criteria. This grouping does not originate research approval, public-health decisions or planning authority.


