\cataloguefield{section}{Capability Overview}

Enable assurance specification and independent review of the assurance service while preserving the distinct Canonical responsibility for assurance against a governed subject.


\cataloguefield{section}{Definition — Reviewed candidate}

Enable assurance specification and independent review of the assurance service while preserving the distinct Canonical responsibility for assurance against a governed subject.


\cataloguefield{section}{Boundary}

Assurance cannot manage, remediate or approve its subject merely because it observes it. Clinical adequacy, financial governance and source-information authority remain outside this mandate.


\cataloguefield{section}{Proposed Placement Rationale}

Responsibility-preserving placement under the human-reviewed BEC hierarchy; the structural assertion remains Proposed.


\cataloguefield{section}{Derivation Provenance}
Inferred from bounded responsibilities and their semantic decomposition. AI architectural synthesis under the explicitly authorised Step 2 task \hyperref[evidence:4bac85accd34ce0b]{business-architecture-metamodel.md:49}; \hyperref[evidence:be61392fefb4bb10]{information-responsibility.md:10}; \hyperref[evidence:14c8f26d232fcb78]{health-service-assurance.md:9}
\cataloguefield{section}{Reviewed reconciliation provenance}
Reconciliation against the explicit human-reviewed BEC candidate hierarchy. Bounded semantic reconciliation; no unconstrained synthesis \hyperref[evidence:405e9742dcba8b45]{reviewed-bec-hierarchy.json:2}
\cataloguefield{section}{Pre-review semantics — historical}

Exact prior assertions are retained as reconciliation evidence, rather than descriptions of the current reviewed capability.


\textbf{Previous definition:} Specify how governed service behaviour is assured and independently establish what applicable evidence demonstrates.


\textbf{Previous overview:} The frame separates design and criteria stewardship from the evaluation activity that produces findings. It preserves the established three assurance capabilities and five Functions without turning observation or operational health into an assurance conclusion.


\textbf{Previous intent:} Establish justified confidence in governed service behaviour without giving the subject control of its own assurance conclusion.


