\cataloguefield{subsubsection}{Capability Overview}

Document attachments, diagnostic media and operational artefacts share a need to locate usable content while distinguishing logical meaning from physical possession.


\cataloguefield{subsubsection}{Definition — Proposed}

Maintain content associations and custody knowledge sufficient for governed payload resolution, retrieval and assembly.


\cataloguefield{subsubsection}{Intent}

Make logical information and its usable payloads consistently associable while retaining custody boundaries.


\cataloguefield{subsubsection}{Boundary}

No universal binary custody, storage topology or persistence authority is implied.


\cataloguefield{subsubsection}{Derivation Provenance}
Inferred from bounded responsibilities and their semantic decomposition. AI architectural synthesis under the explicitly authorised Step 2 task \hyperref[evidence:0c75887c024354f6]{sylloge-binary-content-management.md:14}; \hyperref[evidence:be61392fefb4bb10]{information-responsibility.md:10}
