\cataloguefield{section}{Capability Overview}

Requests, events, work and human interaction are related ways to cause or observe change, with distinct contracts and progression responsibilities.


\cataloguefield{section}{Definition — Proposed}

Enable governed interaction, event participation, boundary exchange and accountable activity progression.


\cataloguefield{section}{Intent}

Make requests, event participation, work and human interaction progress according to their different contracts.


\cataloguefield{section}{Boundary}

Exchange is not execution, notification is not outcome, and interaction is not clinical authority.


\cataloguefield{section}{Derivation Provenance}
Inferred from bounded responsibilities and their semantic decomposition. AI architectural synthesis under the explicitly authorised Step 2 task \hyperref[evidence:27549d51551beae6]{architectural-axioms.md:668}; \hyperref[evidence:be61392fefb4bb10]{information-responsibility.md:10}
