\chapter{Preserved responsibilities and reconciliation history}\label{model:retained}
These entries are deliberately outside the current BEC hierarchy. Superseded structural records retain their identities, labels, last allocated structural IDs and exact prior semantics. Pending responsibilities retain their Canonical or Proposed semantic standing and owned material while a genuine placement or meaning conflict awaits human adjudication. Their historical placements are not current decomposition assertions. This register is evidence and an explicit unresolved register, not an additional BEC branch.

