\cataloguefield{subsection}{HUMAN ADJUDICATION REQUIRED}

HUMAN ADJUDICATION REQUIRED: Canonical internal Work Order, To Do and synthetic Task progression is broader than the reviewed external execution-boundary bridge.


\cataloguefield{subsection}{Capability Overview}

Workflow \&amp; Activity Coordination provides governed progression for three distinct work meanings: human operational Work Orders, human review or decision To Dos, and non-human Synthetic Tasks. It supports dispatch, state and deadline oversight without collapsing those meanings into a generic technical task. The common coordination responsibility makes progression visible while preserving who has authority to perform or decide the underlying activity.


\cataloguefield{subsection}{Intent}

Keep assigned activity, acknowledgement, progress and outcome distinguishable across human and automated work.


\cataloguefield{subsection}{Boundary — v0.1 explanation}

Coordination does not confer clinical work ownership. Synthetic Tasks are not external clinical worklists, and the incomplete stalled/\allowbreak{}failed Process paths remain unresolved.


\cataloguefield{subsection}{Harmonia Architectural Relevance}

Governed activity progression is a substantive Core responsibility; information traceability preserves archetype, work and undertaking distinctions without transferring outcome authority.


\cataloguefield{subsection}{Proposed Placement Rationale}

The responsibility concerns progress governed operational work in identifiable activity and temporal contexts. It is the finest capability frame required for the established behaviour; the older contextual heading is not another capability tier.


