HUMAN ADJUDICATION REQUIRED: Canonical operational badges/\allowbreak{}physical-access credentials are distinct from reviewed clinical-service credential definitions.


\cataloguefield{subsection}{Capability Overview}

Credential Management concerns operational badges and physical-access credentials used in authorised operational participation. It retains a distinct Domain03 responsibility even though Strategy has no matching catalogue entry. This prevents the word credential from merging physical-access context with the professional qualifications and competency evidence checked by Clinical Qualification Management.


\cataloguefield{subsection}{Boundary}

No Strategy correspondence or Feature association is inferred from name similarity. Operational credentials do not themselves establish professional clinical qualification or privilege.


\cataloguefield{subsection}{Harmonia Architectural Relevance — v0.1 explanation}

Relevance remains Unresolved. Established operational behaviour provides context for possible enablement but does not authorise a formal classification.


\cataloguefield{subsection}{Proposed Placement Rationale}

The responsibility concerns represent learning, competence, professional-standing checks and separately governed operational access qualifications. It is the finest capability frame required for the established behaviour; the older contextual heading is not another capability tier.


\cataloguefield{subsection}{Review Confidence}
Medium; applies to the proposal, not to preserved canonical meaning.
