\cataloguefield{subsection}{Capability Overview}

Campus, building, floor, ward and room relationships explain physical containment. The structure provides navigation and context without determining organisational reporting lines or current operational capacity.


\cataloguefield{subsection}{Definition — Proposed}

Modeling the physical architecture of healthcare campuses.


\cataloguefield{subsection}{Intent}

Allow a particular place to be interpreted within its physical surroundings.


\cataloguefield{subsection}{Boundary}

Physical containment differs from organisational structure and operational responsibility.


\cataloguefield{subsection}{Derivation Provenance}
Inferred from bounded responsibilities and their semantic decomposition. AI architectural synthesis under the explicitly authorised Step 2 task \hyperref[evidence:e01893359d483acf]{business-enabling-capabilities.md:181}; \hyperref[evidence:be61392fefb4bb10]{information-responsibility.md:10}
