\cataloguefield{subsection}{Capability Overview}

Service provision joins a named offering to the organisations, places and practitioner roles through which it is provided. The mapping is the owned concern; the identity and meaning of each mapped participant remain with its established capability.


\cataloguefield{subsection}{Definition — Proposed}

Binding health services to specific organizations, locations, and practitioner roles.


\cataloguefield{subsection}{Intent}

Make it clear which provider delivers which service at which place and through which participating roles.


\cataloguefield{subsection}{Boundary}

Owns mapping associations, retaining the owners of each participating entity.


\cataloguefield{subsection}{Derivation Provenance}
Inferred from bounded responsibilities and their semantic decomposition. AI architectural synthesis under the explicitly authorised Step 2 task \hyperref[evidence:e01893359d483acf]{business-enabling-capabilities.md:196}; \hyperref[evidence:be61392fefb4bb10]{information-responsibility.md:10}
\cataloguefield{subsection}{Reviewed successors}
