\cataloguefield{subsection}{Capability Overview}

Regular hours, on-call windows and exceptional closures describe when an offering is nominally available. They provide an input to readiness and scheduling without proving that all required dependencies are ready.


\cataloguefield{subsection}{Definition — Proposed}

Modeling regular operating hours, exceptional closures, and emergency availability.


\cataloguefield{subsection}{Intent}

Express the operating windows against which a service participation request can be considered.


\cataloguefield{subsection}{Boundary}

Represents operating windows and exceptions; it does not establish staffing, capacity or readiness.


\cataloguefield{subsection}{Derivation Provenance}
Inferred from bounded responsibilities and their semantic decomposition. AI architectural synthesis under the explicitly authorised Step 2 task \hyperref[evidence:e01893359d483acf]{business-enabling-capabilities.md:200}; \hyperref[evidence:be61392fefb4bb10]{information-responsibility.md:10}
\cataloguefield{subsection}{Reviewed successors}
