\cataloguefield{subsection}{Capability Overview}

A device can be associated with different patients and care places at different times. Qualified association and its lineage allow observations to be interpreted against the applicable binding rather than the current assignment alone.


\cataloguefield{subsection}{Definition — Proposed}

Associating clinical devices with patients, beds, or rooms.


\cataloguefield{subsection}{Intent}

Allow a device-originated item to be associated with the correct subject and place at the relevant time.


\cataloguefield{subsection}{Boundary}

Represents qualified device-to-subject/\allowbreak{}place association without owning those subjects or observations.


\cataloguefield{subsection}{Derivation Provenance}
Inferred from bounded responsibilities and their semantic decomposition. AI architectural synthesis under the explicitly authorised Step 2 task \hyperref[evidence:e01893359d483acf]{business-enabling-capabilities.md:226}; \hyperref[evidence:be61392fefb4bb10]{information-responsibility.md:10}
