\cataloguefield{subsection}{Capability Overview}

Relate operational care-place and equipment state to the coordinated view of service demand and capacity. Its constituent abilities distinguish Bed \&amp; Care-Place Management; Clinical Resource Management; Service Capacity Management.


\cataloguefield{subsection}{Definition — Proposed}

Relate operational care-place and equipment state to the coordinated view of service demand and capacity.


\cataloguefield{subsection}{Intent}

Make resource-state contributions and coordinated capacity views usable without collapsing their different responsibilities.


\cataloguefield{subsection}{Boundary}

Bed/\allowbreak{}equipment availability is a contribution to capacity, not its definition. Higher-order capacity consumes local capacity without taking its ownership.


