\cataloguefield{subsection}{HUMAN ADJUDICATION REQUIRED}

HUMAN ADJUDICATION REQUIRED: Source credibility and authority standing require an explicit home; information-asset tags alone do not establish that responsibility.


\cataloguefield{subsection}{Capability Overview}

A persisted assertion may be authoritative, informational or anecdotal. This ability carries that standing into interpretation without treating transport reliability, freshness or successful commit as proof of credibility.


\cataloguefield{subsection}{Definition — Proposed}

Represent the source, credibility and qualified authority standing of competing health-information assertions.


\cataloguefield{subsection}{Intent}

Keep an assertion technical acceptance separate from the standing of the source that asserted it.


\cataloguefield{subsection}{Boundary}

Classification does not originate clinical facts or universally adjudicate conflicts. Policy determines how qualified assertions are used.


\cataloguefield{subsection}{Review Confidence}
Medium; applies to the proposal, not to preserved canonical meaning.
\cataloguefield{subsection}{Derivation Provenance}
Inferred from bounded responsibilities and their semantic decomposition. AI architectural synthesis under the explicitly authorised Step 2 task \hyperref[evidence:27549d51551beae6]{architectural-axioms.md:303}; \hyperref[evidence:be61392fefb4bb10]{information-responsibility.md:10}
